/* ---- drawing kit for the Obesity Companion ----
   All colours come from CSS tokens, so they follow the theme. Every function returns an SVG string, or an object
   with .svg (and usually .at, named anchor points in the caller's SVG coordinates), to concatenate into an <svg>'s
   innerHTML. Everything is schematic: no glyph encodes a measured value unless the caller passes one in, and the
   kit holds no clinical numbers (no BMI cut-offs, doses, schedules, trial results or risks). Pass them in from the
   research, with the citation in the surrounding text. Clip paths use fresh ids on every call, so any number of
   glyphs can share a page. Text labels stay a fixed size whatever the scale.

   PEOPLE. person() draws every body size with the same neutral --figure colour, the same upright posture and no
   face: size is never a cue for health, mood or effort. Never draw "before and after" pairs. Body size changes,
   when a module truly needs one, are slow and neutral, and never the punchline of an animation.

   ORIENTATION. Organs are drawn in front view, as if facing the person: the person's left is on the viewer's
   right (the stomach's fundus is on the right, the pylorus and duodenum on the left, the liver's big right lobe on
   the left). The brain is seen from the side, facing left.

   ---- fat tissue ----
   adipocyte(x,y,r,o)   one fat cell centred at (x,y): a thin rim of cytoplasm, one big lipid droplet and the nucleus
                        flattened against the membrane. r = the radius at o.size .5.
     o.size     0..1 (default .5): the cell's size, from small (0) to enlarged (1): hypertrophy, or shrinkage.
     o.inflamed 0..1 a stressed cell: --fat-hot rim and tint. o.kind 'white' (default) | 'beige' | 'brown': beige
                has several droplets, brown many small ones in --brownfat cytoplasm with a central nucleus.
     o.ang      angle in degrees of the nucleus on the rim (default 40, lower right). o.seed: a slightly irregular
                outline. o.op opacity.  Returns {svg, at:{c, R, nucleus}}.
   adiposeTissue(x,y,w,h,o) a packed sheet of fat cells clipped to the box (x,y,w,h).
     o.size     0..1 cell size (hypertrophy): fewer, bigger cells as it grows. o.cell base cell diameter (28).
     o.inflamed 0..1 the share of stressed cells. o.macro 0..1 crown-like structures: macrophages gather round the
                stressed cells. o.vessel 0..1 a capillary winding through (fades as o.hypoxia 0..1 rises: the cells
                far from it turn grey-blue). o.kind as for adipocyte. o.seed. o.frame true draws a rounded border.
     Returns {svg, at:{cells:[[x,y,r],...], c}}.
   macrophage(x,y,r,o)  an amoeboid macrophage centred at (x,y): pseudopods, kidney-shaped nucleus, granules.
                        o.kind 'M1' (inflammatory: spiky, --risk outline) | 'M2' (rounded, the default). o.seed, o.op.

   ---- gut ----
   stomach(x,y,s,o)     the stomach with its oesophagus and the start of the duodenum, front view. (x,y) = top left;
                        s = scale, 1 = 130 wide, 140 tall.
     o.variant  'normal' (default) | 'sleeve' (sleeve gastrectomy: a narrow tube along the lesser curvature, the
                removed part as a dashed ghost and a staple line) | 'bypass' (Roux-en-Y: a small pouch, the bypassed
                remnant left in place and dimmed, the Roux limb leaving the pouch) | 'band' (an adjustable band round
                the top) | 'switch' (a sleeve whose duodenum is divided just past the pylorus, as in a duodenal switch).
     o.morph    0..1 how far the change from the normal stomach has gone (default 1), so it can be animated.
     o.fill     0..1 food in the stomach (or pouch). o.ghost false hides the removed part. o.labels true names parts.
     Returns {svg, at:{eso, cardia, fundus, body, antrum, pylorus, duo, pouch, out}, w, h}.
   gutTract(x,y,s,o)    oesophagus, stomach, duodenum, pancreas, small intestine and colon framing it. (x,y) = top
                        left; s = scale, 1 = 200 wide, 270 tall.
     o.variant  as for stomach; for 'bypass' and 'switch' the bowel is rerouted (Roux limb; ileal limb).
     o.morph    0..1 as for stomach. o.food 0..1: a bolus travelling the route food takes for this variant.
     o.glow     {stomach, duo, ileum, pancreas: 0..1}: a soft glow where those hormones come from (ghrelin from the
                stomach, GIP and CCK from the duodenum, GLP-1 and PYY from L cells in the ileum, insulin from the
                pancreas). o.labels true names the parts. o.dim 0..1 fades it (context drawing).
     Returns {svg, at:{eso, stomach, pylorus, duo, jejunum, ileum, colon, pancreas, pouch, join}, route:f->[x,y], w, h}.

   ---- brain ----
   brainHypothalamus(x,y,s,o) a brain seen from the side with the hypothalamus marked, and beside it a round inset
                        of the hypothalamus: the third ventricle, the arcuate nucleus at its base with POMC (fullness:
                        --pomc, circles) and AgRP/NPY (hunger: --agrp, triangles) neurons, and the paraventricular
                        nucleus (PVN) above, whose neurons carry the MC4R. (x,y) = top left; s = scale, 1 = 260 x 180.
     o.pomc 0..1 POMC activity (glow, and arrows to the PVN). o.agrp 0..1 AgRP activity (glow, and blunt-ended
     inhibitory lines to the PVN). o.mc4r 0..1 the PVN's MC4R signal (the fullness output). o.inset false draws the
     brain alone. o.labels true names the parts.
     Returns {svg, at:{hypo, brainstem, arc, pomc, agrp, pvn, bloodIn, inset:[cx,cy,r]}}.

   ---- signals ----
   hormoneDot(x,y,kind,o) one hormone molecule. Each kind has its own colour AND shape, so colour is never the only
                        cue: 'ghrelin' circle, 'leptin' diamond, 'glp1' hexagon, 'pyy' triangle, 'insulin' rounded
                        square, 'gip' pentagon, 'cck' four-point star, 'drug' (a GLP-1 medicine) hexagon in a ring.
                        o.r radius (5), o.op, o.label true writes its short name beside it.
   HORMONE_INFO         {kind:{name, col}} for legends.

   ---- organs and things ----
   liver(x,y,s,o)       a liver, front view. (x,y) = top left; s = scale, 1 = 140 x 90. o.fat 0..1 fat droplets in
                        the liver (steatosis), o.inflamed 0..1, o.scar 0..1 fibrous strands. Returns {svg, at:{c,
                        right, left, hilum}}.
   pen(x,y,s,o)         a prefilled injector pen centred at (x,y), lying flat; s = scale, 1 = 120 long. o.ang
                        rotation, o.cap true the cap is on, o.needle 0..1 needle out, o.press 0..1 the button pushed
                        in, o.dial 0..1 turns the dose dial (no numbers are drawn). Returns {svg, at:{tip, back}}.
   person(x,y,s,o)      a neutral, respectful standing figure, (x,y) the top of the head, s its height. o.size 0..1
                        body size (0 slimmer, 1 larger), o.kid true child proportions, o.col and o.line override
                        --figure and --figure-line, o.op. No face. Returns {svg, at:{head, chest, belly, liver, hip,
                        knee, foot}, w}.
   seesaw(x,y,w,o)      an energy-balance see-saw: the fulcrum's foot at (x,y), a beam w wide. o.tilt -1..1
                        (negative: the left side is heavier), o.left / o.right labels, o.lw / o.rw 0..1 loads drawn as
                        stacked blocks (left in --fat, right in --lean unless o.lcol / o.rcol). Returns {svg, at:{left,
                        right}}.

   ---- charts ----
   curveAxes(x,y,w,h,o) a chart frame: o {x0,x1,y0,y1, xt:[ticks], yt:[ticks], xfmt, yfmt, xlabel, ylabel, grid}.
                        (x,y) = top left of the plot area. Returns {svg, X, Y}.
   plotLine(P,X,Y,o)    a line through data points P [[x,y],...] in data units. o {col, lw, dash, upto (cut at this x,
                        interpolating), dot (a dot at the end), fill (area down to o.base, default the y0 of the data),
                        smooth (monotone curve)}. Returns {svg, end:[x,y]}.
   iconArray(x,y,o)     a block of people or dots: o {n (100), cols (10), k (highlighted count) or groups
                        [{k, col}, ...], size (12), gap (3), shape 'person' (default) | 'dot', col, base}.
                        Returns {svg, h, w, at:i->[x,y]}.

   ---- helpers ----
   kitLabel(x,y,text,o) a small label with a halo so it reads on any drawing: o {a:'m'|'e', halo (var(--panel))}.
   smoothPath(P,closed) Catmull-Rom path through points. crPts(P,closed,k) the points of that curve. inPoly(p,P).
   ptsD(P) polyline path. polyAt(P) arc-length sampler: f(0..1) -> [x,y] along the polyline P.
   monoFn(P)            monotone cubic through data points [[x,y],...] (sorted by x). Returns f(x).
   blob(cx,cy,r,seed,o) an irregular closed path string: o {n (18), rough (.16), sq}. kid(prefix) a fresh id. */

/* ---- helpers ---- */
let _kid=0;
const kid=p=>'ob'+p+'_'+(++_kid);
function kitLabel(x,y,t,o={}){return `<text x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" class="t-xs${o.a==='m'?' t-mid':o.a==='e'?' t-end':''}" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700;paint-order:stroke;stroke:${o.halo||'var(--panel)'};stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round">${t}</text>`}
function smoothPath(P,closed=true){const n=P.length;let d=`M${f1(P[0][0])} ${f1(P[0][1])}`;
  for(let i=0;i<(closed?n:n-1);i++){const p0=P[closed?(i-1+n)%n:Math.max(0,i-1)],p1=P[i],p2=P[(i+1)%n],p3=P[closed?(i+2)%n:Math.min(n-1,i+2)];
    const c1=[p1[0]+(p2[0]-p0[0])/6,p1[1]+(p2[1]-p0[1])/6],c2=[p2[0]-(p3[0]-p1[0])/6,p2[1]-(p3[1]-p1[1])/6];
    d+=`C${f1(c1[0])} ${f1(c1[1])} ${f1(c2[0])} ${f1(c2[1])} ${f1(p2[0])} ${f1(p2[1])}`}
  return d+(closed?'Z':'')}
function crPts(P,closed=true,k=6){const n=P.length,out=[],m=closed?n:n-1;
  for(let i=0;i<m;i++){const a=P[closed?(i-1+n)%n:Math.max(0,i-1)],b=P[i],c=P[(i+1)%n],d=P[closed?(i+2)%n:Math.min(n-1,i+2)];
    for(let j=0;j<k;j++){const t=j/k,u=t*t,v=u*t,f=q=>.5*(2*b[q]+(c[q]-a[q])*t+(2*a[q]-5*b[q]+4*c[q]-d[q])*u+(3*b[q]-a[q]-3*c[q]+d[q])*v);out.push([f(0),f(1)])}}
  if(!closed)out.push(P[n-1]);return out}
function inPoly(p,P){let c=false;for(let i=0,j=P.length-1;i<P.length;j=i++){const a=P[i],b=P[j];if((a[1]>p[1])!==(b[1]>p[1])&&p[0]<(b[0]-a[0])*(p[1]-a[1])/(b[1]-a[1])+a[0])c=!c}return c}
const ptsD=P=>P.map((p,i)=>(i?'L':'M')+f1(p[0])+' '+f1(p[1])).join('');
function polyAt(P){const L=[0];for(let i=1;i<P.length;i++)L.push(L[i-1]+Math.hypot(P[i][0]-P[i-1][0],P[i][1]-P[i-1][1]));const T=L[L.length-1]||1;
  return u=>{const d=clamp(u)*T;let i=1;while(i<L.length-1&&L[i]<d)i++;const s=(d-L[i-1])/((L[i]-L[i-1])||1);return [lerp(P[i-1][0],P[i][0],s),lerp(P[i-1][1],P[i][1],s)]}}
function monoFn(P){const n=P.length,dx=[],m=[],t=[];for(let i=0;i<n-1;i++){dx[i]=P[i+1][0]-P[i][0];m[i]=(P[i+1][1]-P[i][1])/dx[i]}
  t[0]=m[0];t[n-1]=m[n-2];for(let i=1;i<n-1;i++)t[i]=m[i-1]*m[i]<=0?0:3*(dx[i-1]+dx[i])/((2*dx[i]+dx[i-1])/m[i-1]+(dx[i]+2*dx[i-1])/m[i]);
  return v=>{if(v<=P[0][0])return P[0][1];if(v>=P[n-1][0])return P[n-1][1];let i=0;while(v>P[i+1][0])i++;const h=dx[i],u=(v-P[i][0])/h,u2=u*u,u3=u2*u;
    return (2*u3-3*u2+1)*P[i][1]+(u3-2*u2+u)*h*t[i]+(-2*u3+3*u2)*P[i+1][1]+(u3-u2)*h*t[i+1]}}
function blob(cx,cy,r,seed=1,o={}){const n=o.n||18,ro=o.rough==null?.16:o.rough,rr=rng(seed),P=[];
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const a=i/n*Math.PI*2,k=1+(rr()-.5)*ro*2;P.push([cx+Math.cos(a)*r*k,cy+Math.sin(a)*r*k*(o.sq||1)])}
  return smoothPath(P)}
const _tr=(x,y,k)=>p=>[x+p[0]*k,y+p[1]*k];

/* ---- fat tissue ---- */
function adipocyte(x,y,r=20,o={}){const sz=o.size==null?.5:clamp(o.size),R=r*lerp(.62,1.18,sz),inf=clamp(o.inflamed||0),kind=o.kind||'white',
  A=(o.ang==null?40:o.ang)*Math.PI/180,op=o.op==null?1:o.op;
  const out=o.seed?blob(x,y,R,o.seed,{rough:.06,n:14}):null;
  let s=`<g style="opacity:${op}">`;
  s+=out?`<path d="${out}" style="fill:${kind==='brown'?'var(--brownfat)':'var(--cyto)'};stroke:var(--fat-line);stroke-width:1.3"/>`
         :`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(R)}" style="fill:${kind==='brown'?'var(--brownfat)':'var(--cyto)'};stroke:var(--fat-line);stroke-width:1.3"/>`;
  let nuc;
  if(kind==='white'){const dr=R*.86,ox=-Math.cos(A)*R*.07,oy=-Math.sin(A)*R*.07;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x+ox)}" cy="${f1(y+oy)}" r="${f1(dr)}" style="fill:var(--fat)"/>`;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x+ox-dr*.32)}" cy="${f1(y+oy-dr*.34)}" r="${f1(dr*.22)}" style="fill:var(--panel);opacity:.35"/>`;
    nuc=[x+Math.cos(A)*R*.9,y+Math.sin(A)*R*.9];
    s+=`<ellipse cx="${f1(nuc[0])}" cy="${f1(nuc[1])}" rx="${f1(Math.max(2,R*.26))}" ry="${f1(Math.max(1.2,R*.085))}" transform="rotate(${f1(A*180/Math.PI+90)} ${f1(nuc[0])} ${f1(nuc[1])})" style="fill:var(--nucleus)"/>`}
  else{const rr=rng(o.seed||11),n=kind==='brown'?11:5,big=kind==='beige'?R*.42:0;
    if(big)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x-R*.18)}" cy="${f1(y-R*.12)}" r="${f1(big)}" style="fill:var(--fat)"/>`;
    for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const a=i/n*Math.PI*2+rr(),d=R*(big?.55:.3+rr()*.38),dr=R*(kind==='brown'?.14+rr()*.06:.15+rr()*.07);
      s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x+Math.cos(a)*d)}" cy="${f1(y+Math.sin(a)*d)}" r="${f1(dr)}" style="fill:var(--fat)"/>`}
    nuc=kind==='brown'?[x,y]:[x+R*.42,y+R*.34];
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(nuc[0])}" cy="${f1(nuc[1])}" r="${f1(R*.17)}" style="fill:var(--nucleus)"/>`;
    if(kind==='brown')for(let i=0;i<8;i++){const a=rr()*6.28,d=R*(.35+rr()*.45);s+=`<ellipse cx="${f1(x+Math.cos(a)*d)}" cy="${f1(y+Math.sin(a)*d)}" rx="${f1(R*.07)}" ry="${f1(R*.035)}" style="fill:var(--nucleus);opacity:.55"/>`}}
  if(inf>0)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(R*.97)}" style="fill:var(--fat-hot);opacity:${f1(inf*.3)}"/><circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(R)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--fat-hot);stroke-width:${f1(1.3+inf*1.6)}"/>`;
  return {svg:s+'</g>',at:{c:[x,y],R,nucleus:nuc}}}

function macrophage(x,y,r=9,o={}){const rr=rng(o.seed||7),m1=o.kind==='M1',n=m1?12:10,P=[];
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const a=i/n*Math.PI*2,k=m1?(i%2?1.35+rr()*.25:.82):(1+(rr()-.5)*.3);P.push([x+Math.cos(a)*r*k,y+Math.sin(a)*r*k])}
  let s=`<g style="opacity:${o.op==null?1:o.op}"><path d="${smoothPath(P)}" style="fill:var(--macro);fill-opacity:.55;stroke:${m1?'var(--risk)':'var(--macro)'};stroke-width:1.3"/>`;
  s+=`<path d="M${f1(x-r*.42)} ${f1(y-r*.1)}C${f1(x-r*.4)} ${f1(y-r*.6)} ${f1(x+r*.4)} ${f1(y-r*.6)} ${f1(x+r*.42)} ${f1(y-r*.05)}C${f1(x+r*.2)} ${f1(y+r*.05)} ${f1(x+r*.05)} ${f1(y+r*.3)} ${f1(x-r*.05)} ${f1(y+r*.12)}C${f1(x-r*.2)} ${f1(y+r*.3)} ${f1(x-r*.45)} ${f1(y+r*.2)} ${f1(x-r*.42)} ${f1(y-r*.1)}Z" style="fill:var(--nucleus)"/>`;
  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){const a=rr()*6.28,d=r*(.45+rr()*.25);s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x+Math.cos(a)*d)}" cy="${f1(y+Math.sin(a)*d)}" r="${f1(r*.08)}" style="fill:var(--ink);opacity:.45"/>`}
  return s+'</g>'}

function adiposeTissue(x,y,w,h,o={}){const sz=o.size==null?.5:clamp(o.size),d=(o.cell||28)*lerp(.72,1.3,sz),inf=clamp(o.inflamed||0),mc=clamp(o.macro||0),
  hyp=clamp(o.hypoxia||0),ves=o.vessel==null?0:clamp(o.vessel),id=kid('at'),rr=rng(o.seed||5),cells=[];
  const dy=d*.866;for(let j=-1;j*dy<h+d;j++)for(let i=-1;i*d<w+d;i++){const cx=x+i*d+(j%2?d/2:0)+(rr()-.5)*d*.12,cy=y+j*dy+(rr()-.5)*d*.12;cells.push([cx,cy,d*.56,rr(),rr()])}
  let s=`<defs><clipPath id="${id}"><rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(w)}" height="${f1(h)}" rx="10"/></clipPath></defs><g clip-path="url(#${id})">`;
  s+=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(w)}" height="${f1(h)}" style="fill:var(--cyto)"/>`;
  const vy=u=>y+h*(.55+.25*Math.sin(u*Math.PI*2.2+1)),vP=[];for(let i=0;i<=24;i++){const u=i/24;vP.push([x-6+(w+12)*u,vy(u)])}
  cells.forEach((c,i)=>{const hot=c[3]<inf,far=Math.abs(c[1]-vy((c[0]-x)/w))/h;
    s+=adipocyte(c[0],c[1],c[2]/1.18*1.0,{size:1,kind:o.kind,inflamed:hot?.8:0,seed:3+i,ang:c[4]*360}).svg;
    if(hyp>0&&far>.25)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(c[0])}" cy="${f1(c[1])}" r="${f1(c[2]*.9)}" style="fill:var(--tx);opacity:${f1(hyp*.18*clamp((far-.25)*3))}"/>`});
  if(ves>0)s+=`<path d="${smoothPath(vP,false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--vessel);stroke-width:4;stroke-linecap:round;opacity:${f1(ves*(1-hyp*.5))}"/>`;
  if(mc>0)cells.forEach((c,i)=>{if(!(c[3]<inf))return;const n=Math.round(1+mc*3);for(let k=0;k<n;k++){const a=k/n*Math.PI*2+c[4]*6;
    s+=macrophage(c[0]+Math.cos(a)*c[2]*.92,c[1]+Math.sin(a)*c[2]*.92,Math.max(3.5,d*.13),{seed:i*7+k,kind:'M1',op:clamp(mc*1.4)})}});
  s+='</g>';
  if(o.frame)s+=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(w)}" height="${f1(h)}" rx="10" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
  return {svg:s,at:{cells:cells.filter(c=>c[0]>x&&c[0]<x+w&&c[1]>y&&c[1]<y+h).map(c=>[c[0],c[1],c[2]]),c:[x+w/2,y+h/2]}}}

/* ---- gut ---- */
/* the stomach's outline in local units (130 x 140), front view: fundus on the viewer's right, pylorus on the left */
const ST_LESSER=[[68,32],[64,56],[58,72],[46,82],[32,82],[20,79]];          /* cardia down the lesser curvature to the pylorus */
const ST_GREATER=[[18,93],[32,103],[54,109],[78,103],[96,86],[106,62],[108,40],[100,22],[88,14],[76,16]]; /* pylorus round the greater curvature to the fundus */
const ST_SLEEVE=[[19,92],[32,95],[46,93],[60,86],[70,72],[75,54],[77,36],[76,24]];  /* a narrow tube beside the lesser curvature */
function stomach(x,y,s=1,o={}){const v=o.variant||'normal',m=o.morph==null?1:clamp(o.morph),T=_tr(x,y,s),fill=clamp(o.fill||0),id=kid('st'),ghost=o.ghost!==false;
  const normal=[...ST_LESSER,...ST_GREATER];
  const tube=(P,wd,col,line,op=1)=>`<path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:${line};stroke-width:${f1((wd+2.4)*s)};stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;opacity:${op}"/><path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:${col};stroke-width:${f1(wd*s)};stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;opacity:${op}"/>`;
  const shape=(P,extra='')=>`<path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T))}" style="fill:var(--stomach);stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1.6${extra}"/>`;
  const foodIn=P=>{if(fill<=0)return '';const ys=P.map(p=>p[1]),y0=Math.max(...ys),y1=Math.min(...ys),ly=lerp(y0,y1+6,fill);
    return `<defs><clipPath id="${id}f"><path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T))}"/></clipPath></defs><rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y+ly*s)}" width="${f1(130*s)}" height="${f1((y0-ly+4)*s)}" clip-path="url(#${id}f)" style="fill:var(--gut-line);opacity:.35"/>`};
  let g='',at={eso:T([73,-8]),cardia:T([70,30]),fundus:T([92,26]),body:T([84,64]),antrum:T([40,92]),pylorus:T([16,86]),duo:T([8,128]),pouch:null,out:T([8,128])};
  const eso=[[73,-8],[72,10],[70,30]],duo=[[16,86],[6,96],[4,112],[8,128]];
  if(v==='normal'||v==='band'){
    g+=tube(eso,9,'var(--stomach)','var(--gut-line)')+tube(duo,10,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)')+shape(normal)+foodIn(normal);
    g+=`<path d="${smoothPath([[66,44],[60,66],[46,78]].map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1;opacity:.45"/>`;
    if(v==='band'){const b=T([71,38]);g+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(m)}"><ellipse cx="${f1(b[0])}" cy="${f1(b[1])}" rx="${f1(15*s)}" ry="${f1(5*s)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--device);stroke-width:${f1(5*s)}"/><path d="${smoothPath([[84,40],[100,48],[118,62]].map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--device);stroke-width:${f1(1.6*s)}"/><circle cx="${f1(T([120,64])[0])}" cy="${f1(T([120,64])[1])}" r="${f1(5*s)}" style="fill:var(--device)"/></g>`;at.pouch=T([72,30])}}
  else if(v==='sleeve'||v==='switch'){
    const G2=ST_GREATER.map((p,i)=>{const q=ST_SLEEVE[Math.round(i/(ST_GREATER.length-1)*(ST_SLEEVE.length-1))];return [lerp(p[0],q[0],m),lerp(p[1],q[1],m)]});
    const P=[...ST_LESSER,...G2];
    if(ghost&&m>0)g+=`<path d="${smoothPath(normal.map(T))}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:4 4;opacity:${f1(m*.7)}"/>`;
    g+=tube(eso,9,'var(--stomach)','var(--gut-line)');
    if(v==='switch'){g+=tube([[16,86],[8,92],[4,100]],10,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)');at.out=T([4,104])}
    else g+=tube(duo,10,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)');
    g+=shape(P)+foodIn(P);
    if(m>.5)g+=`<path d="${smoothPath(G2.slice(1,-1).map(p=>[p[0]+1.5,p[1]]).map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--device);stroke-width:${f1(1.4*s)};stroke-dasharray:${f1(2*s)} ${f1(2*s)};opacity:${f1(ramp(m,.5,1))}"/>`;
    if(v==='switch')g+=`<path d="${ptsD([[0,104],[10,100]].map(T))}" style="stroke:var(--device);stroke-width:${f1(2*s)}"/>`;
    at.body=T([66,62])}
  else if(v==='bypass'){
    const pouch=[[66,24],[80,22],[84,34],[80,48],[70,52],[64,42]];
    g+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(lerp(1,.45,m))}">`+tube(duo,10,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)')+shape(normal)+'</g>';
    g+=tube(eso,9,'var(--stomach)','var(--gut-line)');
    const roux=[[74,50],[76,72],[90,98],[104,122],[108,140]];
    g+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(m)}">`+tube(roux,10,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)')+shape(pouch)+foodIn(pouch)+'</g>';
    g+=`<path d="${smoothPath([[60,54],[72,56],[86,50],[96,40]].map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--device);stroke-width:${f1(1.4*s)};stroke-dasharray:${f1(2*s)} ${f1(2*s)};opacity:${f1(m)}"/>`;
    at.pouch=T([74,36]);at.out=T([108,140])}
  if(o.labels){const L=(p,t,a)=>kitLabel(p[0],p[1],t,{a});
    g+=L(T([80,-4]),'oesophagus')+(v==='bypass'?L(T([90,30]),'pouch','')+L(T([60,122]),'bypassed stomach','m')+L(T([112,150]),'Roux limb','m'):L(T([110,22]),'fundus','')+L(T([66,124]),v==='sleeve'||v==='switch'?'sleeve':'body','m'))+L(T([-4,86]),'pylorus','e')+(v==='switch'?'':L(T([-6,128]),'duodenum','e'))}
  return {svg:g,at,w:130*s,h:140*s}}

function gutTract(x,y,s=1,o={}){const v=o.variant||'normal',m=o.morph==null?1:clamp(o.morph),T=_tr(x,y,s),gl=o.glow||{},dim=o.dim==null?1:1-clamp(o.dim)*.7;
  const tube=(P,wd,col,line,op=1)=>`<path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:${line};stroke-width:${f1((wd+2.4)*s)};stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;opacity:${op}"/><path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:${col};stroke-width:${f1(wd*s)};stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;opacity:${op}"/>`;
  const colon=[[44,246],[34,226],[30,180],[34,150],[60,144],[110,148],[160,142],[180,150],[182,190],[178,232],[160,250],[124,252],[106,266]];
  const duo=[[66,104],[54,114],[50,132],[58,148],[80,152],[100,144]];
  const small=[[100,144],[128,158],[150,166],[156,180],[134,186],[96,180],[70,184],[66,198],[92,206],[130,202],[154,210],[150,226],[120,230],[90,224],[68,226],[56,236],[46,242]];
  const SP=crPts(small,false,8),sAt=polyAt(SP);
  let g=`<g style="opacity:${f1(dim)}">`;
  /* colon behind, with haustra */
  g+=tube(colon,15,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)',.85);
  crPts(colon,false,4).forEach((p,i,A)=>{if(i%3||!A[i+1])return;const q=A[i+1],a=Math.atan2(q[1]-p[1],q[0]-p[0])+Math.PI/2,P=T(p);g+=`<line x1="${f1(P[0]+Math.cos(a)*7*s)}" y1="${f1(P[1]+Math.sin(a)*7*s)}" x2="${f1(P[0]-Math.cos(a)*7*s)}" y2="${f1(P[1]-Math.sin(a)*7*s)}" style="stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1;opacity:.5"/>`});
  /* pancreas, partly behind the stomach */
  const pan=[[62,118],[80,112],[110,110],[140,104],[158,100],[160,108],[140,116],[108,122],[80,128],[64,128]];
  g+=`<path d="${smoothPath(pan.map(T))}" style="fill:var(--cyto);stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
  /* small intestine */
  const join=sAt(.32);
  g+=tube(small,9,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)');
  g+=tube(duo,10,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)');
  const st=stomach(x+50*s,y+8*s,s,{variant:v,morph:m,fill:o.fill,ghost:true});
  g+=st.svg;
  if(v==='bypass'){const a=st.at.out,b=T(join);g+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(m)}">`+tube([[(a[0]-x)/s,(a[1]-y)/s],[150,160],[(b[0]-x)/s,(b[1]-y)/s]],9,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)')+'</g>';
    g+=`<circle cx="${f1(b[0])}" cy="${f1(b[1])}" r="${f1(4*s)}" style="fill:var(--device);opacity:${f1(m)}"/>`}
  const ile=sAt(.84);
  if(v==='switch'){const a=st.at.out,b=T(ile);g+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(m)}">`+tube([[(a[0]-x)/s,(a[1]-y)/s],[30,120],[24,170],[(b[0]-x)/s-10,(b[1]-y)/s]],9,'var(--gut)','var(--gut-line)')+'</g>'}
  /* glows */
  const glow=(p,v2,col)=>v2>0?`<circle cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" r="${f1(14*s)}" style="fill:${col};opacity:${f1(v2*.35)}"/><circle cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" r="${f1(6*s)}" style="fill:${col};opacity:${f1(v2*.8)}"/>`:'';
  g+=glow(st.at.fundus,clamp(gl.stomach||0),'var(--ghrelin)')+glow(T([54,124]),clamp(gl.duo||0),'var(--gip)')+glow(T(ile),clamp(gl.ileum||0),'var(--glp1)')+glow(T([128,110]),clamp(gl.pancreas||0),'var(--insulin)');
  /* the route food takes */
  const so=st.at;let R;
  const toL=p=>[(p[0]-x)/s,(p[1]-y)/s];
  if(v==='bypass')R=[toL(so.eso),toL(so.pouch),toL(so.out),[150,160],join,...SP.slice(Math.round(SP.length*.32))];
  else if(v==='switch')R=[toL(so.eso),toL(so.body),toL(so.pylorus),[30,120],[24,170],[ile[0]-10,ile[1]],...SP.slice(Math.round(SP.length*.84))];
  else R=[toL(so.eso),toL(so.body),toL(so.antrum),toL(so.pylorus),...duo,...SP];
  R=R.concat(colon);
  const RP=crPts(R,false,4).map(T),route=polyAt(RP);
  if(o.food!=null&&o.food>0&&o.food<1){const p=route(o.food);g+=`<circle cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" r="${f1(5.5*s)}" style="fill:var(--gut-line);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1.5"/>`}
  if(o.labels){const L=(p,t,a)=>kitLabel(p[0],p[1],t,{a});
    g+=L(T([150,14]),'stomach','')+L(T([46,108]),'duodenum','e')+L(T([150,128]),'pancreas','')+L(T([112,196]),'small intestine','m')+L(T([196,236]),'colon','e')}
  g+='</g>';
  return {svg:g,at:{eso:so.eso,stomach:so.fundus,pylorus:so.pylorus,duo:T([54,124]),jejunum:T(sAt(.15)),ileum:T(ile),colon:T([30,190]),pancreas:T([128,110]),pouch:so.pouch,join:T(join)},route,w:200*s,h:270*s}}

/* ---- brain ---- */
const BR_OUT=[[8,62],[10,38],[24,18],[48,6],[78,4],[104,12],[122,30],[128,52],[124,72],[110,84],[94,86],[86,96],[78,108],[72,104],[70,92],[54,92],[34,90],[16,80]];
function brainHypothalamus(x,y,s=1,o={}){const T=_tr(x,y,s),pomc=clamp(o.pomc||0),agrp=clamp(o.agrp||0),mc4r=clamp(o.mc4r||0),inset=o.inset!==false,id=kid('hy');
  let g=`<path d="${smoothPath(BR_OUT.map(T))}" style="fill:var(--brain);stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:1.6"/>`;
  [[[22,40],[40,30],[58,34],[74,24],[96,28]],[[18,60],[40,54],[62,60],[84,50],[108,54]],[[40,76],[60,72],[80,76]]].forEach(P=>{g+=`<path d="${smoothPath(P.map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:1.1;opacity:.55"/>`});
  /* cerebellum and brainstem */
  g+=`<path d="${smoothPath([[96,78],[114,74],[124,82],[116,94],[100,94]].map(T))}" style="fill:var(--brain);stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
  g+=`<path d="${smoothPath([[84,90],[92,100],[94,118],[88,126],[80,118],[78,102]].map(T))}" style="fill:var(--brain);stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
  const hy=T([66,84]),bs=T([88,112]);
  g+=`<circle cx="${f1(hy[0])}" cy="${f1(hy[1])}" r="${f1(6*s)}" style="fill:var(--pomc);opacity:${f1(.35+.4*Math.max(pomc,agrp))}"/><circle cx="${f1(hy[0])}" cy="${f1(hy[1])}" r="${f1(6*s)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
  g+=`<path d="${ptsD([T([64,90]),T([66,100])])}" style="stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:${f1(2.4*s)};stroke-linecap:round"/><circle cx="${f1(T([66,103])[0])}" cy="${f1(T([66,103])[1])}" r="${f1(3.4*s)}" style="fill:var(--brain);stroke:var(--brain-line)"/>`;
  let at={hypo:hy,brainstem:bs,arc:hy,pomc:hy,agrp:hy,pvn:hy,bloodIn:T([66,96]),inset:null};
  if(inset){const C=T([196,92]),r=64*s;
    g+=`<path d="${ptsD([[hy[0]+5*s,hy[1]-4*s],[C[0]-r*.86,C[1]-r*.5]])}${ptsD([[hy[0]+5*s,hy[1]+4*s],[C[0]-r*.86,C[1]+r*.5]])}" style="stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.2;fill:none"/>`;
    g+=`<defs><clipPath id="${id}"><circle cx="${f1(C[0])}" cy="${f1(C[1])}" r="${f1(r)}"/></clipPath></defs><circle cx="${f1(C[0])}" cy="${f1(C[1])}" r="${f1(r)}" style="fill:var(--brain);stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:1.6"/>`;
    const P=(u,v)=>[C[0]+u*r,C[1]+v*r];
    g+=`<g clip-path="url(#${id})"><path d="${smoothPath([P(-.05,-1.1),P(.05,-1.1),P(.06,.2),P(.12,.6),P(0,.82),P(-.12,.6),P(-.06,.2)])}" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--brain-line);stroke-width:1"/>`;
    g+=`<path d="${smoothPath([P(-.5,1.2),P(-.2,.84),P(0,.9),P(.2,.84),P(.5,1.2)],false)}" style="fill:var(--vessel);fill-opacity:.12;stroke:var(--vessel);stroke-width:1.2;opacity:.7"/></g>`;
    const pv=[P(-.3,-.42),P(.3,-.42)],po=[P(-.3,.5),P(-.42,.38),P(-.2,.34)],ag=[P(.3,.5),P(.42,.38),P(.2,.34)];
    /* PVN */
    pv.forEach(p=>{g+=`<ellipse cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" rx="${f1(r*.2)}" ry="${f1(r*.13)}" style="fill:var(--pomc);opacity:${f1(.12+.5*mc4r)}"/><ellipse cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" rx="${f1(r*.2)}" ry="${f1(r*.13)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/>`;
      for(let k=0;k<3;k++)g+=`<circle cx="${f1(p[0]+(k-1)*r*.1)}" cy="${f1(p[1]+(k%2?-1:1)*r*.03)}" r="${f1(r*.035)}" style="fill:var(--ink);opacity:.7"/>`});
    /* projections */
    po.forEach((p,i)=>{if(pomc<=0)return;const q=pv[0];g+=`<path d="M${f1(p[0])} ${f1(p[1])}Q${f1(p[0]-r*.15)} ${f1((p[1]+q[1])/2)} ${f1(q[0]-r*.04)} ${f1(q[1]+r*.12)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--pomc);stroke-width:${f1(1+pomc*1.6)};opacity:${f1(.3+pomc*.7)}"/>`});
    ag.forEach((p,i)=>{if(agrp<=0)return;const q=pv[1],e=[q[0]+r*.04,q[1]+r*.12];g+=`<path d="M${f1(p[0])} ${f1(p[1])}Q${f1(p[0]+r*.15)} ${f1((p[1]+q[1])/2)} ${f1(e[0])} ${f1(e[1])}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--agrp);stroke-width:${f1(1+agrp*1.6)};opacity:${f1(.3+agrp*.7)}"/><path d="M${f1(e[0]-r*.06)} ${f1(e[1]+r*.01)}L${f1(e[0]+r*.06)} ${f1(e[1]-r*.01)}" style="stroke:var(--agrp);stroke-width:2.4;opacity:${f1(.3+agrp*.7)}"/>`});
    po.forEach(p=>{if(pomc>0)g+=`<circle cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" r="${f1(r*(.07+.06*pomc))}" style="fill:var(--pomc);opacity:${f1(pomc*.35)}"/>`;g+=`<circle cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" r="${f1(r*.055)}" style="fill:var(--pomc);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1"/>`});
    ag.forEach(p=>{if(agrp>0)g+=`<circle cx="${f1(p[0])}" cy="${f1(p[1])}" r="${f1(r*(.07+.06*agrp))}" style="fill:var(--agrp);opacity:${f1(agrp*.35)}"/>`;const k=r*.065;g+=`<path d="M${f1(p[0])} ${f1(p[1]-k)}L${f1(p[0]+k)} ${f1(p[1]+k*.8)}L${f1(p[0]-k)} ${f1(p[1]+k*.8)}Z" style="fill:var(--agrp);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1"/>`});
    at={hypo:hy,brainstem:bs,arc:P(0,.45),pomc:P(-.3,.42),agrp:P(.3,.42),pvn:P(0,-.42),bloodIn:P(0,.96),inset:[C[0],C[1],r]};
    if(o.labels){g+=kitLabel(P(0,-.7)[0],P(0,-.7)[1],'PVN (MC4R)',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(P(-.62,.72)[0],P(-.62,.72)[1],'POMC',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(P(.62,.72)[0],P(.62,.72)[1],'AgRP',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(P(0,.22)[0],P(0,.22)[1],'arcuate',{a:'m'})}}
  if(o.labels){g+=kitLabel(T([66,72])[0],T([66,72])[1]-2,'hypothalamus',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(bs[0]+8*s,bs[1]+6,'brainstem',{})}
  return {svg:g,at}}

/* ---- signals ---- */
const HORMONE_INFO={ghrelin:{name:'ghrelin',col:'var(--ghrelin)'},leptin:{name:'leptin',col:'var(--leptin)'},glp1:{name:'GLP-1',col:'var(--glp1)'},
  pyy:{name:'PYY',col:'var(--pyy)'},insulin:{name:'insulin',col:'var(--insulin)'},gip:{name:'GIP',col:'var(--gip)'},cck:{name:'CCK',col:'var(--gip)'},drug:{name:'medicine',col:'var(--rx-drug)'}};
function hormoneDot(x,y,kind='glp1',o={}){const r=o.r||5,H=HORMONE_INFO[kind]||HORMONE_INFO.glp1,c=H.col,op=o.op==null?1:o.op,st=`fill:${c};stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1`;
  const poly=(n,rot=-Math.PI/2,rad=r)=>{let d='';for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const a=rot+i/n*Math.PI*2;d+=(i?'L':'M')+f1(x+Math.cos(a)*rad)+' '+f1(y+Math.sin(a)*rad)}return d+'Z'};
  let s;
  if(kind==='ghrelin')s=`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(r)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  else if(kind==='leptin')s=`<path d="${poly(4,-Math.PI/2,r*1.2)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  else if(kind==='pyy')s=`<path d="${poly(3,-Math.PI/2,r*1.25)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  else if(kind==='insulin')s=`<rect x="${f1(x-r*.9)}" y="${f1(y-r*.9)}" width="${f1(r*1.8)}" height="${f1(r*1.8)}" rx="${f1(r*.4)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  else if(kind==='gip')s=`<path d="${poly(5,-Math.PI/2,r*1.1)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  else if(kind==='cck'){let d='';for(let i=0;i<8;i++){const a=-Math.PI/2+i/8*Math.PI*2,rad=i%2?r*.5:r*1.25;d+=(i?'L':'M')+f1(x+Math.cos(a)*rad)+' '+f1(y+Math.sin(a)*rad)}s=`<path d="${d}Z" style="${st}"/>`}
  else if(kind==='drug')s=`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(r*1.55)}" style="fill:none;stroke:${c};stroke-width:1.4"/><path d="${poly(6,0,r)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  else s=`<path d="${poly(6,0,r*1.05)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  if(o.label)s+=`<text x="${f1(x+r*1.9)}" y="${f1(y+3.5)}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink)">${H.name}</text>`;
  return `<g style="opacity:${f1(op)}">${s}</g>`}

/* ---- organs and things ---- */
const LV_OUT=[[4,30],[20,10],[52,4],[90,6],[122,12],[138,22],[132,34],[110,46],[86,60],[60,78],[40,86],[22,80],[8,62]];
function liver(x,y,s=1,o={}){const T=_tr(x,y,s),fat=clamp(o.fat||0),inf=clamp(o.inflamed||0),sc=clamp(o.scar||0),id=kid('lv'),P=LV_OUT.map(T),rr=rng(o.seed||17);
  let g=`<defs><clipPath id="${id}"><path d="${smoothPath(P)}"/></clipPath></defs><path d="${smoothPath(P)}" style="fill:var(--liver);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-opacity:.5"/>`;
  g+=`<g clip-path="url(#${id})">`;
  g+=`<path d="${smoothPath([[86,8],[80,30],[74,54]].map(T),false)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;opacity:.3"/>`;
  const n=Math.round(fat*60);for(let i=0;i<70;i++){const p=[4+rr()*134,4+rr()*82],r=2+rr()*3.5;if(i>=n||!inPoly(p,LV_OUT))continue;const q=T(p);g+=`<circle cx="${f1(q[0])}" cy="${f1(q[1])}" r="${f1(r*s)}" style="fill:var(--liverfat);opacity:.92"/>`}
  if(inf>0)for(let i=0;i<14;i++){const p=[10+rr()*120,8+rr()*70];if(!inPoly(p,LV_OUT))continue;const q=T(p);g+=`<circle cx="${f1(q[0])}" cy="${f1(q[1])}" r="${f1(2.4*s)}" style="fill:var(--risk);opacity:${f1(inf*.8)}"/>`}
  if(sc>0)for(let i=0;i<9;i++){const a=[10+rr()*110,10+rr()*60],b=[a[0]+20+rr()*20,a[1]+(rr()-.5)*30];g+=`<path d="${ptsD([T(a),T([(a[0]+b[0])/2,(a[1]+b[1])/2+(rr()-.5)*10]),T(b)])}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:${f1(1.6*s)};opacity:${f1(sc*.8)}"/>`}
  g+='</g>';
  return {svg:g,at:{c:T([60,40]),right:T([34,44]),left:T([112,24]),hilum:T([70,58])}}}

function pen(x,y,s=1,o={}){const L=120*s,h=16*s,ang=o.ang||0,nd=clamp(o.needle||0),pr=clamp(o.press||0),dial=clamp(o.dial||0),cap=!!o.cap;
  const x0=-L/2,x1=L/2;let g=`<g transform="translate(${f1(x)} ${f1(y)}) rotate(${f1(ang)})">`;
  /* needle end on the left */
  if(nd>0&&!cap)g+=`<line x1="${f1(x0+2*s)}" y1="0" x2="${f1(x0-14*s*nd)}" y2="0" style="stroke:var(--device);stroke-width:${f1(1.2*s)}"/>`;
  g+=`<rect x="${f1(x0)}" y="${f1(-h/2)}" width="${f1(L*.82)}" height="${f1(h)}" rx="${f1(h/2)}" style="fill:var(--pen);stroke:var(--pen-dark);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
  g+=`<rect x="${f1(x0+L*.14)}" y="${f1(-h*.28)}" width="${f1(L*.2)}" height="${f1(h*.56)}" rx="${f1(h*.2)}" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--pen-dark);stroke-width:.8"/>`;
  g+=`<rect x="${f1(x0+L*.17)}" y="${f1(-h*.16)}" width="${f1(L*.14)}" height="${f1(h*.32)}" rx="${f1(h*.1)}" style="fill:var(--rx-drug);opacity:.55"/>`;
  g+=`<rect x="${f1(x0+L*.4)}" y="${f1(-h/2)}" width="${f1(L*.16)}" height="${f1(h)}" style="fill:var(--rx-drug);opacity:.85"/>`;
  /* dial and button */
  const dx=x0+L*.82;g+=`<rect x="${f1(dx)}" y="${f1(-h*.56)}" width="${f1(L*.1)}" height="${f1(h*1.12)}" rx="${f1(3*s)}" style="fill:var(--pen-dark)"/>`;
  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){const u=(i/4+dial)%1;g+=`<line x1="${f1(dx+L*.1*u)}" x2="${f1(dx+L*.1*u)}" y1="${f1(-h*.5)}" y2="${f1(h*.5)}" style="stroke:var(--pen);stroke-width:1;opacity:${f1(.3+.7*Math.sin(u*Math.PI))}"/>`}
  g+=`<rect x="${f1(dx+L*.1+(1-pr)*L*.06-L*.02)}" y="${f1(-h*.32)}" width="${f1(L*.06)}" height="${f1(h*.64)}" rx="${f1(2*s)}" style="fill:var(--rx-drug)"/>`;
  if(cap)g+=`<rect x="${f1(x0-L*.12)}" y="${f1(-h*.6)}" width="${f1(L*.34)}" height="${f1(h*1.2)}" rx="${f1(h*.5)}" style="fill:var(--pen-dark);opacity:.92"/>`;
  g+='</g>';
  const a=ang*Math.PI/180,P=u=>[x+Math.cos(a)*u,y+Math.sin(a)*u];
  return {svg:g,at:{tip:P(x0-14*s*nd),back:P(x1)}}}

function person(x,y,s=100,o={}){const k=s/100,w=clamp(o.size==null?.3:o.size),kidF=!!o.kid,col=o.col||'var(--figure)',line=o.line||'var(--figure-line)';
  const hr=kidF?11:8.5,hy=kidF?11.5:9,by=kidF?(v=>22+(v-19)*.82):(v=>v),bx=kidF?.9:1;
  const B=(px,py)=>[px*bx,by(py)];
  const half=[B(3.6,18.5),B(11+3*w,23),B(9.5+5.5*w,31),B(8.6+9.4*w,45),B(10+9.6*w,54),B(9.6+8.4*w,64),B(6.4+3.6*w,77),B(5.4+3*w,86),B(4.2+1.4*w,95),B(6.6+1.4*w,99.4),B(1.6+.6*w,99.6),B(1.8+.7*w,95),B(2.3+1.5*w,78),B(1.4+1.3*w,66),B(0,61+1.5*w)];
  const full=[...half,...half.slice(0,-1).reverse().map(p=>[-p[0],p[1]])].map(p=>[x+p[0]*k,y+p[1]*k]);
  /* drop the duplicate centre point at the crotch, keep the outline symmetric */
  const arm=sg=>[B(11.4+3*w,22.6),B(13.6+5.6*w,31),B(14.6+7.4*w,45),B(14+6.2*w,57),B(13.4+5.6*w,62.6),B(11.2+5*w,62.2),B(11.2+5.4*w,56),B(11.6+6.4*w,45),B(10.4+5.6*w,32)].map(p=>[x+sg*p[0]*k,y+p[1]*k]);
  let g=`<g style="opacity:${o.op==null?1:o.op}">`;
  const st=`fill:${col};stroke:${line};stroke-width:${f1(Math.max(.8,1.1*k))};stroke-linejoin:round`;
  g+=`<path d="${smoothPath(arm(1))}" style="${st}"/><path d="${smoothPath(arm(-1))}" style="${st}"/>`;
  g+=`<path d="${smoothPath(full)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  g+=`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y+hy*k)}" r="${f1(hr*k)}" style="${st}"/>`;
  g+='</g>';
  const P=(px,py)=>[x+px*k,y+by(py)*k];
  return {svg:g,at:{head:[x,y+hy*k],chest:P(0,32),belly:P(0,46),liver:P(-4,40),hip:P(0,56),knee:P(-5,77),foot:P(-5,99)},w:2*(14.6+7.4*w)*k}}

function seesaw(x,y,w=200,o={}){const tl=clamp(o.tilt||0,-1,1),a=tl*12*Math.PI/180,hh=22,cx=x,cy=y-hh;
  /* tilt < 0: the left end sinks (heavier) */
  const L=[cx-Math.cos(a)*w/2,cy-Math.sin(a)*w/2],R=[cx+Math.cos(a)*w/2,cy+Math.sin(a)*w/2];
  let g=`<path d="M${f1(cx)} ${f1(cy)}L${f1(cx-14)} ${f1(y)}L${f1(cx+14)} ${f1(y)}Z" style="fill:var(--panel-2);stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.4"/>`;
  g+=`<line x1="${f1(L[0])}" y1="${f1(L[1])}" x2="${f1(R[0])}" y2="${f1(R[1])}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:4;stroke-linecap:round"/><circle cx="${f1(cx)}" cy="${f1(cy)}" r="3.5" style="fill:var(--ink)"/>`;
  const stack=(p,v,col)=>{let s='';const n=Math.round(clamp(v)*5),bw=w*.16,bh=9;for(let i=0;i<n;i++)s+=`<rect x="${f1(p[0]-bw/2)}" y="${f1(p[1]-4-(i+1)*(bh+1))}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="${bh}" rx="2" style="fill:${col};stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1"/>`;return s};
  const lp=[lerp(L[0],cx,.18),lerp(L[1],cy,.18)],rp=[lerp(R[0],cx,.18),lerp(R[1],cy,.18)];
  g+=stack(lp,o.lw||0,o.lcol||'var(--fat)')+stack(rp,o.rw||0,o.rcol||'var(--lean)');
  if(o.left)g+=kitLabel(lp[0],lp[1]+16,o.left,{a:'m'});
  if(o.right)g+=kitLabel(rp[0],rp[1]+16,o.right,{a:'m'});
  return {svg:g,at:{left:lp,right:rp}}}

/* ---- charts ---- */
function curveAxes(x,y,w,h,o={}){const x0=o.x0||0,x1=o.x1==null?1:o.x1,y0=o.y0||0,y1=o.y1==null?1:o.y1,xf=o.xfmt||(v=>v),yf=o.yfmt||(v=>v);
  const X=v=>x+w*(v-x0)/(x1-x0),Y=v=>y+h-h*(v-y0)/(y1-y0);
  let s=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(w)}" height="${f1(h)}" style="fill:var(--field)"/>`;
  (o.yt||[]).forEach(v=>{const yy=Y(v);if(o.grid!==false)s+=`<line x1="${f1(x)}" x2="${f1(x+w)}" y1="${f1(yy)}" y2="${f1(yy)}" class="grid"/>`;s+=`<text x="${f1(x-6)}" y="${f1(yy+3.5)}" class="t-xs t-end">${yf(v)}</text>`});
  (o.xt||[]).forEach(v=>{const xx=X(v);s+=`<line x1="${f1(xx)}" x2="${f1(xx)}" y1="${f1(y+h)}" y2="${f1(y+h+4)}" class="axis"/><text x="${f1(xx)}" y="${f1(y+h+16)}" class="t-xs t-mid">${xf(v)}</text>`});
  s+=`<line x1="${f1(x)}" x2="${f1(x+w)}" y1="${f1(y+h)}" y2="${f1(y+h)}" class="axis"/><line x1="${f1(x)}" x2="${f1(x)}" y1="${f1(y)}" y2="${f1(y+h)}" class="axis"/>`;
  if(o.xlabel)s+=`<text x="${f1(x+w)}" y="${f1(y+h+30)}" class="t-xs t-end">${o.xlabel}</text>`;
  if(o.ylabel)s+=`<text x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y-8)}" class="t-xs">${o.ylabel}</text>`;
  return {svg:s,X,Y}}
function plotLine(P,X,Y,o={}){if(!P.length)return {svg:'',end:null};const col=o.col||'var(--brand)';let Q=P.slice();
  const f=o.smooth&&P.length>2?monoFn(P):null;
  if(f){Q=[];const a=P[0][0],b=P[P.length-1][0];for(let i=0;i<=80;i++){const v=lerp(a,b,i/80);Q.push([v,f(v)])}}
  if(o.upto!=null){const u=o.upto,out=[];for(let i=0;i<Q.length;i++){if(Q[i][0]<=u)out.push(Q[i]);else{if(i>0){const p=Q[i-1],q=Q[i],t=(u-p[0])/((q[0]-p[0])||1);out.push([u,lerp(p[1],q[1],t)])}break}}Q=out}
  if(!Q.length)return {svg:'',end:null};
  const pts=Q.map(p=>[X(p[0]),Y(p[1])]);let s='';
  if(o.fill){const b=Y(o.base==null?0:o.base);s+=`<path d="${ptsD(pts)}L${f1(pts[pts.length-1][0])} ${f1(b)}L${f1(pts[0][0])} ${f1(b)}Z" style="fill:${col};opacity:.15"/>`}
  s+=`<path d="${ptsD(pts)}" style="fill:none;stroke:${col};stroke-width:${o.lw||2.6};stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-linecap:round${o.dash?';stroke-dasharray:'+o.dash:''}"/>`;
  const e=pts[pts.length-1];if(o.dot)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(e[0])}" cy="${f1(e[1])}" r="4.5" style="fill:${col};stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`;
  return {svg:s,end:e}}
function iconArray(x,y,o={}){const n=o.n||100,c=o.cols||10,sz=o.size||12,gp=o.gap==null?3:o.gap,base=o.base||'var(--line)';
  const groups=o.groups||[{k:o.k||0,col:o.col||'var(--brand)'}];const colOf=i=>{let acc=0;for(const g of groups){acc+=g.k;if(i<acc)return g.col}return base};
  const at=i=>[x+(i%c)*(sz+gp),y+Math.floor(i/c)*(sz+gp*1.4)];let s='';
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const[px,py]=at(i),f=colOf(i);
    if(o.shape==='dot')s+=`<circle cx="${f1(px+sz/2)}" cy="${f1(py+sz/2)}" r="${f1(sz*.42)}" style="fill:${f}"/>`;
    else{const r=sz*.18;s+=`<circle cx="${f1(px+sz/2)}" cy="${f1(py+r)}" r="${f1(r)}" style="fill:${f}"/><path d="M${f1(px+sz*.22)} ${f1(py+sz)}V${f1(py+sz*.62)}Q${f1(px+sz*.22)} ${f1(py+sz*.42)} ${f1(px+sz/2)} ${f1(py+sz*.42)}Q${f1(px+sz*.78)} ${f1(py+sz*.42)} ${f1(px+sz*.78)} ${f1(py+sz*.62)}V${f1(py+sz)}Z" style="fill:${f}"/>`}}
  return {svg:s,h:Math.ceil(n/c)*(sz+gp*1.4),w:c*(sz+gp)-gp,at}}
/* =============== routing (shared: tools/core/03-router.js) =============== */
const inits={},onShow={},onHide={};let cur=null;
/* Each module is its own page, so search engines can index it: the body names the
   module (data-page) and the way back up to the companion's first page (data-root).
   A page that carries every module, like the artifact, has no data-page and switches
   modules by #hash. */
const PAGE=document.body.dataset.page||'',UP=document.body.dataset.root||'';
const href=id=>PAGE?(id==='home'?UP||'./':UP+id+'/'):'#'+id;
function go(id,hash,replace){const u=href(id)+(location.protocol==='file:'?'index.html':'')+(hash||'');replace?location.replace(u):location.assign(u)}
/* the first page opened in a tab (not one reached by a click inside the guide) may reopen the module last read */
let fresh=false;try{fresh=!sessionStorage.getItem(PREFIX+'tab');sessionStorage.setItem(PREFIX+'tab','1')}catch(e){}
(function buildNav(){
  const amp=s=>s.replace(/&/g,'&amp;');
  let h='';
  for(const g of Object.keys(GROUPS).map(Number)){
    h+=`<div class="navgroup ${GROUPS[g][1]}"><h3>${amp(GROUPS[g][0])}</h3><ol>`;
    MODS.filter(m=>m.g===g).forEach(m=>{h+=`<li><a class="navbtn" href="${href(m.id)}" data-go="${m.id}"><span class="n">${m.n}</span><span>${amp(m.t)}</span></a></li>`});
    h+='</ol></div>';
  }
  $('#navgroups').innerHTML=h;
  let u='';
  Object.keys(GROUPS).map(Number).forEach(g=>{
    u+=`<div class="unit"><p class="eyebrow">Part ${g}</p><h2>${amp(GROUPS[g][0])}</h2><ol>`;
    MODS.filter(m=>m.g===g).forEach(m=>{u+=`<li><button data-go="${m.id}"><span class="n">${m.n}</span><b>${amp(m.t)}</b><small>${m.d}</small></button></li>`});
    u+='</ol></div>';
  });
  if($('#homeUnits'))$('#homeUnits').innerHTML=u;
  MODS.forEach((m,i)=>{
    const sec=$('#m-'+m.id);if(!sec)return;
    if(m.g)sec.classList.add(GROUPS[m.g][2]);
    if(m.id==='home')return;
    const p=MODS[i-1],n=MODS[i+1];
    const pg=document.createElement('div');pg.className='pager';
    pg.innerHTML=(p?`<button data-go="${p.id}"><small>← Previous</small><span>${amp(p.t)}</span></button>`:'')+(n?`<button class="next" data-go="${n.id}"><small>Next →</small><span>${amp(n.t)}</span></button>`:'');
    sec.appendChild(pg);
  });
})();
function show(id,keepScroll){
  if(!MODS.some(m=>m.id===id))id='home';
  if(PAGE&&id!==PAGE){
    /* boot asks first: for the #module of an old link, or for the module last read */
    if(cur){go(id);return}
    if(location.hash.slice(1)===id||(PAGE==='home'&&fresh)){go(id,'',true);return}
    id=PAGE;
  }
  const first=!cur;
  if(cur&&onHide[cur])onHide[cur]();
  $$('[data-mod]').forEach(s=>s.hidden=s.dataset.mod!==id);
  $$('.navbtn').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-current',b.dataset.go===id?'page':'false'));
  cur=id;
  if(inits[id]&&!inits[id].done){inits[id].done=true;inits[id]()}
  guardLive($('#m-'+id)||document);
  if(onShow[id])onShow[id]();
  store.set('last',id);
  if(!PAGE)try{history.replaceState(null,'','#'+id)}catch(e){}
  if(!keepScroll)window.scrollTo(0,0);
  const nb=$(`.navbtn[data-go="${id}"]`);
  if(nb&&matchMedia('(max-width:900px)').matches){const side=$('#side');side.scrollTo({left:nb.offsetLeft-side.clientWidth/2+nb.offsetWidth/2,behavior:RM?'auto':'smooth'})}
  if(first&&location.hash.startsWith('#src-'))flashSrc(location.hash.slice(5));
}
function flashSrc(k){const li=document.getElementById('src-'+k);if(li){li.scrollIntoView({block:'center',behavior:RM?'auto':'smooth'});li.classList.add('flash');setTimeout(()=>li.classList.remove('flash'),2200)}}
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{
  /* the skip link focuses the main column when that can take focus (it has a tabindex); otherwise the browser follows #main */
  const sk=e.target.closest('.skip'),mn=sk&&$('#main');if(mn&&mn.hasAttribute('tabindex')){e.preventDefault();mn.focus();return}
  const c=e.target.closest('sup.c');
  if(c){e.preventDefault();const k=c.dataset.ref.split(',')[0];if(PAGE&&PAGE!=='sources'){go('sources','#src-'+k);return}show('sources');flashSrc(k);return}
  const b=e.target.closest('[data-go]');if(b){if(b.href&&(e.metaKey||e.ctrlKey||e.shiftKey||e.altKey))return;e.preventDefault();show(b.dataset.go)}
});
/* theme: auto → light → dark */
/* language switch keeps the current module */
(function lang(){const a=$('#langBtn');if(!a)return;const base=a.getAttribute('href');
  const upd=()=>a.setAttribute('href',base+location.hash);['pointerdown','focus','click','mouseenter'].forEach(e=>a.addEventListener(e,upd));upd()})();
(function theme(){
  const btn=$('#themeBtn');const modes=['auto','light','dark'];let m=store.get('theme','auto');
  function apply(){if(m==='auto')document.documentElement.removeAttribute('data-theme');else document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme',m);btn.textContent='Theme: '+{auto:'auto',light:'light',dark:'dark'}[m]}
  btn.addEventListener('click',()=>{m=modes[(modes.indexOf(m)+1)%3];store.set('theme',m);apply()});apply();
})();
/* ---- narrow mode ----
   Phone stages are too small for the 720-wide layouts, so draw() asks NARROW()
   and lays its panels out in a tall column instead of a wide row. Modules that
   register a player are redrawn automatically when the stage crosses the
   threshold, so a rotation or a window resize re-lays-out the scene. */
const NARROW=()=>matchMedia('(max-width:820px)').matches;
const redraws={};
let _wasNarrow=NARROW(),_rt;
addEventListener('resize',()=>{clearTimeout(_rt);_rt=setTimeout(()=>{
  const n=NARROW();if(n===_wasNarrow)return;_wasNarrow=n;
  const f=redraws[cur];if(f)try{f()}catch(e){}
},160)});
/* fit the viewBox to the mode: wide|narrow are "w h" pairs */
function vb(svg,wide,narrow){const v=NARROW()?narrow:wide;svg.setAttribute('viewBox','0 0 '+v);svg.dataset.mode=NARROW()?'n':'w';return NARROW()}

/* ---- live regions ----
   Every frame of an animation rewrites its note panel, and a screen reader will
   announce an aria-live region each time its contents are replaced, even with the
   same text. Shadow innerHTML on those elements so an identical write is dropped:
   the reader hears the note once per real change, not sixty times a second. */
const _ihDesc=Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(Element.prototype,'innerHTML');
function guardLive(root=document){
  $$('[aria-live]',root).forEach(el=>{
    if(el._lguard)return;el._lguard=true;
    Object.defineProperty(el,'innerHTML',{configurable:true,
      get(){return _ihDesc.get.call(this)},
      set(v){if(v===this._lastHTML)return;this._lastHTML=v;_ihDesc.set.call(this,v)}});
  });
}

/* the shared player: a range input + a play button drive draw(t) */
function playWire(rg,pb,draw,dur,doneLabel='Replay',hideKey){
  let stopA=null;function stop(){if(stopA)stopA();stopA=null;pb.textContent='Play'}
  rg.addEventListener('input',()=>{stop();draw(+rg.value)});
  rg.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Enter'||e.key===' '){e.preventDefault();pb.click()}});
  if(!rg.getAttribute('aria-keyshortcuts'))rg.setAttribute('aria-keyshortcuts','Enter Space');
  pb.addEventListener('click',()=>{if(stopA){stop();return}let t0=+rg.value;const mx=+rg.max||1,mn=+rg.min||0;if(t0>=mx-(mx-mn)*.01)t0=mn;pb.textContent='Pause';
    stopA=animate((mx-t0)/(mx-mn)*dur,p=>{const t=t0+(mx-t0)*p;rg.value=t;draw(t)},()=>{stopA=null;pb.textContent=doneLabel})});
  if(hideKey){const prev=onHide[hideKey];onHide[hideKey]=()=>{prev&&prev();stop()}}
  if(hideKey){const prevR=redraws[hideKey];redraws[hideKey]=()=>{prevR&&prevR();stop();draw(+rg.value)}}
  return stop;
}
/* stepper buttons that jump the timeline */
function stepWire(el,steps,rg,draw,stop){
  el.innerHTML=steps.map((s,i)=>`<button data-st="${i}" aria-pressed="false"><b>${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</b><span>${s.t}</span></button>`).join('');
  el.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('[data-st]');if(!b)return;stop&&stop();const s=steps[+b.dataset.st];rg.value=s.at;draw(s.at)});
  el.setAttribute('role','group');el.setAttribute('aria-label','Steps');
  return i=>{$$('[data-st]',el).forEach((b,k)=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',k===i));
    /* screen readers hear the step name, not a bare number, when the slider moves */
    if(rg&&steps[i])rg.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',`Step ${i+1} of ${steps.length}: ${steps[i].t}`)};
}
function phaseOf(steps,t){let p=0;steps.forEach((s,i)=>{if(t>=s.from)p=i});return p}
function noteHTML(P){return `<div class="kicker">${P.k||''}</div><h4>${P.t}</h4>${P.txt?`<p>${P.txt}</p>`:''}${P.pt?`<div class="pt"><b>In plain words</b>${P.pt}</div>`:''}${P.hook?`<div class="hook"><b>Exam hook</b>${P.hook}</div>`:''}`}
/* =============== home: the appetite loop between gut, fat and brain, and how it pushes back =============== */
/* Everything drawn here is a schematic with no figures: the hormone particles and neuron glows show direction and
   balance, not amounts or times. Modules 1.4, 1.6 and 3.2 tell the story with sources. */
const HERO_CAP='Schematic, not to scale: no amounts or times are shown. Modules 1.4, 1.6 and 3.2 give them, with sources.';
const HERO_PH=[
  {from:0,t:'Before a meal',sub:'the stomach sends ghrelin; hunger neurons fire',k:'hungry'},
  {from:.17,t:'A meal arrives',sub:'the gut releases GLP-1 and PYY',k:'meal'},
  {from:.34,t:'Fullness',sub:'fullness neurons win; the drive to eat fades',k:'full'},
  {from:.5,t:'Stores report in',sub:'fat cells send leptin, a slow signal',k:'stores'},
  {from:.67,t:'After weight loss',sub:'leptin falls, hunger pushes back: biology',k:'after loss'},
  {from:.84,t:'A GLP-1 medicine',sub:'adds its own long-lasting fullness signal',k:'medicine'}];
/* the level of each signal along the schematic loop, 0..1 */
function heroLv(t){
  const ghr=Math.max(1-ramp(t,.14,.3),.15*bump(t,.5,.66),bump(t,.66,.86)*.95),
        glp=bump(t,.15,.5)*1,fill=Math.max(bump(t,.14,.6),0),
        size=t<.62?.62:lerp(.62,.22,ease(ramp(t,.62,.78))),
        lep=bump(t,.46,.7)*1+(t>.66?.18:0),
        drug=ramp(t,.84,.92),
        pomc=clamp(Math.max(ramp(t,.2,.36)*(1-ramp(t,.55,.7)),drug*.95)),
        agrp=clamp(Math.max(1-ramp(t,.18,.32),ramp(t,.68,.76)*(1-drug*.6))),
        mc4r=pomc*(1-agrp*.5);
  return {ghr:clamp(ghr),glp:clamp(glp),fill:clamp(fill),size,lep:clamp(lep),drug,pomc,agrp,mc4r}}
inits.home=()=>{
  const svg=$('#heroSvg'),rg=$('#heroT'),cap=$('#heroCap');
  /* particles travel along a quadratic curve from a source to the brain; ph shifts them so they stream */
  const stream=(a,b,bend,kind,n,lv,ph,r)=>{if(lv<=.02)return '';let s='';const c=[(a[0]+b[0])/2+bend[0],(a[1]+b[1])/2+bend[1]];
    s+=`<path d="M${f1(a[0])} ${f1(a[1])}Q${f1(c[0])} ${f1(c[1])} ${f1(b[0])} ${f1(b[1])}" style="fill:none;stroke:${HORMONE_INFO[kind].col};stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:2 4;opacity:${f1(lv*.55)}"/>`;
    const m=Math.max(1,Math.round(n*lv));
    for(let i=0;i<m;i++){const u=((i/m)+ph)%1,q=1-u,x=q*q*a[0]+2*q*u*c[0]+u*u*b[0],y=q*q*a[1]+2*q*u*c[1]+u*u*b[1];s+=hormoneDot(x,y,kind,{r,op:clamp(lv*1.4)*(u<.08?u/.08:u>.92?(1-u)/.08:1)})}
    return s};
  function draw(t){const N=vb(svg,'520 300','400 560'),p=phaseOf(HERO_PH,t),P=HERO_PH[p],V=heroLv(t),ph=RM?0:(t*14)%1;
    const L=N?{tx:12,ty:24,bx:20,by:50,bs:1.3,gx:6,gy:266,gs:.92,fx:212,fy:292,fw:176,fh:96,px:300,py:426,ps:.9,kx:214,ky:454,lx:12,ly:540,lw:376,r:5.5}
             :{tx:14,ty:24,bx:252,by:30,bs:1.0,gx:18,gy:62,gs:.74,fx:178,fy:190,fw:118,fh:60,px:338,py:222,ps:.62,kx:402,ky:206,lx:14,ly:276,lw:492,r:4.6};
    let s=`<text x="${L.tx}" y="${L.ty}" class="t-big" style="font-size:19px;fill:${p===4?'var(--accent)':p===5?'var(--tx)':'var(--brand)'}">${P.t}</text><text x="${L.tx}" y="${L.ty+15}" class="t-sm">${P.sub}</text>`;
    /* gut, fat tissue, brain */
    const G=gutTract(L.gx,L.gy,L.gs,{fill:V.fill,food:t>.15&&t<.5?ramp(t,.15,.5)*.42:null,glow:{stomach:V.ghr*.9,ileum:V.glp}});
    s+=G.svg;
    const F=adiposeTissue(L.fx,L.fy,L.fw,L.fh,{size:V.size,seed:4,frame:true,cell:N?30:24});
    s+=F.svg+kitLabel(L.fx+L.fw/2,L.fy+L.fh+13,'fat tissue',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(G.at.stomach[0]+6,G.at.stomach[1]-20,'stomach',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(G.at.ileum[0],G.at.ileum[1]+22,'gut',{a:'m'});
    const B=brainHypothalamus(L.bx,L.by,L.bs,{pomc:V.pomc,agrp:V.agrp,mc4r:V.mc4r,labels:true});
    s+=B.svg;
    const tgt=B.at.bloodIn;
    /* the signals */
    s+=stream(G.at.stomach,tgt,N?[60,-40]:[20,-70],'ghrelin',7,V.ghr,ph,L.r);
    s+=stream(G.at.ileum,tgt,N?[90,-10]:[40,-40],'glp1',6,V.glp,(ph+.33)%1,L.r);
    s+=stream([G.at.ileum[0]+10,G.at.ileum[1]+6],tgt,N?[110,10]:[60,-20],'pyy',5,V.glp*.85,(ph+.6)%1,L.r);
    s+=stream([L.fx+L.fw*.6,L.fy+4],tgt,N?[60,-30]:[40,-30],'leptin',6,V.lep,(ph+.15)%1,L.r);
    if(V.drug>0){const Pn=pen(L.px,L.py,L.ps,{needle:V.drug,press:ramp(t,.9,.96),op:V.drug});s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(V.drug)}">${Pn.svg}</g>`;
      s+=stream(Pn.at.back,tgt,N?[-70,-60]:[30,-50],'drug',5,V.drug,(ph+.45)%1,L.r)}
    /* legend */
    const keys=[['ghrelin','ghrelin (hunger)'],['glp1','GLP-1 (fullness)'],['pyy','PYY (fullness)'],['leptin','leptin (stores)'],['drug','GLP-1 medicine']];
    keys.forEach((k,i)=>{const x=L.kx,y=L.ky+i*(N?15:13);
      s+=hormoneDot(x+5,y,k[0],{r:4})+`<text x="${f1(x+15)}" y="${f1(y+3.5)}" class="t-xs">${k[1]}</text>`});
    /* phase strip */
    const sw=L.lw/HERO_PH.length;
    HERO_PH.forEach((q,i)=>{const on=i===p,x=L.lx+i*sw;s+=`<rect x="${f1(x+1)}" y="${L.ly-8}" width="${f1(sw-2)}" height="6" rx="3" style="fill:${on?'var(--brand)':'var(--panel-2)'}"/><text x="${f1(x+sw/2)}" y="${L.ly+12}" class="t-xs t-mid" style="${on?'fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700':''}">${q.k}</text>`});
    const mx=L.lx+L.lw*t;s+=`<circle cx="${f1(mx)}" cy="${L.ly-5}" r="5.5" style="fill:var(--ink);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`;
    svg.innerHTML=s;
    if(cap.textContent!==HERO_CAP)cap.textContent=HERO_CAP;
    rg.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',`${P.t}: ${P.sub}`)}
  playWire(rg,$('#heroPlay'),draw,24000,'Replay','home');draw(+rg.value);
};
/* =============== 1.1 What obesity is =============== */
/* Main player: a 10x10 grid of figures fills from the 1990 to the 2022 NCD-RisC estimate for the chosen group, and a
   bar counts the people living with obesity worldwide up past one billion, while a side panel tells the definition
   story step by step. Only the two survey endpoints exist in the source, so the fill between them is drawn as a
   transition with no year attached. Explorer: the Commission's clinical vs preclinical logic on two identical figures.
   Chart: US adult obesity from NHANES survey periods. */
const WH_GRP={
 women:{l:'women',lab:'adult women',p:[8.8,18.5],m:[127,504]},
 men:{l:'men',lab:'adult men',p:[4.8,14.0],m:[67,374]},
 girls:{l:'girls',lab:'girls aged 5–19',p:[1.7,6.9],m:[13.9,65.1]},
 boys:{l:'boys',lab:'boys aged 5–19',p:[2.1,9.3],m:[17.5,94.2]}};
/* NCD-RisC 2024: 2022 counts as published; 1990 counts derived by subtracting the reported increases <sup class="c" data-ref="NCDRisC2024" title="Source 384"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-NCDRisC2024">384</a></sup> */
const WH_TOT=[127+67+13.9+17.5,504+374+65.1+94.2];
const WH_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.03,k:'Step 1 · definition',t:'Excess adiposity',sub:'more body fat than is healthy, with many causes',
  txt:`The 2025 Lancet Diabetes &amp; Endocrinology Commission defines obesity as "a condition characterised by excess adiposity, with or without abnormal distribution or function of adipose tissue, and with causes that are multifactorial and still incompletely understood" <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>. Its 58 experts, who included people with lived experience of obesity, reached 90–100% agreement, and 76 organisations endorsed it <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`Obesity means carrying more body fat than is healthy for you. It is a long-term condition with many causes, including genes, biology, surroundings and life circumstances, not a failure of willpower <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission,Bray2017WOF" title="Source 53,480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">53,480</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`Commission 2025: obesity is excess adiposity, with or without abnormal distribution or function of fat tissue <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.2,at:.3,k:'Step 2 · BMI',t:'The BMI definition',sub:'weight in kg ÷ height in metres, squared',
  txt:`Body mass index is weight in kilograms divided by height in metres squared <sup class="c" data-ref="Keys1972,Eknoyan2008" title="Source 133,280"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Keys1972">133,280</a></sup>. The WHO adult classes are 25.0–29.9 pre-obese (overweight), 30.0–34.9 class I, 35.0–39.9 class II and 40.0 or more class III obesity <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2000TRS894,Flegal1998" title="Source 155,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2000TRS894">155,598</a></sup>. The Commission recommends BMI only as a surrogate for health risk at population level, for epidemiology or screening, not as an individual measure of health <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>. More in <a href="#measuring" data-go="measuring">BMI, waist &amp; body fat</a>.`,
  pt:`BMI is a quick screening number, but it cannot tell fat from muscle, so on its own it is not a diagnosis <sup class="c" data-ref="Okorodudu2010,Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 412,480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Okorodudu2010">412,480</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`WHO classes: 25–29.9 overweight, 30–34.9 class I, 35–39.9 class II, ≥40 class III <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2000TRS894,Flegal1998" title="Source 155,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2000TRS894">155,598</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.4,at:.5,k:'Step 3 · two states',t:'Clinical or preclinical',sub:'is excess fat already changing how the body works?',
  txt:`Clinical obesity is "a chronic, systemic illness characterised by alterations in the function of tissues, organs, the entire individual, or a combination thereof, due to excess adiposity". Preclinical obesity is excess adiposity with preserved function of other tissues and organs, and a varying but generally increased risk of clinical obesity and other non-communicable diseases <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>. The Commission set 18 criteria for adults and 13 for children and adolescents <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`Doctors now separate obesity that is already affecting how organs work or how someone manages daily life ("clinical obesity") from obesity that is not yet doing so ("preclinical obesity") <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`Clinical obesity = confirmed excess adiposity + organ dysfunction and/or limits on daily activities; 18 adult and 13 child criteria <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.6,at:.68,k:'Step 4 · chronic',t:'A chronic, relapsing disease',sub:'statements that frame obesity as a disease',
  txt:`In 2013 the American Medical Association recognised obesity as "a complex, chronic disease requiring medical attention" <sup class="c" data-ref="Kyle2016AMA" title="Source 305"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kyle2016AMA">305</a></sup>. AACE/ACE proposed "adiposity-based chronic disease" <sup class="c" data-ref="Mechanick2017ABCD,Garvey2016AACE" title="Source 180,362"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Mechanick2017ABCD">180,362</a></sup>, and the World Obesity Federation called obesity "a chronic relapsing progressive disease process" <sup class="c" data-ref="Bray2017WOF" title="Source 53"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Bray2017WOF">53</a></sup>. The Commission defines remission as resolution of organ dysfunction that "does not imply cure", and says public-health strategy should rest on evidence "rather than unproven assumptions that blame individual responsibility" <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`After weight loss, hunger hormones and appetite stay changed for at least a year. Weight coming back is the body defending its weight: biology, not weakness <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`WOF 2017: "a chronic relapsing progressive disease process" <sup class="c" data-ref="Bray2017WOF" title="Source 53"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Bray2017WOF">53</a></sup>; AMA disease recognition: 2013 <sup class="c" data-ref="Kyle2016AMA" title="Source 305"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kyle2016AMA">305</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.8,at:.93,k:'Step 5 · burden',t:'The global burden',sub:'more than a billion people; millions of deaths',
  txt:`Between 1990 and 2022, age-standardised adult obesity rose from 8.8% to 18.5% in women and from 4.8% to 14.0% in men. In 2022, 504 million women, 374 million men, 65.1 million girls and 94.2 million boys were living with obesity: over 1 billion people in all (sum of the four groups) <sup class="c" data-ref="NCDRisC2024" title="Source 384"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-NCDRisC2024">384</a></sup>. High BMI accounted for 4.0 million deaths in 2015 <sup class="c" data-ref="Afshin2017" title="Source 7"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Afshin2017">7</a></sup>, and the age-standardised disability-adjusted life-year rate it causes rose 15.7% from 2000 to 2021 <sup class="c" data-ref="GBD2021RiskFactors" title="Source 189"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-GBD2021RiskFactors">189</a></sup>. These are population statistics.`,
  pt:`Obesity has become much more common worldwide since 1990. More than 1 billion people now live with it, including children <sup class="c" data-ref="NCDRisC2024" title="Source 384"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-NCDRisC2024">384</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`2022: over 1 billion people with obesity, 878 million adults and 159 million aged 5–19 <sup class="c" data-ref="NCDRisC2024" title="Source 384"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-NCDRisC2024">384</a></sup>. High BMI: 4.0 million deaths in 2015, over two thirds cardiovascular <sup class="c" data-ref="Afshin2017" title="Source 7"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Afshin2017">7</a></sup>.`}];

/* the Commission's 18 adult criteria, short names from Table 2 <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>; p = where the point sits on the figure */
const WH_CRIT=[
 {g:'Brain & breathing',id:'icp',l:'Raised pressure inside the skull',p:'head'},
 {g:'Brain & breathing',id:'osa',l:'Sleep apnoeas or hypopnoeas',p:'neck'},
 {g:'Brain & breathing',id:'hypo',l:'Hypoventilation or breathlessness',p:'lungL'},
 {g:'Heart & circulation',id:'hfref',l:'Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction',p:'heart'},
 {g:'Heart & circulation',id:'hfpef',l:'Heart failure with preserved ejection fraction',p:'heart'},
 {g:'Heart & circulation',id:'af',l:'Chronic or recurrent atrial fibrillation',p:'heart'},
 {g:'Heart & circulation',id:'ph',l:'Pulmonary hypertension',p:'lungR'},
 {g:'Heart & circulation',id:'vte',l:'Recurrent deep-vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism',p:'calf'},
 {g:'Heart & circulation',id:'bp',l:'Raised blood pressure',p:'arm'},
 {g:'Metabolism, liver & kidney',id:'met',l:'High blood glucose with high triglycerides and low HDL',p:'belly'},
 {g:'Metabolism, liver & kidney',id:'liv',l:'Fatty liver disease with liver fibrosis',p:'liver'},
 {g:'Metabolism, liver & kidney',id:'kid',l:'Microalbuminuria with reduced kidney function',p:'kidney'},
 {g:'Pelvis & reproduction',id:'uri',l:'Recurrent or chronic urinary incontinence',p:'pelvis'},
 {g:'Pelvis & reproduction',id:'ov',l:'Anovulation, oligomenorrhoea or PCOS',p:'pelvis'},
 {g:'Pelvis & reproduction',id:'hg',l:'Male hypogonadism',p:'pelvis'},
 {g:'Joints, limbs & daily life',id:'jnt',l:'Chronic severe knee or hip pain with stiffness',p:'knee'},
 {g:'Joints, limbs & daily life',id:'lym',l:'Lower-limb lymphoedema',p:'ankle'},
 {g:'Joints, limbs & daily life',id:'adl',l:'Significant limitation of daily activities',p:'whole'}];
const WH_CONF={
 none:`BMI alone does not confirm excess adiposity unless it is above 40. The Commission asks for BMI plus one body measure, two body measures, or direct fat measurement, with cut-offs validated for age, sex and ethnicity <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
 bmi1:`BMI plus at least one anthropometric criterion (waist circumference, waist-to-hip or waist-to-height ratio) confirms excess adiposity <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
 two:`At least two anthropometric criteria confirm excess adiposity regardless of BMI <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
 dexa:`Direct body-fat measurement, such as DEXA or bioimpedance, confirms excess adiposity <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`,
 b40:`When BMI is above 40, excess adiposity "can pragmatically be assumed" without further confirmation <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`};

inits.what=()=>{
  const T=(x,y,s,c='t-xs',st='')=>`<text x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" class="${c}"${st?` style="${st}"`:''}>${s}</text>`;
  const wrap=(s,n)=>{const out=[];let c='';s.split(' ').forEach(w=>{if(c&&(c+' '+w).length>n){out.push(c);c=w}else c=c?c+' '+w:w});if(c)out.push(c);return out};
  const lines=(x,y,arr,lh,c,st)=>arr.map((l,i)=>T(x,y+i*lh,l,c,st)).join('');
  const INK='fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700';
  const fmtM=v=>v>=1000?(v/1000).toFixed(2).replace(/0$/,'')+' billion':Math.round(v)+' million';
  /* ---------- main player ---------- */
  const svg=$('#whSvg'),rg=$('#whT'),note=$('#whNote');let grp='women',setSt=()=>{};
  /* the side panel: one small scene per step; lp = progress through the step, 0..1 */
  function panel(p,lp,X,Y,W,H){let s=`<rect x="${X}" y="${Y}" width="${W}" height="${H}" rx="12" style="fill:var(--field);stroke:var(--line)"/>`;
    const cx=X+W/2,wn=Math.floor((W-32)/6.7);
    if(p===0){const A=adiposeTissue(X+16,Y+16,W-32,H*.4,{size:lerp(.3,.85,ease(lp)),seed:7,frame:true,cell:26});s+=A.svg;
      s+=T(cx,Y+H*.4+36,'fat cells enlarge as stores grow','t-sm t-mid');
      s+=lines(X+16,Y+H*.4+66,wrap('Obesity: excess adiposity, with or without abnormal distribution or function of fat tissue.',wn),16,'t-sm','fill:var(--ink)');
      s+=lines(X+16,Y+H*.4+66+16*wrap('Obesity: excess adiposity, with or without abnormal distribution or function of fat tissue.',wn).length+10,wrap('Causes: genetic, environmental, psychological, nutritional and metabolic; still incompletely understood.',wn),16,'t-sm')}
    else if(p===1){s+=T(cx,Y+36,'BMI = weight (kg) ÷ height (m)²','t-big t-mid');
      s+=T(cx,Y+56,'Quetelet 1832 · named BMI by Keys 1972','t-xs t-mid');
      const B=[15,18.5,25,30,35,40,45],bx=X+18,bw=W-36,by=Y+96,bxv=v=>bx+bw*(v-15)/30;
      const nm=['under-\nweight','','pre-\nobese','class I','class II','class III'];
      for(let i=0;i<6;i++){const x0=bxv(B[i]),x1=bxv(B[i+1]);s+=`<rect x="${f1(x0)}" y="${by}" width="${f1(x1-x0-1)}" height="22" rx="3" style="fill:var(--accent);opacity:${f1(.08+i*.08)}"/>`;
        nm[i].split('\n').forEach((q,j)=>{if(q)s+=T((x0+x1)/2,by+40+j*11,q,'t-xs t-mid')})}
      B.slice(1,6).forEach(v=>s+=T(bxv(v),by-6,v,'t-xs t-mid'));
      const v=lerp(21,42,ease(lp)),mx=bxv(v);s+=`<path d="M${f1(mx)} ${by-2}v26" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2.4"/><circle cx="${f1(mx)}" cy="${by+11}" r="5" style="fill:var(--ink);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`;
      s+=T(cx,by+86,`BMI ${f1(v)}`,'t-lbl t-mid');
      s+=lines(X+16,by+116,wrap('A surrogate for risk across populations, for surveillance and screening; not an individual measure of health.',wn),16,'t-sm','fill:var(--ink)')}
    else if(p===2){const fy=Y+40,fs=Math.min(210,H-100),ax=X+W*.27,bx2=X+W*.73;
      const A=person(ax,fy,fs,{size:.55}),B=person(bx2,fy,fs,{size:.55});s+=A.svg+B.svg;
      s+=T(ax,Y+24,'Preclinical','t-lbl t-mid')+T(bx2,Y+24,'Clinical','t-lbl t-mid');
      const k=fs/100,pts=[[4,33],[-4,40],[0,19],[5,77],[-4,47]];
      pts.forEach((q,i)=>{const a=ramp(lp,.15+i*.14,.27+i*.14);if(a<=0)return;const x=bx2+q[0]*k,y=fy+q[1]*k;
        s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(9*a)}" style="fill:var(--risk);opacity:.25"/><circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${f1(4*a)}" style="fill:var(--risk)"/>`});
      s+=lines(ax,fy+fs+20,['organs work normally;','risk is raised'],14,'t-sm t-mid')+lines(bx2,fy+fs+20,['organ function or','daily life affected'],14,'t-sm t-mid')}
    else if(p===3){const ev=[['2013','AMA','"a complex, chronic disease"'],['2016–17','AACE/ACE','"adiposity-based chronic disease"'],['2017','World Obesity Fed.','"chronic relapsing progressive"'],['2025','Lancet Commission','clinical vs preclinical obesity']];
      const lx=X+30,y0=Y+30,gap=(H-50)/4;s+=`<line x1="${lx}" x2="${lx}" y1="${y0}" y2="${f1(y0+gap*3+6)}" style="stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:3"/>`;
      ev.forEach((e,i)=>{const a=ramp(lp,i*.2,i*.2+.15),y=y0+i*gap;
        s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(.15+.85*a)}"><circle cx="${lx}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="7" style="fill:${a>=1?'var(--brand)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:2"/>`+T(lx+16,y+4,e[0]+' · '+e[1],'t-lbl')+T(lx+16,y+21,e[2],'t-sm')+'</g>'})}
    else{const bx=X+18,bw=W-36,a=ease(ramp(lp,0,.5)),b=ease(ramp(lp,.35,.85));
      s+=T(X+18,Y+30,'Deaths attributed to high BMI, 2015','t-lbl')+T(X+18,Y+56,'4.0 million','t-big','font-size:24px;fill:var(--hl)');
      const bar=(y,sh,lab1,lab2,al)=>{let q=`<rect x="${bx}" y="${y}" width="${bw}" height="20" rx="4" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/>`;
        q+=`<rect x="${bx}" y="${y}" width="${f1(bw*sh*al)}" height="20" rx="4" style="fill:var(--hl);opacity:.75"/>`;
        return q+T(bx,y+38,lab1,'t-sm','fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700')+T(bx,y+53,lab2,'t-sm')};
      s+=bar(Y+76,2/3,'more than two thirds:','from cardiovascular disease',a);
      s+=bar(Y+150,.4,'nearly 40%: in people whose BMI','was below the obesity threshold',b);
      const c3=ease(ramp(lp,.6,.95));
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(c3)}">`+T(X+18,Y+250,'+15.7%','t-big','font-size:22px;fill:var(--hl)')+lines(X+18,Y+270,['disability-adjusted life-year rate','from high BMI, 2000 to 2021'],15,'t-sm')+'</g>';
      s+=T(X+18,Y+H-14,'GBD modelled estimates; population statistics','t-xs')}
    return s}
  function draw(t){const N=vb(svg,'720 380','400 690'),p=phaseOf(WH_STEPS,t),P=WH_STEPS[p],G=WH_GRP[grp];
    const L=N?{tx:12,ty:22,gx:14,gy:62,sx:222,sy:78,trx:14,trw:372,try:312,tby:352,px:10,py:396,pw:380,ph:286,sz:16}
             :{tx:16,ty:24,gx:18,gy:66,sx:226,sy:84,trx:18,trw:370,try:300,tby:338,px:406,py:20,pw:300,ph:344,sz:15};
    const u=ease(ramp(t,.04,.8)),pct=lerp(G.p[0],G.p[1],u),k=Math.round(pct),mil=lerp(G.m[0],G.m[1],u),tot=lerp(WH_TOT[0],WH_TOT[1],u);
    const ylab=u<=0?'1990':u>=1?'2022':'1990 → 2022';
    let s=T(L.tx,L.ty,P.t,'t-big')+T(L.tx,L.ty+16,P.sub,'t-sm');
    /* the grid of 100 */
    const IA=iconArray(L.gx,L.gy,{n:100,cols:10,k,size:L.sz,gap:4,col:'var(--accent)',base:'var(--line)'});s+=IA.svg;
    /* readout */
    s+=T(L.sx,L.sy,ylab,'t-sm',INK)+T(L.sx,L.sy+34,f1(pct)+'%','t-big','font-size:30px;fill:var(--accent)');
    s+=lines(L.sx,L.sy+56,[`of ${G.lab}`,'living with obesity'],15,'t-sm','fill:var(--ink)');
    s+=T(L.sx,L.sy+104,fmtM(mil),'t-lbl')+T(L.sx,L.sy+120,'people in this group','t-sm');
    s+=T(L.sx,L.sy+148,`1990: ${f1(G.p[0])}%`,'t-sm')+T(L.sx,L.sy+164,`2022: ${f1(G.p[1])}%`,'t-sm');
    s+=T(L.sx,L.sy+190,'1 figure = 1 in 100','t-xs');
    /* endpoint track */
    const tx0=L.trx,tx1=L.trx+L.trw,mx=lerp(tx0,tx1,u);
    s+=`<line x1="${tx0}" x2="${tx1}" y1="${L.try}" y2="${L.try}" style="stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:4;stroke-linecap:round"/><line x1="${tx0}" x2="${f1(mx)}" y1="${L.try}" y2="${L.try}" style="stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:4;stroke-linecap:round"/>`;
    s+=T(tx0,L.try-9,'1990','t-sm')+T(tx1,L.try-9,'2022','t-sm t-end')+`<circle cx="${f1(mx)}" cy="${L.try}" r="5.5" style="fill:var(--accent);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`;
    /* the billion bar: all four groups together */
    const bw=L.trw,bmax=1100,bX=v=>L.trx+bw*v/bmax,by=L.tby;
    s+=`<rect x="${L.trx}" y="${by}" width="${bw}" height="14" rx="7" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${L.trx}" y="${by}" width="${f1(bX(tot)-L.trx)}" height="14" rx="7" style="fill:var(--brand)"/>`;
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(bX(1000))}" x2="${f1(bX(1000))}" y1="${by-6}" y2="${by+20}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:3 2"/>`;
    s+=T(bX(1000),by+32,'1 billion','t-sm t-mid',tot>=1000?INK:'');
    s+=T(L.trx,by+32,`Everyone with obesity: ${fmtM(tot)}`,'t-sm',tot>=1000?'fill:var(--brand);font-weight:700':'fill:var(--ink)');
    s+=panel(p,ramp(t,P.from,(WH_STEPS[p+1]||{from:1}).from),L.px,L.py,L.pw,L.ph);
    svg.innerHTML=s;setSt(p);note.innerHTML=noteHTML(P)}
  const stop=playWire(rg,$('#whPlay'),draw,22000,'Replay','what');
  setSt=stepWire($('#whSteps'),WH_STEPS,rg,draw,stop);
  $$('[data-whg]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{grp=b.dataset.whg;$$('[data-whg]').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',x===b));draw(+rg.value)}));
  draw(+rg.value);

  /* ---------- clinical vs preclinical explorer ---------- */
  const ex=$('#whEx'),out=$('#whOut'),conf=$('#whConf'),crit=$('#whCrit');
  const groups=[...new Set(WH_CRIT.map(c=>c.g))];
  crit.innerHTML=groups.map(g=>`<fieldset><legend>${g}</legend>${WH_CRIT.filter(c=>c.g===g).map(c=>`<label><input type="checkbox" data-whc="${c.id}"><span>${c.l}</span></label>`).join('')}</fieldset>`).join('');
  const POS={head:[0,9],neck:[0,19],lungL:[-6,30],lungR:[6,30],heart:[4,34],arm:[-17,46],belly:[0,47],liver:[-5,41],kidney:[5,48],pelvis:[0,57],knee:[-5,77],calf:[5,87],ankle:[-5,94]};
  function exDraw(){const N=vb(ex,'600 330','400 380');const on=WH_CRIT.filter(c=>$(`[data-whc="${c.id}"]`).checked),cv=conf.value,ok=cv!=='none';
    const cls=!ok?0:on.length?2:1;
    const L=N?{w:194,h:360,x0:6,y0:10,fs:250,fy:58,gap:0}:{w:292,h:310,x0:6,y0:10,fs:236,fy:52,gap:10};
    let s='';
    [['Preclinical obesity','organs and daily life unaffected',1],['Clinical obesity','organ dysfunction or limits on daily life',2]].forEach(([h,sub,c],i)=>{
      const x=L.x0+i*(L.w+L.gap),cx=x+L.w/2,sel=cls===c;
      s+=`<rect x="${x}" y="${L.y0}" width="${L.w-4}" height="${L.h}" rx="14" style="fill:${sel?'var(--brand-soft)':'var(--field)'};stroke:${sel?'var(--brand)':'var(--line)'};stroke-width:${sel?2.6:1}"/>`;
      s+=T(cx,L.y0+24,h,'t-lbl t-mid',sel?'fill:var(--brand)':'')+T(cx,L.y0+40,N?(c===1?'organs unaffected':'organs or daily life affected'):sub,'t-xs t-mid');
      const P=person(cx,L.fy,L.fs,{size:.55,op:ok?1:.5});s+=P.svg;
      if(c===2){const k=L.fs/100;
        if(on.some(q=>q.p==='whole'))s+=`<ellipse cx="${f1(cx)}" cy="${f1(L.fy+L.fs*.53)}" rx="${f1(L.fs*.3)}" ry="${f1(L.fs*.49)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--risk);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/>`;
        const seen={};on.filter(q=>q.p!=='whole').forEach(q=>{const b=POS[q.p],n=seen[q.p]=(seen[q.p]||0)+1,x2=cx+b[0]*k+(n-1)*7,y2=L.fy+b[1]*k;
          s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x2)}" cy="${f1(y2)}" r="9" style="fill:var(--risk);opacity:.22"/><circle cx="${f1(x2)}" cy="${f1(y2)}" r="4.2" style="fill:var(--risk);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1.2"/>`})}
      if(sel)s+=T(cx,L.y0+L.h-12,'matches the choices','t-xs t-mid',INK)});
    if(!ok)s+=T(N?200:300,N?372:326,'excess adiposity not confirmed: neither category applies yet','t-xs t-mid',INK);
    ex.innerHTML=s;
    let h=`<div class="kicker">Commission framework, as a teaching tool</div>`;
    if(!cls)h+=`<p class="verdict none">Not classed as obesity yet</p><p>${WH_CONF.none}</p>`+(on.length?`<p>The problems ticked still deserve care in their own right; the framework only counts them as clinical obesity when excess adiposity is confirmed and is their cause <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.</p>`:'');
    else if(cls===1)h+=`<p class="verdict">Preclinical obesity</p><p>${WH_CONF[cv]}</p><p>With no organ dysfunction and no limits on daily activities, the framework calls this preclinical obesity: preserved function, with a varying but generally increased risk of clinical obesity, type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, some cancers and mental disorders <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.</p>`;
    else h+=`<p class="verdict">Clinical obesity</p><p>${WH_CONF[cv]}</p><p>Confirmed excess adiposity plus ${on.length===1?'one criterion':on.length+' criteria'} (reduced organ or tissue function due to obesity, or substantial limits on daily activities) meets the definition of clinical obesity <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>. Ticked: ${on.map(c=>c.l.toLowerCase()).join('; ')}.</p>`;
    h+=`<div class="pt"><b>In plain words</b>The label is about how the body is working, not about size. Two people with the same BMI can be in different categories.</div>`;
    h+=`<div class="hook"><b>Exam hook</b>Confirm adiposity first (BMI + 1 body measure, 2 body measures, or direct fat measurement; assumed above BMI 40), then look for organ dysfunction <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.</div>`;
    out.innerHTML=h}
  conf.addEventListener('change',exDraw);crit.addEventListener('change',exDraw);
  exDraw();
  redraws.what=(()=>{const prev=redraws.what;return()=>{prev&&prev();exDraw();usDraw()}})();

  /* ---------- US adults chart ---------- */
  const us=$('#whUs');
  const US_A=[[1961,12.8],[1973,14.1],[1978,14.5],[1991,22.5]];           /* ages 20-74 <sup class="c" data-ref="Flegal1998" title="Source 155"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Flegal1998">155</a></sup> */
  const US_B=[[1991,22.9],[2000,30.5],[2008,33.8],[2012,34.9],[2014,37.7],[2022,40.3]]; /* ages 20+ */
  const US_S=[[1991,2.9],[2000,4.7],[2014,7.7],[2022,9.7]];                /* BMI >=40, age-adjusted */
  function usDraw(){const N=vb(us,'720 300','400 340');
    const A=N?{x:44,y:24,w:330,h:250}:{x:56,y:22,w:620,h:236};
    const C=curveAxes(A.x,A.y,A.w,A.h,{x0:1955,x1:2033,y0:0,y1:52,xt:N?[1960,1980,2000,2020]:[1960,1970,1980,1990,2000,2010,2020,2030],yt:[0,10,20,30,40,50],yfmt:v=>v+'%'});
    let s=C.svg;
    s+=plotLine(US_A,C.X,C.Y,{col:'var(--brand)',lw:2.4,dash:'5 3'}).svg+plotLine(US_B,C.X,C.Y,{col:'var(--brand)',lw:2.8}).svg+plotLine(US_S,C.X,C.Y,{col:'var(--accent)',lw:2.6}).svg;
    s+=`<path d="M${f1(C.X(2022))} ${f1(C.Y(40.3))}L${f1(C.X(2030))} ${f1(C.Y(48.9))}" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:3 4;fill:none"/><circle cx="${f1(C.X(2030))}" cy="${f1(C.Y(48.9))}" r="4.5" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:2"/>`;
    [...US_A,...US_B].forEach(q=>s+=`<circle cx="${f1(C.X(q[0]))}" cy="${f1(C.Y(q[1]))}" r="3.4" style="fill:var(--brand);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1.4"/>`);
    US_S.forEach(q=>s+=`<circle cx="${f1(C.X(q[0]))}" cy="${f1(C.Y(q[1]))}" r="3.2" style="fill:var(--accent);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1.4"/>`);
    s+=T(C.X(1961)+4,C.Y(12.8)-10,'12.8%','t-xs');
    s+=T(C.X(1991)-6,C.Y(22.5)-10,'22.5%','t-xs t-end');
    s+=T(C.X(2022)-6,C.Y(40.3)-10,'40.3%','t-xs t-end',INK);
    s+=T(C.X(2030),C.Y(48.9)-12,'48.9% projected','t-xs t-mid');
    s+=T(C.X(2022)-6,C.Y(9.7)-10,'9.7%','t-xs t-end','fill:var(--accent);font-weight:700');
    s+=T(A.x+8,A.y+14,'% of US adults','t-xs');
    us.innerHTML=s}
  usDraw();
};
/* =============== 1.2 BMI, waist & body fat =============== */
/* Main player: the height x weight plane shaded by the WHO BMI classes (curves w = BMI x h^2), with an optional
   overlay of the WHO 2004 Asian action points. An imaginary adult's point moves through the classes while a side
   panel works the formula, lists the classes, shows what BMI >=30 misses (Okorodudu2010) and the ethnicity
   equivalents (Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity), the waist-to-height ratio and the Commission's confirmation rules.
   Calculator: BMI and waist-to-height for an imaginary adult, read against published cut-offs, with no advice. */
const MS_CLASSES=[ /* WHO adult classes <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2000TRS894,Flegal1998" title="Source 155,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2000TRS894">155,598</a></sup>; underweight below 18.5 <sup class="c" data-ref="NCDRisC2016" title="Source 382"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-NCDRisC2016">382</a></sup> */
 {lo:0,hi:18.5,n:'underweight',r:'below 18.5'},
 {lo:18.5,hi:25,n:'18.5 to 24.9',r:'18.5–24.9'},
 {lo:25,hi:30,n:'pre-obese, or overweight',r:'25.0–29.9'},
 {lo:30,hi:35,n:'obesity class I',r:'30.0–34.9'},
 {lo:35,hi:40,n:'obesity class II',r:'35.0–39.9'},
 {lo:40,hi:99,n:'obesity class III',r:'40.0 or more'}];
const MS_ASIAN=[23,27.5,32.5,37.5];                     /* <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2004Asian" title="Source 599"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2004Asian">599</a></sup> */
const MS_ETH=[['White',30.0],['Black',28.1],['Chinese',26.9],['Arab',26.6],['South Asian',23.9]]; /* <sup class="c" data-ref="Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity" title="Source 60"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity">60</a></sup> */
const MS_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.08,k:'Step 1 · the formula',t:"Quetelet's formula",sub:'weight in kg divided by height in metres, squared',
  txt:`BMI is weight in kilograms divided by height in metres squared <sup class="c" data-ref="Keys1972,Eknoyan2008" title="Source 133,280"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Keys1972">133,280</a></sup>. In 1832 Adolphe Quetelet concluded from growth studies that, outside the growth spurts of infancy and puberty, "the weight increases as the square of the height" <sup class="c" data-ref="Eknoyan2008" title="Source 133"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Eknoyan2008">133</a></sup>. In 1972 Ancel Keys and colleagues compared indices in 7,424 healthy men in 12 cohorts and named weight/height² the "body mass index": it correlated little with height and well with body fat <sup class="c" data-ref="Keys1972,Eknoyan2008" title="Source 133,280"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Keys1972">133,280</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`BMI is your weight divided by your height squared. It is a quick screening number, but it cannot tell fat from muscle, so on its own it is not a diagnosis <sup class="c" data-ref="Okorodudu2010,Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 412,480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Okorodudu2010">412,480</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`BMI = kg/m². Quetelet described the index in 1832; Keys named it in 1972 <sup class="c" data-ref="Eknoyan2008,Keys1972" title="Source 133,280"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Eknoyan2008">133,280</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.2,at:.36,k:'Step 2 · the classes',t:'The WHO classes',sub:'bands for comparing populations',
  txt:`The WHO classification used in international surveillance runs: pre-obese (overweight) 25.0–29.9, class I obesity 30.0–34.9, class II 35.0–39.9 and class III 40.0 or more <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2000TRS894,Flegal1998" title="Source 155,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2000TRS894">155,598</a></sup>; NCD-RisC adds underweight below 18.5 <sup class="c" data-ref="NCDRisC2016" title="Source 382"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-NCDRisC2016">382</a></sup>. The bands came from WHO's first obesity consultation (1997) and its 2000 report <sup class="c" data-ref="James2008WHO,WHO2000TRS894" title="Source 250,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-James2008WHO">250,598</a></sup>. Across 239 cohorts of never-smokers, all-cause mortality was lowest at BMI 20–25, with a hazard ratio of 1.45 at 30–35 and 2.76 at 40–60: group averages, not predictions for one person <sup class="c" data-ref="GBMC2016" title="Source 190"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-GBMC2016">190</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`The classes are bands for comparing large groups of people. They describe groups, not how healthy one person is.`,
  hook:`25–29.9 overweight · 30–34.9 class I · 35–39.9 class II · ≥40 class III <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2000TRS894,Flegal1998" title="Source 155,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2000TRS894">155,598</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.42,at:.56,k:'Step 3 · blind spots',t:'Why BMI misclassifies',sub:'muscle, age, sex and ethnicity',
  txt:`Across 32 samples (31,968 people), BMI ≥30 had a sensitivity of 0.42 and a specificity of 0.97 for excess body fat; the authors conclude that BMI "fail[s] to identify half of the people with excess BF%" <sup class="c" data-ref="Okorodudu2010" title="Source 412"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Okorodudu2010">412</a></sup>. BMI does worst in the 25–29.9 range, in men and in older adults <sup class="c" data-ref="RomeroCorral2008" title="Source 469"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-RomeroCorral2008">469</a></sup>. Risk also starts at lower BMI in some groups: the BMI matching the diabetes risk of 30 in White adults was 23.9 in south Asian, 26.6 in Arab, 26.9 in Chinese and 28.1 in Black adults in England <sup class="c" data-ref="Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity" title="Source 60"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity">60</a></sup>, and WHO added action points at 23, 27.5, 32.5 and 37.5 for Asian populations <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2004Asian" title="Source 599"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2004Asian">599</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`Health risks can start at a lower BMI in people of south Asian, Chinese, Arab or Black background, so some services use lower cut-off points <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2004Asian,Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity" title="Source 60,599"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2004Asian">60,599</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`BMI ≥30 is specific (0.97) but insensitive (0.42) for excess body fat <sup class="c" data-ref="Okorodudu2010" title="Source 412"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Okorodudu2010">412</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.62,at:.74,k:'Step 4 · the waist',t:'Waist and waist-to-height',sub:'where the fat sits adds information',
  txt:`The IAS/ICCR consensus calls waist circumference a "vital sign" that gives "both independent and additive information to BMI" <sup class="c" data-ref="Ross2020IASICCR" title="Source 474"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Ross2020IASICCR">474</a></sup>. In EPIC, the highest waist fifth carried a relative risk of death of 2.05 in men and 1.78 in women after adjusting for BMI <sup class="c" data-ref="Pischon2008EPIC" title="Source 429"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Pischon2008EPIC">429</a></sup>. Waist-to-height ratio discriminated cardiometabolic outcomes slightly better than waist or BMI (mean AUC 0.704, 0.693, 0.671), with a proposed boundary of 0.5 <sup class="c" data-ref="Browning2010,Ashwell2012" title="Source 30,55"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Browning2010">30,55</a></sup>. A fixed cut-off over-classifies shorter adults <sup class="c" data-ref="Nevill2023" title="Source 399"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Nevill2023">399</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`A simple guide some services use is that a waist under half your height is a lower-risk range. It is rough, and may be less fair to shorter people <sup class="c" data-ref="Browning2010,Nevill2023" title="Source 55,399"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Browning2010">55,399</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`WHtR boundary 0.5 <sup class="c" data-ref="Browning2010,Ashwell2012" title="Source 30,55"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Browning2010">30,55</a></sup>; waist action levels 94/80 and 102/88 cm, men/women <sup class="c" data-ref="Lean1995" title="Source 312"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Lean1995">312</a></sup>.`},
 {from:.8,at:.9,k:'Step 5 · confirm',t:'Confirm with a second measure',sub:'the Lancet Commission, 2025',
  txt:`To confirm excess adiposity the Commission requires one of: direct body-fat measurement (DEXA, bioimpedance and others); BMI plus at least one of waist, waist-to-hip or waist-to-height; or at least two of those body measures whatever the BMI, with cut-offs validated for age, sex and ethnicity (agreement 98%). Above BMI 40, excess adiposity "can pragmatically be assumed" <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>. In pooled cohorts, 5% of people with a normal BMI had a high waist, and 9% of people with obesity a low one <sup class="c" data-ref="Dardari2026" title="Source 111"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Dardari2026">111</a></sup>.`,
  pt:`Many health experts now say a waist measurement should be checked as well as BMI, because fat around the middle carries extra risk <sup class="c" data-ref="Ross2020IASICCR,Pischon2008EPIC" title="Source 429,474"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Ross2020IASICCR">429,474</a></sup>.`,
  hook:`Commission: BMI + 1 body measure, 2 body measures, or direct fat measurement; assumed above BMI 40 <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.`}];
/* the imaginary adult: height fixed, weight keyframes [t, kg] */
const MS_H=1.72;
const MS_KF=[[0,70],[.2,70],[.24,50],[.4,132],[.46,85],[.84,85],[.95,124],[1,124]];

inits.measuring=()=>{
  const T=(x,y,s,c='t-xs',st='')=>`<text x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" class="${c}"${st?` style="${st}"`:''}>${s}</text>`;
  const INK='fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700';
  const wrap=(s,n)=>{const out=[];let c='';s.split(' ').forEach(w=>{if(c&&(c+' '+w).length>n){out.push(c);c=w}else c=c?c+' '+w:w});if(c)out.push(c);return out};
  const lines=(x,y,arr,lh,c,st)=>arr.map((l,i)=>T(x,y+i*lh,l,c,st)).join('');
  const clsOf=b=>MS_CLASSES.find(c=>b<c.hi)||MS_CLASSES[5];
  const kgAt=t=>{for(let i=1;i<MS_KF.length;i++){const a=MS_KF[i-1],b=MS_KF[i];if(t<=b[0])return lerp(a[1],b[1],ease(ramp(t,a[0],b[0])))}return MS_KF[MS_KF.length-1][1]};
  const svg=$('#msSvg'),rg=$('#msT'),note=$('#msNote'),asb=$('#msAsian');let asian=false,setSt=()=>{};
  function chart(L,kg,p){const h0=1.45,h1=2.0,w0=40,w1=150,X=h=>L.cx+L.cw*(h-h0)/(h1-h0),Y=w=>L.cy+L.ch-L.ch*(w-w0)/(w1-w0);
    const cid=kid('msclip');let s=`<defs><clipPath id="${cid}"><rect x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy}" width="${L.cw}" height="${L.ch}"/></clipPath></defs>`;
    s+=`<rect x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy}" width="${L.cw}" height="${L.ch}" style="fill:var(--field)"/><g clip-path="url(#${cid})">`;
    const curve=(B,rev)=>{const P=[];for(let i=0;i<=24;i++){const h=lerp(h0,h1,i/24);P.push([X(h),Y(B*h*h)])}return rev?P.reverse():P};
    const bmiNow=kg/(MS_H*MS_H),cur=clsOf(bmiNow);
    MS_CLASSES.forEach((c,i)=>{const P=[...curve(Math.max(c.lo,8)),...curve(Math.min(c.hi,80),true)];
      s+=`<path d="${ptsD(P)}Z" style="fill:var(--accent);opacity:${f1(.05+i*.075+(c===cur&&p<2?.08:0))}"/>`});
    [18.5,25,30,35,40].forEach(B=>s+=`<path d="${ptsD(curve(B))}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.2;opacity:.7"/>`);
    if(asian)MS_ASIAN.forEach(B=>s+=`<path d="${ptsD(curve(B))}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--tx);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/>`);
    s+='</g>';
    /* axes */
    [1.5,1.6,1.7,1.8,1.9,2.0].forEach(h=>s+=`<line x1="${f1(X(h))}" x2="${f1(X(h))}" y1="${L.cy+L.ch}" y2="${L.cy+L.ch+4}" class="axis"/>`+T(X(h),L.cy+L.ch+16,h.toFixed(1),'t-xs t-mid'));
    [40,60,80,100,120,140].forEach(w=>s+=T(L.cx-6,Y(w)+3.5,w,'t-xs t-end'));
    s+=`<line x1="${L.cx}" x2="${L.cx+L.cw}" y1="${L.cy+L.ch}" y2="${L.cy+L.ch}" class="axis"/><line x1="${L.cx}" x2="${L.cx}" y1="${L.cy}" y2="${L.cy+L.ch}" class="axis"/>`;
    s+=T(L.cx+L.cw,L.cy+L.ch+30,'height (m)','t-xs t-end')+T(L.cx,L.cy-8,'weight (kg)','t-xs');
    /* curve labels where each line leaves the plot */
    [18.5,25,30,35,40].forEach(B=>{const hT=Math.sqrt(w1/B);const top=hT<h1;const hx=top?hT:h1,wy=top?w1:B*h1*h1;
      s+=T(top?X(hx):X(hx)+3,top?Y(wy)-3:Y(wy)+3.5,B,top?'t-xs t-mid':'t-xs','fill:var(--accent);font-weight:700')});
    if(asian)MS_ASIAN.forEach(B=>{const hT=Math.sqrt(w1/B),top=hT<h1;s+=T(top?X(hT):X(h1)+3,top?Y(w1)-3:Y(B*h1*h1)+3.5,B,top?'t-xs t-mid':'t-xs','fill:var(--tx);font-weight:700')});
    /* class names inside the bands, at h = 1.6 (underweight further right) */
    [[0,1.9,16.2],[1,1.88,21.75],[2,1.88,27.5],[3,1.88,32.5],[4,1.88,37.5],[5,1.6,50]].forEach(([i,h,mid])=>{const c=MS_CLASSES[i];
      s+=T(X(h),Y(mid*h*h)+3.5,['underweight','18.5–24.9','pre-obese','class I','class II','class III'][i],'t-sm t-mid',c===cur?INK:'fill:var(--ink);opacity:.75')});
    /* the point */
    const px=X(MS_H),py=Y(kg);
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(px)}" x2="${f1(px)}" y1="${f1(py)}" y2="${L.cy+L.ch}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/><line x1="${L.cx}" x2="${f1(px)}" y1="${f1(py)}" y2="${f1(py)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/>`;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(px)}" cy="${f1(py)}" r="7" style="fill:var(--ink);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2.4"/>`;
    s+=kitLabel(px+12,py-10,`BMI ${f1(bmiNow)}`,{});
    s+=T(L.cx,L.cy+L.ch+46,`${MS_H.toFixed(2)} m · ${Math.round(kg)} kg → BMI ${f1(bmiNow)} · ${cur.n}`,'t-sm',INK);
    if(asian)s+=T(L.cx+L.cw,L.cy+L.ch+46,'dashed: WHO 2004 action points','t-xs t-end','fill:var(--tx)');
    return s}
  function panel(p,lp,kg,X0,Y0,W,H){let s=`<rect x="${X0}" y="${Y0}" width="${W}" height="${H}" rx="12" style="fill:var(--field);stroke:var(--line)"/>`;const x=X0+16,wn=W>320?50:42;
    const bmi=kg/(MS_H*MS_H);
    if(p===0){const a=[ramp(lp,0,.2),ramp(lp,.2,.4),ramp(lp,.4,.6)];
      s+=T(x,Y0+28,'BMI = weight ÷ height²','t-big');
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(a[0])}">`+T(x,Y0+58,`= ${Math.round(kg)} ÷ (${MS_H.toFixed(2)} × ${MS_H.toFixed(2)})`,'t-lbl')+'</g>';
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(a[1])}">`+T(x,Y0+82,`= ${Math.round(kg)} ÷ ${(MS_H*MS_H).toFixed(2)}`,'t-lbl')+'</g>';
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(a[2])}">`+T(x,Y0+110,`= ${f1(bmi)} kg/m²`,'t-big','fill:var(--brand);font-size:22px')+'</g>';
      const H2=[['1832','Quetelet: weight rises as the square of height'],['1972','Keys names it the "body mass index"'],['1985','Garrow: r ≈ 0.95 with measured fat mass/height²']];
      H2.forEach((e,i)=>{const op=ramp(lp,.55+i*.12,.65+i*.12),y=Y0+150+i*44;
        s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(.2+.8*op)}">`+T(x,y,e[0],'t-lbl','fill:var(--brand)')+lines(x+44,y,wrap(e[1],W>320?36:30),14,'t-sm','fill:var(--ink)')+'</g>'})}
    else if(p===1){const cur=clsOf(bmi);s+=T(x,Y0+26,'WHO adult classes (kg/m²)','t-lbl');
      MS_CLASSES.forEach((c,i)=>{const y=Y0+48+i*36,on=c===cur;
        s+=`<rect x="${x-6}" y="${y-4}" width="${W-20}" height="30" rx="7" style="fill:${on?'var(--accent-soft)':'transparent'};stroke:${on?'var(--accent)':'none'};stroke-width:1.6"/>`;
        s+=T(x+4,y+15,c.r,'t-sm',on?INK:'fill:var(--ink)')+T(x+(W>320?110:100),y+15,c.n,'t-sm',on?INK:'')});
      s+=T(x,Y0+H-14,asian?'Asian action points: 23 · 27.5 · 32.5 · 37.5':'Toggle the Asian action points below the chart','t-xs',asian?'fill:var(--tx);font-weight:700':'')}
    else if(p===2){const k=Math.round(42*ease(ramp(lp,0,.4)));
      s+=lines(x,Y0+24,['100 adults with excess body fat,','measured directly'],13,'t-xs',INK);
      const IA=iconArray(x,Y0+44,{n:100,cols:10,k,size:9,gap:3.4,col:'var(--accent)',base:'var(--line)'});s+=IA.svg;
      const cx2=x+IA.w+14;
      s+=T(cx2,Y0+70,`${k}`,'t-big','font-size:24px;fill:var(--accent)')+T(cx2,Y0+86,'flagged by BMI ≥30','t-xs',INK);
      s+=T(cx2,Y0+122,`${100-k}`,'t-big','font-size:24px')+T(cx2,Y0+138,'missed','t-xs',INK);
      const ey=Y0+44+IA.h+26,ax0=x+78,aw=W-(ax0-X0)-22,sc=v=>ax0+aw*(v-22)/10;
      s+=lines(x,ey,['BMI with the type 2 diabetes risk','of BMI 30 in White adults (England)'],13,'t-xs',INK);
      [24,26,28,30,32].forEach(v=>s+=`<line x1="${f1(sc(v))}" x2="${f1(sc(v))}" y1="${ey+20}" y2="${ey+20+5*21}" style="stroke:var(--line);stroke-dasharray:2 3"/>`+T(sc(v),ey+20+5*21+12,v,'t-xs t-mid'));
      MS_ETH.forEach((e,i)=>{const a=ramp(lp,.2+i*.08,.3+i*.08),y=ey+32+i*21,vx=sc(lerp(30,e[1],ease(a)));
        s+=T(x,y+3.5,e[0],'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')+`<line x1="${f1(sc(30))}" x2="${f1(vx)}" y1="${y}" y2="${y}" style="stroke:var(--tx);stroke-width:2"/><circle cx="${f1(vx)}" cy="${y}" r="4.5" style="fill:var(--tx)"/>`+(a>.95?T(vx-8,y+3.5,f1(e[1]),'t-xs t-end',INK):'')});
      }
    else if(p===3){const cmW=lerp(70,100,ease(lp)),ratio=cmW/(MS_H*100),fx=X0+W*.24,fs=Math.min(230,H-70),fy=Y0+26;
      const P=person(fx,fy,fs,{size:.5});s+=P.svg;const k=fs/100,wy=fy+50*k,half=(12+5*.5)*k,axx=X0+12;
      s+=`<ellipse cx="${f1(fx)}" cy="${f1(wy)}" rx="${f1(half)}" ry="${f1(3.5*k)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--tx);stroke-width:2.6"/>`;
      s+=`<path d="M${f1(axx)} ${fy}V${f1(fy+fs)}" style="stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.2" marker-start="url(#msAr)" marker-end="url(#msAr)"/>`;
      s+=T(axx+4,fy+fs+18,`height ${Math.round(MS_H*100)} cm`,'t-xs',INK);
      const rx=X0+W*.5,rw=W*.46;
      s+=T(rx,Y0+40,'waist','t-sm')+T(rx,Y0+62,`${Math.round(cmW)} cm`,'t-big','fill:var(--tx)');
      s+=T(rx,Y0+96,'waist ÷ height','t-sm')+T(rx,Y0+124,ratio.toFixed(2),'t-big','font-size:28px;fill:'+(ratio>=.5?'var(--tx)':'var(--ink)'));
      const sx=v=>rx+rw*(v-.35)/.35,by=Y0+142;
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(rx)}" y="${by}" width="${f1(rw)}" height="10" rx="5" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${f1(rx)}" y="${by}" width="${f1(sx(clamp(ratio,.35,.7))-rx)}" height="10" rx="5" style="fill:var(--tx);opacity:.7"/>`;
      s+=`<line x1="${f1(sx(.5))}" x2="${f1(sx(.5))}" y1="${by-6}" y2="${by+16}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2"/>`+T(sx(.5),by+30,'0.5 boundary','t-xs t-mid',INK);
      s+=lines(rx,by+62,['Waist action levels','(Lean 1995):','men 94 and 102 cm','women 80 and 88 cm'],15,'t-sm','fill:var(--ink)');
      s+=lines(rx,by+136,['EPIC: top waist fifth,','death RR 2.05 men,','1.78 women, after BMI'],14,'t-xs');
      s+=`<defs><marker id="msAr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" style="fill:var(--muted)"/></marker></defs>`}
    else{const bmiNow=bmi,assumed=bmiNow>40,bw=W-32;
      const box=(y,h,txt,on,col='var(--tx)')=>`<rect x="${x}" y="${y}" width="${bw}" height="${h}" rx="9" style="fill:${on?'var(--tx-soft)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:${on?col:'var(--line)'};stroke-width:${on?2:1}"/>`+lines(x+10,y+17,txt,13,'t-xs',on?INK:'fill:var(--ink)');
      const a=i=>ramp(lp,i*.12,i*.12+.1)>.5;
      s+=T(x,Y0+24,'Confirm excess adiposity with one of:','t-lbl');
      s+=box(Y0+36,40,wrap('BMI plus waist, waist-to-hip or waist-to-height',W>320?46:40),a(1));
      s+=box(Y0+82,40,wrap('two of those body measures, whatever the BMI',W>320?46:40),a(2));
      s+=box(Y0+128,40,wrap('direct fat measurement: DEXA, bioimpedance',W>320?46:40),a(3));
      s+=box(Y0+184,40,wrap(`BMI above 40: "can pragmatically be assumed"`,W>320?46:40),assumed,'var(--accent)');
      s+=T(x,Y0+246,`now: BMI ${f1(bmiNow)}${assumed?' · above 40':''}`,'t-sm',INK);
      s+=lines(x,Y0+268,wrap('Cut-offs validated for age, sex and ethnicity. Then: is organ function or daily life affected?',W>320?50:44),13,'t-xs')}
    return s}
  function draw(t){const N=vb(svg,'720 380','400 744'),p=phaseOf(MS_STEPS,t),P=MS_STEPS[p],kg=kgAt(t);
    const L=N?{tx:12,ty:22,cx:46,cy:62,cw:328,ch:260,px:10,py:396,pw:380,ph:338}
             :{tx:16,ty:24,cx:50,cy:62,cw:330,ch:248,px:420,py:20,pw:288,ph:344};
    let s=T(L.tx,L.ty,P.t,'t-big')+T(L.tx,L.ty+16,P.sub,'t-sm');
    s+=chart(L,kg,p);
    s+=panel(p,ramp(t,P.from,(MS_STEPS[p+1]||{from:1}).from),kg,L.px,L.py,L.pw,L.ph);
    svg.innerHTML=s;setSt(p);note.innerHTML=noteHTML(P)}
  const stop=playWire(rg,$('#msPlay'),draw,22000,'Replay','measuring');
  setSt=stepWire($('#msSteps'),MS_STEPS,rg,draw,stop);
  asb.addEventListener('click',()=>{asian=!asian;asb.setAttribute('aria-pressed',asian);draw(+rg.value)});
  draw(+rg.value);

  /* ---------- calculator ---------- */
  const gauge=$('#msGauge'),out=$('#msOut'),met=$('#msMet'),imp=$('#msImp');let metric=true;
  const num=id=>{const v=parseFloat($('#'+id).value);return isFinite(v)?v:NaN};
  function read(){let h,w,wa;
    if(metric){h=num('msHcm')/100;w=num('msWkg');wa=num('msWaist')}
    else{const ft=num('msHft'),inch=num('msHin');h=((isFinite(ft)?ft:0)*12+(isFinite(inch)?inch:0))*0.0254;w=num('msWlb')*0.45359237;wa=num('msWaistIn')*2.54}
    return {h,w,wa}}
  function gDraw(b,r){const N=vb(gauge,'440 190','400 220');const x0=20,gw=N?360:400;
    const bx=v=>x0+gw*(clamp(v,15,45)-15)/30,rx=v=>x0+gw*(clamp(v,.35,.75)-.35)/.4;let s='';
    s+=T(x0,20,'BMI (kg/m²)','t-xs',INK);
    const B=[15,18.5,25,30,35,40,45];for(let i=0;i<6;i++)s+=`<rect x="${f1(bx(B[i]))}" y="30" width="${f1(bx(B[i+1])-bx(B[i])-1)}" height="22" rx="3" style="fill:var(--accent);opacity:${f1(.08+i*.08)}"/>`;
    B.slice(1,6).forEach(v=>s+=T(bx(v),66,v,'t-xs t-mid'));
    if(isFinite(b)){const m=bx(b);s+=`<path d="M${f1(m)} 26v30" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2.6"/><circle cx="${f1(m)}" cy="41" r="6" style="fill:var(--ink);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`+kitLabel(clamp(m,x0+30,x0+gw-30),N?88:86,f1(b),{a:'m'})}
    const ry=N?130:122;s+=T(x0,ry-10,'Waist ÷ height','t-xs',INK);
    s+=`<rect x="${x0}" y="${ry}" width="${gw}" height="16" rx="8" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${f1(rx(.5))}" y="${ry}" width="${f1(rx(.75)-rx(.5))}" height="16" rx="8" style="fill:var(--tx);opacity:.2"/>`;
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(rx(.5))}" x2="${f1(rx(.5))}" y1="${ry-5}" y2="${ry+21}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.8"/>`;
    [.4,.5,.6,.7].forEach(v=>s+=T(rx(v),ry+34,v.toFixed(1),'t-xs t-mid'));
    if(isFinite(r)){const m=rx(r);s+=`<circle cx="${f1(m)}" cy="${ry+8}" r="7" style="fill:var(--tx);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`+kitLabel(clamp(m,x0+24,x0+gw-24),ry+54,r.toFixed(2),{a:'m'})}
    else s+=T(x0+gw,ry-10,'add a waist to see the ratio','t-xs t-end');
    gauge.innerHTML=s}
  function calc(){const {h,w,wa}=read(),sex=$('#msSex').value;
    if(!(h>=1&&h<=2.3&&w>=25&&w<=350)){out.innerHTML=`<div class="kicker">Teaching calculator</div><p>Enter an adult height between 100 and 230 cm (3 ft 4 in to 7 ft 6 in) and a weight between 25 and 350 kg (55 to 770 lb).</p>`;gDraw(NaN,NaN);return}
    const b=w/(h*h),c=clsOf(b),hasW=wa>=40&&wa<=250,r=hasW?wa/(h*100):NaN;
    const ap=MS_ASIAN.filter(v=>b>=v).pop();
    let H=`<div class="kicker">Teaching calculator · published cut-offs</div><div class="row"><span>BMI</span><b>${f1(b)} kg/m²</b></div>`;
    H+=`<p>In the WHO adult classification this BMI falls in the band <b>${c.r}</b>${c.lo>=25||c.hi<=18.5?` (${c.n})`:''} <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2000TRS894,Flegal1998" title="Source 155,598"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2000TRS894">155,598</a></sup>.</p>`;
    H+=`<p>Against the WHO 2004 action points for Asian populations, it is ${ap?`at or above the <b>${ap}</b> point`:'below the first point (23)'} <sup class="c" data-ref="WHO2004Asian" title="Source 599"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-WHO2004Asian">599</a></sup>.</p>`;
    if(b>40)H+=`<p>Above BMI 40, the Lancet Commission says excess adiposity "can pragmatically be assumed" <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>.</p>`;
    if(hasW){H+=`<div class="row"><span>Waist ÷ height</span><b>${r.toFixed(2)}</b></div><p>That is ${r>=.5?'at or above':'below'} the 0.5 boundary proposed by Browning and colleagues <sup class="c" data-ref="Browning2010" title="Source 55"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Browning2010">55</a></sup>.</p>`;
      if(sex){const L1=sex==='m'?94:80,L2=sex==='m'?102:88;H+=`<p>A waist of ${Math.round(wa)} cm is ${wa>=L2?`at or above both of Lean's levels (${L1} and ${L2} cm)`:wa>=L1?`at or above the first of Lean's levels (${L1} cm) and below the second (${L2} cm)`:`below both of Lean's levels (${L1} and ${L2} cm)`} for ${sex==='m'?'men':'women'} <sup class="c" data-ref="Lean1995" title="Source 312"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Lean1995">312</a></sup>.</p>`}
      else H+=`<p class="stage-cap">Choose a sex to compare the waist with Lean's action levels, which differ for men and women <sup class="c" data-ref="Lean1995" title="Source 312"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Lean1995">312</a></sup>.</p>`}
    H+=`<div class="pt"><b>Keep in mind</b><ul><li>BMI cannot tell fat from muscle and misses about half of adults with excess body fat <sup class="c" data-ref="Okorodudu2010" title="Source 412"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Okorodudu2010">412</a></sup>.</li><li>Risk can start at lower BMI in south Asian, Chinese, Arab and Black adults <sup class="c" data-ref="Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity" title="Source 60"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Caleyachetty2021Ethnicity">60</a></sup>.</li><li>A fixed waist-to-height cut-off over-classifies shorter adults <sup class="c" data-ref="Nevill2023" title="Source 399"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Nevill2023">399</a></sup>.</li><li>These are population cut-offs: a teaching result, not a diagnosis or a target.</li></ul></div>`;
    out.innerHTML=H;gDraw(b,r)}
  function setUnits(m){if(m===metric)return;const a=read();metric=m;met.setAttribute('aria-pressed',m);imp.setAttribute('aria-pressed',!m);$('#msCalcMet').hidden=!m;$('#msCalcImp').hidden=m;
    if(isFinite(a.h)&&isFinite(a.w)){if(m){$('#msHcm').value=(a.h*100).toFixed(1);$('#msWkg').value=a.w.toFixed(1);if(isFinite(a.wa))$('#msWaist').value=a.wa.toFixed(1)}
      else{const ti=a.h/0.0254,ft=Math.floor(ti/12);$('#msHft').value=ft;$('#msHin').value=(ti-ft*12).toFixed(1);$('#msWlb').value=Math.round(a.w/0.45359237);if(isFinite(a.wa))$('#msWaistIn').value=(a.wa/2.54).toFixed(1)}}
    calc()}
  met.addEventListener('click',()=>setUnits(true));imp.addEventListener('click',()=>setUnits(false));
  $$('#m-measuring input[type=number],#msSex').forEach(el=>{el.addEventListener('input',calc);el.addEventListener('change',calc)});
  calc();
  redraws.measuring=(()=>{const prev=redraws.measuring;return()=>{prev&&prev();calc()}})();
};
/* =============== 1.3 Causes: genes & environment =============== */
/* The main player stacks influences on body weight as layers: four genetic layers (heritability, common variants,
   polygenic score, single genes), then four environmental ones (food, sleep, medicines, social context), then shows
   them acting together. Every number drawn is a published population figure from research pass B; anything that is
   only a shape (the middle polygenic deciles, the line joining published weight points) is drawn dashed or pale and
   named as schematic in the caption. */
const CA_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.13,k:'Genes · families, adoptees and twins',t:'Heritability',
  txt:'In 540 Danish adoptees, adult weight class tracked the BMI of their biological parents, not their adoptive parents. <sup class="c" data-ref="Stunkard1986" title="Source 527"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Stunkard1986">527</a></sup> Identical twins reared apart had BMI correlations of 0.70 (men) and 0.66 (women). <sup class="c" data-ref="Stunkard1990" title="Source 528"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Stunkard1990">528</a></sup> Across 88 twin estimates (140,525 twins), BMI heritability ranged from 0.47 to 0.90, median 0.75; family studies gave lower figures, median 0.46. <sup class="c" data-ref="Elks2012" title="Source 134"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Elks2012">134</a></sup> In 87,782 twin pairs, the genetic share was lowest at age 4 (0.42 in boys) and rose to 0.75 by age 19. <sup class="c" data-ref="Silventoinen2016" title="Source 509"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Silventoinen2016">509</a></sup>',
  pt:'Body size runs in families mostly because of shared genes, not shared kitchens. Heritability describes differences between people in one setting; it does not mean weight is fixed. <sup class="c" data-ref="Stunkard1986,Elks2012" title="Source 134,527"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Stunkard1986">134,527</a></sup>',
  hook:'Twin heritability of BMI 0.47–0.90 (median 0.75); family studies lower (median 0.46). Adoptees resemble their biological, not adoptive, parents. <sup class="c" data-ref="Elks2012,Stunkard1986" title="Source 134,527"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Elks2012">134,527</a></sup>'},
 {from:.17,at:.3,k:'Genes · common variants',t:'FTO and many small nudges',
  txt:'FTO was the first common obesity variant, replicated in 13 cohorts (38,759 people): the 16% of adults with two risk copies weighed about 3 kg more and had 1.67-fold odds of obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Frayling2007" title="Source 169"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Frayling2007">169</a></sup> By 2015, 97 genome regions explained about 2.7% of BMI variation, and all common variants together were estimated at more than 20%. <sup class="c" data-ref="Locke2015" title="Source 331"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Locke2015">331</a></sup> By 2018, 941 variants explained about 6.0%. <sup class="c" data-ref="Yengo2018" title="Source 616"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Yengo2018">616</a></sup> The pathways point strongly to the brain. <sup class="c" data-ref="Locke2015" title="Source 331"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Locke2015">331</a></sup>',
  pt:'Hundreds of small gene differences each nudge weight a little. Added together, they can make a big difference. <sup class="c" data-ref="Locke2015,Khera2019" title="Source 281,331"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Locke2015">281,331</a></sup>',
  hook:'FTO: two risk copies, about +3 kg and OR 1.67 for obesity. 97 loci explain about 2.7% of BMI variance; all common variants more than 20%. <sup class="c" data-ref="Frayling2007,Locke2015" title="Source 169,331"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Frayling2007">169,331</a></sup>'},
 {from:.34,at:.47,k:'Genes · adding them up',t:'Polygenic scores',
  txt:'A score built from 2.1 million variants was tested in 288,016 UK Biobank adults (mean age 57). The top decile weighed 13.0 kg more than the bottom decile (85.3 vs 72.2 kg). Severe obesity (BMI 40 or more) affected 5.6% vs 0.2%, a 25-fold gradient; obesity affected 43.2% vs 9.5%. In a birth cohort the gap was only 0.06 kg at birth, 3.5 kg at age 8 and 12.3 kg at age 18. <sup class="c" data-ref="Khera2019" title="Source 281"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Khera2019">281</a></sup>',
  pt:'Many small gene effects add up. The gap between people with high and low scores is almost nothing at birth and grows through childhood, in the world a child grows up in. Even in the top decile, 43.2% had obesity, so most did not. <sup class="c" data-ref="Khera2019" title="Source 281"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Khera2019">281</a></sup>',
  hook:'Top vs bottom polygenic decile: 13 kg heavier, a 25-fold gradient for severe obesity, only 0.06 kg apart at birth. <sup class="c" data-ref="Khera2019" title="Source 281"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Khera2019">281</a></sup>'},
 {from:.5,at:.63,k:'Genes · rare and powerful',t:'Single-gene causes',
  txt:'Rare single-gene changes break the leptin–melanocortin pathway. Congenital leptin deficiency gives very low leptin despite high fat mass; <sup class="c" data-ref="Montague1997" title="Source 372"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Montague1997">372</a></sup> daily leptin injections brought sustained improvements in appetite and fat mass. <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi2002Leptin" title="Source 138"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi2002Leptin">138</a></sup> Loss of the leptin receptor adds absent puberty and low growth hormone and thyrotropin; <sup class="c" data-ref="Clement1998" title="Source 86"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Clement1998">86</a></sup> POMC loss gives early obesity, adrenal insufficiency and red hair; <sup class="c" data-ref="Krude1998" title="Source 301"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Krude1998">301</a></sup> PC1 (PCSK1) loss impairs prohormone processing. <sup class="c" data-ref="Jackson1997" title="Source 247"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Jackson1997">247</a></sup> MC4R mutations were found in 29 of 500 people with severe childhood obesity (5.8%). <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi2003MC4R" title="Source 139"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi2003MC4R">139</a></sup>',
  pt:'A few children have one powerful gene change, such as in MC4R or leptin, that makes them feel hungry all the time. A genetic test can find this. <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi2003MC4R,Montague1997" title="Source 139,372"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi2003MC4R">139,372</a></sup>',
  hook:'MC4R deficiency is the commonest monogenic obesity: codominant, with hyperphagia, faster growth and severe hyperinsulinaemia. POMC triad: early obesity, adrenal insufficiency, red hair. <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi2003MC4R,Krude1998" title="Source 139,301"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi2003MC4R">139,301</a></sup>'},
 {from:.67,at:.8,k:'Environment',t:'The world around us',
  txt:'In a 4-week inpatient crossover trial, 20 adults ate 508 kcal a day more on an ultra-processed diet than on an unprocessed one. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup> Short sleep was linked to obesity in children (OR 1.89) and adults (OR 1.55), mostly in cross-sectional studies. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cappuccio2008" title="Source 61"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cappuccio2008">61</a></sup> In 257 trials, weight gain compared with placebo averaged 2.4 kg for olanzapine, 2.2 kg for gabapentin, 1.8 kg for amitriptyline and 1.5 kg for mirtazapine. <sup class="c" data-ref="Domecq2015" title="Source 123"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Domecq2015">123</a></sup> A person\'s chance of developing obesity rose 57% if a friend did, 40% for a sibling and 37% for a spouse, with no effect among neighbours (observational). <sup class="c" data-ref="Christakis2007" title="Source 76"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Christakis2007">76</a></sup>',
  pt:'The world around us shapes weight: what food is easy to get, how much we sleep, the medicines we need, and the people around us. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF,Cappuccio2008,Domecq2015,Christakis2007" title="Source 61,76,123,211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">61,76,123,211</a></sup>',
  hook:'Ultra-processed vs unprocessed diet: +508 kcal a day and +0.9 vs −0.9 kg in 2 weeks. Short sleep: OR 1.89 in children, 1.55 in adults. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF,Cappuccio2008" title="Source 61,211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">61,211</a></sup>'},
 {from:.84,at:.97,k:'Genes × environment',t:'Genes meet environment',
  txt:'Pima people in Mexico had type 2 diabetes at 6.9%, less than a fifth of the 38% among Pima people in Arizona, and much less obesity, despite considerable genetic similarity; physical activity was much higher in Mexico. <sup class="c" data-ref="Schulz2006" title="Source 497"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Schulz2006">497</a></sup> Each FTO risk copy raised the odds of obesity 1.30-fold in inactive adults and 1.22-fold in active adults, about 27% less. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kilpelainen2011" title="Source 283"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kilpelainen2011">283</a></sup> The FTO effect also changed for people born after 1942. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rosenquist2015" title="Source 473"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rosenquist2015">473</a></sup> A consensus statement says obesity results "primarily from a combination of genetic, epigenetic, and environmental factors", and that calling it a choice is a misconception. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2020Stigma" title="Source 477"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2020Stigma">477</a></sup>',
  pt:'Genes load the dice, but the environment rolls them. Obesity is not a choice or a lack of willpower. <sup class="c" data-ref="Schulz2006,Rubino2020Stigma" title="Source 477,497"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Schulz2006">477,497</a></sup>',
  hook:'The FTO effect is about 27% smaller in physically active adults (per-allele OR 1.22 vs 1.30). <sup class="c" data-ref="Kilpelainen2011" title="Source 283"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kilpelainen2011">283</a></sup>'}
];
/* the layers of the tower: g 1 = genes, 0 = environment; s = the step that adds it; e = the environment sub-step */
const CA_LAYERS=[
 {g:1,n:'Heritability',sn:'Heritability',v:'twins: 0.75',s:0},
 {g:1,n:'Common variants',sn:'Variants',v:'FTO: +3 kg',s:1},
 {g:1,n:'Polygenic score',sn:'Polygenic',v:'13 kg gap',s:2},
 {g:1,n:'Single genes',sn:'One gene',v:'MC4R: 5.8%',s:3},
 {g:0,n:'Food',sn:'Food',v:'+508 kcal/d',s:4,e:0},
 {g:0,n:'Sleep',sn:'Sleep',v:'OR 1.55',s:4,e:1},
 {g:0,n:'Medicines',sn:'Medicines',v:'e.g. +2.4 kg',s:4,e:2},
 {g:0,n:'Social context',sn:'Social',v:'friend +57%',s:4,e:3}
];

/* the Hall 2019 crossover: 20 adults, 14 days on each diet in random order <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup> */
const CA_UPF={extra:508,carb:280,fat:230,prot:-2,wUp:.9,wDown:-.9};
const CA_UPF_NOTES={
 start:{k:'Design',t:'Same people, both diets',
  txt:'20 weight-stable adults (mean BMI 27) lived on a metabolic ward for 4 weeks: 2 weeks on an ultra-processed diet and 2 weeks on an unprocessed diet, in random order. The meals offered were matched for calories, energy density, macronutrients, sugar, sodium and fibre, and people ate as much or as little as they wanted. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>',
  pt:'Each person was their own comparison. Only the type of food changed, not how much was offered.',
  hook:'A crossover trial: each participant receives both diets in random order, so they act as their own control.'},
 upf:{k:'Ultra-processed weeks',t:'About 500 kcal a day more, without trying',
  txt:'On the ultra-processed diet people ate 508 ± 106 kcal a day more. The extra came from carbohydrate (+280 kcal a day) and fat (+230 kcal a day), not protein (−2 kcal a day). They ate faster, by 17 kcal per minute, but their hunger and appetite ratings did not differ between the diets. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>',
  pt:'Highly processed foods make it easy to eat more without noticing. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>',
  hook:'Ultra-processed vs unprocessed: +508 kcal/day, from carbohydrate and fat, not protein. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>'},
 unp:{k:'Unprocessed weeks',t:'The reference diet',
  txt:'The unprocessed diet is the comparison, so its bars sit at zero: the trial reported the difference between the diets as a mean, not each person\'s daily intake. On this diet weight fell by 0.9 ± 0.3 kg over 2 weeks and body fat by 0.3 kg. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>',
  pt:'The same people, offered unprocessed food, ate less and lost a little weight, without being asked to.'},
 end:{k:'After 4 weeks',t:'What the trial showed, and its limits',
  txt:'Weight rose 0.9 kg on the ultra-processed diet and fell 0.9 kg on the unprocessed diet; body fat rose 0.4 kg and fell 0.3 kg. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup> The trial was small (20 people), short (2 weeks per diet) and in hospital, and why ultra-processed food is overeaten (eating rate, energy density, taste or texture) is still unresolved. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>',
  pt:'It is one carefully controlled study. It shows that the food environment, not willpower alone, changes how much people eat.',
  hook:'Weight +0.9 kg vs −0.9 kg in 2 weeks; eating rate +17 kcal/min on ultra-processed food. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hall2019UPF" title="Source 211"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hall2019UPF">211</a></sup>'}
};

inits.causes=()=>{
  /* ---------- small helpers, scoped to this module ---------- */
  const T=(x,y,s,cls='t-sm',st='')=>`<text x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" class="${cls}"${st?` style="${st}"`:''}>${s}</text>`;
  const INK='fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700';
  const wrap=(s,n)=>{const L=[];let c='';s.split(' ').forEach(w=>{if(c&&(c+' '+w).length>n){L.push(c);c=w}else c=c?c+' '+w:w});if(c)L.push(c);return L};
  const TL=(x,y,s,n,lh,cls,st)=>wrap(s,n).map((l,i)=>T(x,y+i*lh,l,cls,st)).join('');
  const box=(x,y,w,h,fill,stroke,rx=8,extra='')=>`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(Math.max(0,w))}" height="${f1(Math.max(0,h))}" rx="${rx}" style="fill:${fill};stroke:${stroke};stroke-width:1.2${extra}"/>`;
  /* horizontal bars, label above each bar: rows [{l,v,txt,col,dash}] */
  function hbars(x,y,w,rows,o){let s='';const rh=o.rh||34,vw=o.vw||92,bw=w-vw,mn=o.min||0;
    rows.forEach((r,i)=>{const ui=ease(ramp(o.u,i*.16,i*.16+.42)),yy=y+i*rh,v=clamp((r.v-mn)/(o.max-mn)),bx=x,col=r.col||o.col;
      s+=T(x,yy,r.l,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink);font-weight:600');
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(bx)}" y="${f1(yy+5)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="12" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/>`;
      const L=Math.max(r.v>mn?2:0,bw*v*ui);
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(bx)}" y="${f1(yy+5)}" width="${f1(L)}" height="12" rx="3" style="fill:${r.dash?'none':col};stroke:${col};stroke-width:${r.dash?1.6:0}${r.dash?';stroke-dasharray:4 3':''}"/>`;
      if(ui>.5)s+=T(bx+L+6,yy+15,r.txt,'t-xs',`${INK};opacity:${f1(ramp(ui,.5,1))}`)});
    return s}

  /* ---------- the tower of layers ---------- */
  function tower(t,N){let s='';const p=phaseOf(CA_STEPS,t);
    const env=CA_STEPS[4];
    const appear=L=>L.s<4?ramp(t,CA_STEPS[L.s].from-.01,CA_STEPS[L.s].from+.05):ramp(t,env.from+L.e*.03,env.from+L.e*.03+.035);
    const together=ramp(t,.84,.9);
    if(N){
      /* two rows of chips: environment above, genes below */
      const cw=88,ch=40,gx=6,x0=14;
      CA_LAYERS.forEach((L,i)=>{const a=appear(L),col=L.g?'var(--brand)':'var(--accent)',soft=L.g?'var(--brand-soft)':'var(--accent-soft)';
        const k=L.g?i:i-4,x=x0+k*(cw+gx),y=(L.g?100:54)-(1-ease(a))*14,cur=(L.s===p&&L.s<4)||(p===4&&L.g===0&&a>0)||together>0;
        s+=box(x,L.g?100:54,cw,ch,'var(--panel)','var(--line)',8,';stroke-dasharray:3 3');
        if(a>0)s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(a)}">`+box(x,y,cw,ch,soft,col,8,cur?';stroke-width:2.4':'')+T(x+7,y+16,L.sn,'t-sm',INK+';font-size:10px')+T(x+7,y+31,L.v,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')+'</g>'});
    }else{
      const x=34,w=206,h=34,gap=5,base=388;
      s+=`<text transform="translate(22 ${base-80}) rotate(-90)" class="t-xs t-mid" style="fill:var(--brand);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em">GENES</text>`;
      s+=`<text transform="translate(22 ${base-236}) rotate(-90)" class="t-xs t-mid" style="fill:var(--accent);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em">ENVIRONMENT</text>`;
      CA_LAYERS.forEach((L,i)=>{const a=appear(L),col=L.g?'var(--brand)':'var(--accent)',soft=L.g?'var(--brand-soft)':'var(--accent-soft)';
        const y0=base-(i+1)*(h+gap)+gap,y=y0-(1-ease(a))*26,cur=(L.s===p&&L.s<4)||(p===4&&L.g===0&&a>0);
        s+=box(x,y0,w,h,'none','var(--line)',8,';stroke-dasharray:3 3');
        if(a>0)s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(a)}">`+box(x,y,w,h,soft,col,8,cur||together>0?';stroke-width:2.4':'')+T(x+10,y+21,L.n,'t-lbl','font-size:12.5px')+T(x+w-10,y+21,L.v,'t-sm t-end','fill:var(--ink)')+'</g>'});
      if(together>0){const yj=base-4*(h+gap)+gap/2;
        s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(together)}"><circle cx="${x+w/2}" cy="${f1(yj)}" r="10" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.6"/>${T(x+w/2,yj+5,'×','t-lbl t-mid','font-size:16px')}</g>`}
    }
    return s}

  /* ---------- the detail panels, one per step: (x,y,w,h, u = build-up 0..1, N narrow) ---------- */
  function pHerit(X,Y,W,H,u,N){let s=T(X,Y+12,'Share of BMI variation that tracks with genes','t-lbl');
    const x0=X+4,x1=X+W-30,XV=v=>x0+(x1-x0)*v,rh=N?66:52,y0=Y+36;
    const rows=[
      {l:'Twin studies: 88 estimates, 140,525 twins',lo:.47,hi:.90,p5:.58,p95:.87,m:.75,txt:'range 0.47–0.90 · median 0.75'},
      {l:'Family studies: 27 estimates, 42,968 people',lo:.24,hi:.81,p5:.25,p95:.68,m:.46,txt:'range 0.24–0.81 · median 0.46'},
      {l:'Identical twins reared apart: BMI correlation',dots:[.66,.70],txt:'women 0.66 · men 0.70'},
      {l:'Twin children: genetic share by age',age:[.42,.75],txt:''}];
    rows.forEach((r,i)=>{const ui=ease(ramp(u,i*.17,i*.17+.4)),y=y0+i*rh;if(ui<=0&&i>0){s+=T(X,y,r.l,'t-xs','fill:var(--muted)');return}
      s+=T(X,y,r.l,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink);font-weight:600');
      s+=`<line x1="${f1(x0)}" x2="${f1(x1)}" y1="${y+16}" y2="${y+16}" style="stroke:var(--panel-2);stroke-width:12;stroke-linecap:round"/>`;
      if(r.lo!=null){const a=XV(r.lo),b=XV(lerp(r.lo,r.hi,ui)),c=XV(r.p5),d=XV(lerp(r.p5,r.p95,ui));
        s+=`<line x1="${f1(a)}" x2="${f1(b)}" y1="${y+16}" y2="${y+16}" style="stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:2.4"/><line x1="${f1(c)}" x2="${f1(Math.max(c,d))}" y1="${y+16}" y2="${y+16}" style="stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:9;stroke-linecap:round;opacity:.55"/>`;
        if(ui>.85)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(XV(r.m))}" cy="${y+16}" r="6.5" style="fill:var(--brand);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`}
      if(r.dots)r.dots.forEach((v,k)=>{if(ui>k*.4)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(XV(v))}" cy="${y+16}" r="6" style="fill:${k?'var(--brand)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:2"/>`});
      if(r.age){const v=lerp(r.age[0],r.age[1],ui);
        s+=`<circle cx="${f1(XV(r.age[0]))}" cy="${y+16}" r="6" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:2 2"/><circle cx="${f1(XV(r.age[1]))}" cy="${y+16}" r="6" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:2 2"/>`;
        s+=`<line x1="${f1(XV(r.age[0]))}" x2="${f1(XV(v))}" y1="${y+16}" y2="${y+16}" style="stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/><circle cx="${f1(XV(v))}" cy="${y+16}" r="6.5" style="fill:var(--brand);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`;
        s+=T(XV(r.age[0]),y+38,'age 4: 0.42','t-xs t-mid','fill:var(--ink)')+T(XV(r.age[1]),y+38,'age 19: 0.75','t-xs t-mid','fill:var(--ink)')}
      if(r.txt&&ui>.6)s+=T(r.lo!=null?XV(r.lo):XV(.5),y+38,r.txt,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')});
    const ya=y0+4*rh+2;
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(x0)}" x2="${f1(x1)}" y1="${ya}" y2="${ya}" class="axis"/>`;
    [0,.25,.5,.75,1].forEach(v=>{s+=`<line x1="${f1(XV(v))}" x2="${f1(XV(v))}" y1="${ya}" y2="${ya+4}" class="axis"/>`+T(XV(v),ya+16,v===0?'0':v===1?'1':String(v),'t-xs t-mid')});
    s+=T(x1,ya+30,'0 = none of the variation, 1 = all of it','t-xs t-end');
    s+=TL(X,ya+(N?60:46),'Heritability is a population statistic for one setting. It can change when the environment changes, and it does not make anyone\'s weight fixed.',N?58:76,14,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)');
    return s}

  function chromo(x,y,risk){let s='';[0,12].forEach(dx=>{s+=`<rect x="${x+dx}" y="${y}" width="8" height="30" rx="4" style="fill:var(--panel-2);stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1"/><rect x="${x+dx}" y="${y+12}" width="8" height="6" style="fill:${risk?'var(--accent)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:.8"/>`});return s}
  function pVariants(X,Y,W,H,u,N){let s='';
    const A=N?[X,Y,W,212]:[X,Y,W*.47,H],B=N?[X,Y+236,W,H-236]:[X+W*.53,Y,W*.47,H];
    /* FTO */
    const ua=ramp(u,0,.55),[ax,ay,aw]=A;
    s+=T(ax,ay+12,'FTO, the first common variant (2007)','t-lbl');
    s+=chromo(ax,ay+30,false)+T(ax+30,ay+44,'0 risk copies','t-sm',INK)+T(ax+30,ay+58,'the comparison group','t-xs');
    s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(.3+.7*ramp(ua,0,.3))}">`+chromo(ax,ay+76,true)+T(ax+30,ay+90,'2 risk copies','t-sm',INK)+T(ax+30,ay+104,'16% of adults','t-xs')+'</g>';
    const bw=aw-24,g=ease(ramp(ua,.25,.8));
    s+=T(ax,ay+132,'weight compared with 0 copies','t-xs','fill:var(--ink);font-weight:600');
    s+=`<rect x="${ax}" y="${ay+138}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="12" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${ax}" y="${ay+138}" width="${f1(bw*.6*g)}" height="12" rx="3" style="fill:var(--brand)"/>`;
    if(g>.6)s+=T(ax+bw*.6*g+6,ay+148,'about +3 kg','t-xs',INK);
    s+=T(ax,ay+170,'odds of obesity ×1.67','t-sm',`fill:var(--brand);font-weight:700;opacity:${f1(ramp(ua,.6,1))}`);
    s+=TL(ax,ay+190,'Lab work: the risk variant shifts fat-cell precursors from heat-burning beige fat towards storing white fat (early evidence).',N?62:40,13,'t-xs',`fill:var(--ink);opacity:${f1(ramp(u,.5,.8))}`);
    /* variance explained */
    const ub=ramp(u,.35,1),[bx,by,bw2]=B;
    s+=T(bx,by+12,'Share of BMI variation explained','t-lbl');
    s+=hbars(bx,by+40,bw2,[
      {l:'97 genome regions (2015)',v:2.7,txt:'≈2.7%'},
      {l:'941 variants (2018)',v:6,txt:'≈6.0%'},
      {l:'all common variants (estimate)',v:20,txt:'over 20%',dash:1},
      {l:'twin heritability (median)',v:75,txt:'75%',col:'var(--muted)'}],{u:ub,max:80,col:'var(--brand)',rh:N?36:40,vw:70});
    s+=TL(bx,by+(N?190:210),'The gap between what twins suggest and what found variants explain is called "missing heritability".',N?62:40,13,'t-xs',`fill:var(--ink);opacity:${f1(ramp(ub,.7,1))}`);
    return s}

  function pPoly(X,Y,W,H,u,N){let s='';
    const A=N?[X,Y,W,232]:[X,Y,W*.5,H-36],B=N?[X,Y+252,W,186]:[X+W*.56,Y,W*.44,H-36];
    const [ax,ay,aw,ah]=A,C=curveAxes(ax+26,ay+30,aw-84,ah-74,{x0:0,x1:10,y0:0,y1:90,yt:[0,30,60,90],ylabel:'mean weight, kg'});
    s+=T(ax,ay+10,'Weight by polygenic-score decile','t-lbl')+C.svg;
    const bwid=C.X(.72)-C.X(0);
    for(let i=0;i<10;i++){const ui=ease(ramp(u,i*.05,i*.05+.3)),end=i===0||i===9,v=end?(i?85.3:72.2):lerp(72.2,85.3,i/9),x=C.X(i+.14),yt=C.Y(v*ui),yb=C.Y(0);
      if(ui>0)s+=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(yt)}" width="${f1(bwid)}" height="${f1(yb-yt)}" rx="2" style="fill:${end?'var(--brand)':'var(--brand-soft)'};stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:${end?0:1};${end?'':'stroke-dasharray:3 2'}"/>`;
      s+=T(C.X(i+.5),yb+13,String(i+1),'t-xs t-mid');
      if(end&&ui>.9)s+=T(i?C.X(i+.5):x+bwid,yt-5,v.toFixed(1),'t-xs '+(i?'t-mid':'t-end'),INK)}
    s+=T(C.X(0),C.Y(0)+27,'decile 1 (lowest) to 10 (highest)','t-xs');
    if(u>.62){const o=ramp(u,.62,.75),xl=C.X(.5),xr=C.X(10)+8,y1=C.Y(72.2),y2=C.Y(85.3);
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(o)}"><line x1="${f1(xl)}" x2="${f1(xr+4)}" y1="${f1(y1)}" y2="${f1(y1)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 2"/><line x1="${f1(C.X(9.86))}" x2="${f1(xr+4)}" y1="${f1(y2)}" y2="${f1(y2)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:2 2"/><line x1="${f1(xr)}" x2="${f1(xr)}" y1="${f1(y1)}" y2="${f1(y2)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.6"/>${T(xr+6,(y1+y2)/2-2,'13.0 kg','t-xs',INK)+T(xr+6,(y1+y2)/2+10,'heavier','t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')}</g>`}
    /* the gap by age */
    const [bx,by,bw,bh]=B,D=curveAxes(bx+26,by+30,bw-36,bh-74,{x0:0,x1:60,y0:0,y1:14,xt:[0,8,18,57],yt:[0,5,10],ylabel:'gap, kg',xlabel:'age, years'});
    s+=T(bx,by+10,'The gap grows with age','t-lbl')+D.svg;
    const P=[[0,.06],[8,3.5],[18,12.3],[57,13]],ub=ramp(u,.3,1),up=lerp(0,60,ub);
    s+=plotLine(P,D.X,D.Y,{col:'var(--brand)',lw:2,dash:'5 4',upto:up}).svg;
    P.forEach((q,i)=>{if(q[0]<=up){s+=`<circle cx="${f1(D.X(q[0]))}" cy="${f1(D.Y(q[1]))}" r="4.5" style="fill:var(--brand);stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`;
      s+=i===0?T(D.X(24),D.Y(5),'at birth: 0.06 kg','t-xs',INK):T(D.X(q[0])+(i===3?0:7),D.Y(q[1])+(i===1?4:i===2?16:-10),q[1].toFixed(1)+' kg','t-xs'+(i===3?' t-end':''),INK)}});
    const yS=Y+H-24;
    s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(ramp(u,.75,1))}">`;
    s+=N?T(X,yS-15,'BMI 40 or more: 5.6% in the top decile vs 0.2%','t-xs',INK)+T(X,yS,'in the bottom (25-fold)','t-xs',INK)+T(X,yS+15,'BMI 30 or more: 43.2% vs 9.5%','t-xs',INK)
      :T(X,yS,'BMI 40 or more: 5.6% in the top decile vs 0.2% in the bottom (25-fold)','t-xs',INK)+T(X,yS+15,'BMI 30 or more: 43.2% vs 9.5%','t-xs',INK);
    return s+'</g>'}

  const CA_CHAIN=[['leptin','LEP · fat'],['receptor','LEPR'],['POMC','neuron'],['α-MSH','cut by PC1'],['MC4R','in the PVN']];
  const CA_GENES=[
    {g:'LEP',n:0,a:'very low leptin, severe early obesity;',b:'leptin treatment helped'},
    {g:'LEPR',n:1,a:'severe early obesity, no puberty,',b:'low growth hormone and TSH'},
    {g:'POMC',n:2,a:'early obesity, adrenal insufficiency,',b:'red hair'},
    {g:'PCSK1',n:2.5,a:'extreme childhood obesity, faulty',b:'prohormone processing'},
    {g:'MC4R',n:4,a:'intense hunger, faster growth;',b:'one or two copies (codominant)'}];
  function pMono(X,Y,W,H,u,N){let s='';const gap=N?11:16,nw=(W-4*gap)/5,ny=Y+40,nh=40;
    s+=T(X,Y+10,'The leptin–melanocortin pathway, and where single genes break it','t-lbl',N?'font-size:11.5px':'');
    const cur=Math.min(4,Math.floor(u*5.6));
    CA_CHAIN.forEach((c,i)=>{const x=X+i*(nw+gap);
      s+=box(x,ny,nw,nh,'var(--brand-soft)','var(--brand)',8)+T(x+nw/2,ny+17,c[0],'t-sm t-mid',INK)+T(x+nw/2,ny+31,c[1],'t-xs t-mid','fill:var(--ink)');
      if(i<4)s+=`<line x1="${f1(x+nw+2)}" x2="${f1(x+nw+gap-3)}" y1="${ny+nh/2}" y2="${ny+nh/2}" style="stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:1.8" marker-end="url(#caArr)"/>`});
    CA_GENES.forEach((G,k)=>{const on=ramp(u,k*.13,k*.13+.08);if(on<=0)return;const cx=X+G.n*(nw+gap)+(G.n%1?-gap/2+nw/2:nw/2)+(G.n%1?nw/2:0),cy=ny+nh/2,r=9;
      const xx=G.n%1?X+Math.floor(G.n)*(nw+gap)+nw+gap/2:cx;
      const yy=G.n%1?cy:ny-11;s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(on)}"><circle cx="${f1(xx)}" cy="${f1(yy)}" r="${r}" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--risk);stroke-width:2"/><path d="M${f1(xx-4)} ${f1(yy-4)}l8 8m0-8l-8 8" style="stroke:var(--risk);stroke-width:2.2;stroke-linecap:round"/></g>`});
    /* the list */
    const ly=Y+108,lw=N?W:W*.6;
    CA_GENES.forEach((G,k)=>{const on=ramp(u,k*.13,k*.13+.08),y=ly+k*34,hi=k===cur;
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(.25+.75*on)}">`+(hi&&on>0?box(X-4,y-12,lw,32,'var(--panel-2)','none',6):'')+T(X+2,y+2,G.g,'t-sm',`fill:var(--brand);font-weight:700`)+T(X+54,y+1,G.a,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')+T(X+54,y+14,G.b,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')+'</g>'});
    /* 29 of 500 */
    const ud=ramp(u,.66,1),dx=N?X:X+W*.64,dy=N?ly+178:ly-6,pit=N?7.2:6.4,lit=Math.round(29*ease(ud));
    if(ud>0){for(let i=0;i<500;i++){const c=i%25,r=Math.floor(i/25);s+=`<circle cx="${f1(dx+c*pit+3)}" cy="${f1(dy+r*pit+3)}" r="${f1(pit*.36)}" style="fill:${i<lit?'var(--accent)':'var(--line)'}"/>`}
      const tx=N?dx+25*pit+12:dx,ty=N?dy+14:dy+20*pit+18;
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(ramp(ud,.5,1))}">`+T(tx,ty,'29 of 500 (5.8%)','t-sm',INK)+TL(tx,ty+15,'children with severe early obesity had an MC4R mutation',N?26:30,13,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)')+'</g>'}
    if(u>.9){const yb=N?Y+H-30:Y+H-14;s+=TL(X,yb,'UK birth cohort: about 1 in 337 people carry one faulty MC4R copy; carriers were 17.76 kg heavier on average at 18',Math.floor(W/6),13,'t-xs',`${INK};opacity:${f1(ramp(u,.9,1))}`)}
    return s}

  function pEnv(X,Y,W,H,u,N){let s='';
    const M=[
      {t:'Food',sub:'extra kcal/day on ultra-processed',rows:[{l:'all extra',v:508,txt:'+508'},{l:'carbohydrate',v:280,txt:'+280'},{l:'fat',v:230,txt:'+230'},{l:'protein',v:0,txt:'−2'}],max:600},
      {t:'Sleep',sub:'short sleep and obesity: odds ratio',rows:[{l:'children',v:1.89,txt:'1.89'},{l:'adults',v:1.55,txt:'1.55'}],min:1,max:2.2,foot:'2 short nights: ghrelin +28%, leptin −18%'},
      {t:'Medicines',sub:'weight gain vs placebo, kg (trials)',rows:[{l:'olanzapine',v:2.4,txt:'2.4'},{l:'gabapentin',v:2.2,txt:'2.2'},{l:'amitriptyline',v:1.8,txt:'1.8'},{l:'mirtazapine',v:1.5,txt:'1.5'}],max:3},
      {t:'Social context',sub:'your chance rises when they do',rows:[{l:'a friend',v:57,txt:'+57%'},{l:'a sibling',v:40,txt:'+40%'},{l:'a spouse',v:37,txt:'+37%'},{l:'a neighbour',v:0,txt:'no effect'}],max:70}];
    const cols=N?1:2,mw=(W-(cols-1)*14)/cols,mh=N?(H-12)/4:(H-14)/2;
    M.forEach((m,i)=>{const um=ramp(u,i*.2,i*.2+.32);const x=X+(i%cols)*(mw+14),y=Y+Math.floor(i/cols)*(mh+(N?4:14));
      s+=box(x,y,mw,mh-4,'var(--panel)','var(--line)',10);
      if(um<=0){s+=T(x+12,y+20,m.t,'t-lbl','fill:var(--muted)');return}
      s+=box(x,y,mw,mh-4,'var(--accent-soft)','var(--accent)',10,`;opacity:${f1(um)}`);
      s+=T(x+12,y+20,m.t,'t-lbl')+T(x+12,y+34,m.sub,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)');
      /* label on the left, bar to the right */
      const lw=N?96:82,rh=N?(m.rows.length>2?19:24):(m.rows.length>2?22:26),y0=y+(N?44:50);
      m.rows.forEach((r,k)=>{const yy=y0+k*rh;s+=T(x+12,yy+11,r.l,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink);font-weight:600')});
      s+=hbarsInline(x+12+lw,y0,mw-24-lw,m.rows,{u:um,min:m.min||0,max:m.max,rh,col:'var(--accent)'});
      if(m.foot)s+=TL(x+12,y+mh-(N?24:34),m.foot,Math.floor((mw-24)/5.8),13,'t-xs',`fill:var(--ink);opacity:${f1(ramp(um,.6,1))}`)});
    return s}
  function hbarsInline(x,y,w,rows,o){let s='';const vw=60,bw=w-vw,mn=o.min||0;
    rows.forEach((r,i)=>{const ui=ease(ramp(o.u,.15+i*.12,.15+i*.12+.4)),yy=y+i*o.rh,v=clamp((r.v-mn)/(o.max-mn)),L=bw*v*ui;
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(yy+2)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="11" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/>`;
      if(L>0)s+=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(yy+2)}" width="${f1(L)}" height="11" rx="3" style="fill:${o.col}"/>`;
      if(ui>.5)s+=T(x+L+5,yy+11,r.txt,'t-xs',`${INK};opacity:${f1(ramp(ui,.5,1))}`)});
    return s}

  function pTogether(X,Y,W,H,u,N){let s='';
    const A=N?[X,Y,W,210]:[X,Y,W*.48,250],B=N?[X,Y+226,W,190]:[X+W*.54,Y,W*.46,250];
    /* Pima */
    const [ax,ay,aw,ah]=A,ua=ease(ramp(u,0,.5));
    s+=T(ax,ay+12,'Pima people, two environments','t-lbl')+TL(ax,ay+27,'type 2 diabetes, % of adults; similar genes, far more activity in Mexico',Math.floor(aw/6),13,'t-xs','fill:var(--ink)');
    const base=ay+ah-28,top=ay+62,Hh=base-top,bw=Math.min(70,aw*.26),col=[ax+aw*.18,ax+aw*.6];
    [[6.9,'Mexico',''],[38,'Arizona','']].forEach((d,i)=>{const hh=Hh*d[0]/40*ua;
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(col[i])}" y="${f1(base-hh)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="${f1(hh)}" rx="3" style="fill:${i?'var(--accent)':'var(--brand)'}"/>`;
      if(ua>.7)s+=T(col[i]+bw/2,base-hh-6,d[0]+'%','t-sm t-mid',INK);
      s+=T(col[i]+bw/2,base+13,d[1],'t-xs t-mid',INK)+T(col[i]+bw/2,base+25,d[2],'t-xs t-mid')});
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(ax)}" x2="${f1(ax+aw)}" y1="${f1(base)}" y2="${f1(base)}" class="axis"/>`;
    /* FTO by activity */
    const [bx,by,bw2,bh]=B,ub=ease(ramp(u,.35,.85));
    s+=T(bx,by+12,'FTO and physical activity','t-lbl')+T(bx,by+27,'odds of obesity per risk copy','t-xs','fill:var(--ink)');
    const b0=by+bh-28,t0=by+50,HH=b0-t0,OR=v=>HH*(v-1)/.4,cw=Math.min(70,bw2*.26),cx=[bx+bw2*.18,bx+bw2*.6];
    [[1.3,'inactive'],[1.22,'active']].forEach((d,i)=>{const hh=OR(d[0])*ub;
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(cx[i])}" y="${f1(b0-hh)}" width="${f1(cw)}" height="${f1(hh)}" rx="3" style="fill:${i?'var(--brand)':'var(--accent)'}"/>`;
      if(ub>.7)s+=T(cx[i]+cw/2,b0-hh-6,'×'+d[0].toFixed(2),'t-sm t-mid',INK);
      s+=T(cx[i]+cw/2,b0+13,d[1],'t-xs t-mid',INK)});
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(bx)}" x2="${f1(bx+bw2)}" y1="${f1(b0)}" y2="${f1(b0)}" class="axis"/>`+T(bx+bw2,b0+25,'baseline ×1.00 (no extra odds)','t-xs t-end');
    if(ub>.8)s+=T(bx,t0-8,'about 27% smaller effect when active','t-xs',`fill:var(--brand);font-weight:700;opacity:${f1(ramp(ub,.8,1))}`);
    /* the line to remember */
    const um=ramp(u,.75,1),my=N?Y+H-40:Y+H-36;
    s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(um)}">`+(N?T(X,my,'Genes load the dice;','t-big','font-size:18px')+T(X,my+22,'the environment rolls them.','t-big','font-size:18px'):T(X,my,'Genes load the dice; the environment rolls them.','t-big','font-size:19px'))+'</g>';
    return s}

  const PANELS=[pHerit,pVariants,pPoly,pMono,pEnv,pTogether];

  /* ---------- the main player ---------- */
  const svg=$('#caSvg'),rg=$('#caT');
  function draw(t){
    const N=vb(svg,'720 400','400 670'),p=phaseOf(CA_STEPS,t),P=CA_STEPS[p];
    const next=p<CA_STEPS.length-1?CA_STEPS[p+1].from:1.01,u=ramp(t,P.from+.005,Math.min(P.at,next-.01));
    const D=N?{x:14,y:162,w:372,h:496,hx:14,hy:24}:{x:262,y:64,w:446,h:326,hx:262,hy:28};
    let s=`<defs>${marker('caArr','var(--brand)',6)}</defs>`;
    s+=T(D.hx,D.hy,P.t,'t-big','font-size:18px')+T(D.hx,D.hy+16,P.k,'t-sm');
    s+=tower(t,N);
    if(N)s+=`<line x1="14" x2="386" y1="150" y2="150" class="axis"/>`;
    /* crossfade at the start of each step */
    const fade=ramp(t,P.from,P.from+.025);
    s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(p===0?1:fade)}">`+PANELS[p](D.x,D.y,D.w,D.h,u,N)+'</g>';
    svg.innerHTML=s;
    setSt(p);$('#caNote').innerHTML=noteHTML(P);
  }
  const stop=playWire(rg,$('#caPlay'),draw,30000,'Replay','causes');
  const setSt=stepWire($('#caSteps'),CA_STEPS,rg,draw,stop);
  draw(+rg.value);

  /* ---------- the ultra-processed food crossover ---------- */
  const usv=$('#caUpf'),urg=$('#caUpfT'),ubtn=$('#caUpfOrder'),usplit=$('#caUpfSplit'),uread=$('#caUpfRead'),unote=$('#caUpfNote');
  let order='upf';
  ubtn.innerHTML=[['upf','Ultra-processed first'],['unp','Unprocessed first']].map(o=>`<button class="btn" data-ord="${o[0]}" aria-pressed="${o[0]===order}">${o[1]}</button>`).join('');
  const dietOf=day=>(day<=14)===(order==='upf')?'upf':'unp';
  function wAt(d){/* schematic straight line between the published 2-week changes */
    const first=order==='upf'?CA_UPF.wUp:CA_UPF.wDown,second=-first;
    return d<=14?first*d/14:first+second*(d-14)/14}
  function drawUpf(t){
    const N=vb(usv,'720 340','400 520'),d=t*28,split=usplit.checked;
    const L=N?{x0:52,x1:384,ay:46,ah:170,by:300,bh:150,lab:14}:{x0:74,x1:704,ay:40,ah:140,by:226,bh:84,lab:16};
    const X=v=>L.x0+(L.x1-L.x0)*v/28,YA=v=>L.ay+L.ah-L.ah*v/600,YB=v=>L.by+L.bh/2-L.bh/2*v/1.2;
    let s='';
    /* period shading */
    [[0,14],[14,28]].forEach((r,i)=>{const dd=r[0]+1,diet=dietOf(dd),c=diet==='upf'?'var(--accent-soft)':'var(--good-soft)';
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(X(r[0]))}" y="${L.ay-22}" width="${f1(X(r[1])-X(r[0]))}" height="${L.by+L.bh-L.ay+22}" style="fill:${c};opacity:.55"/>`;
      s+=T((X(r[0])+X(r[1]))/2,L.ay-8,(N?'':`Days ${r[0]+1}–${r[1]}: `)+(diet==='upf'?'ultra-processed':'unprocessed'),'t-xs t-mid',`fill:${diet==='upf'?'var(--accent)':'var(--good)'};font-weight:700`)});
    /* chart A: extra intake */
    [0,250,500].forEach(v=>{s+=`<line x1="${L.x0}" x2="${L.x1}" y1="${f1(YA(v))}" y2="${f1(YA(v))}" class="grid"/>`+T(L.x0-6,YA(v)+3.5,String(v),'t-xs t-end')});
    s+=`<line x1="${L.x0}" x2="${L.x1}" y1="${f1(YA(0))}" y2="${f1(YA(0))}" class="axis"/>`;
    s+=`<text transform="translate(${L.lab} ${f1(L.ay+L.ah/2)}) rotate(-90)" class="t-xs t-mid" style="fill:var(--ink)">extra kcal/day</text>`;
    const bw=(X(1)-X(0))*.7;
    for(let i=1;i<=28;i++){if(i>Math.ceil(d-1e-6)||d<=0)break;const xi=X(i-.85),diet=dietOf(i);
      if(diet==='upf'){
        if(split){const yc=YA(CA_UPF.carb),yf=YA(CA_UPF.carb+CA_UPF.fat);
          s+=`<rect x="${f1(xi)}" y="${f1(yc)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="${f1(YA(0)-yc)}" style="fill:var(--accent)"/><rect x="${f1(xi)}" y="${f1(yf)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="${f1(yc-yf)}" style="fill:var(--gold);opacity:.85"/>`}
        else{const y=YA(CA_UPF.extra);s+=`<rect x="${f1(xi)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="${f1(YA(0)-y)}" style="fill:var(--accent)"/>`}}
      else s+=`<rect x="${f1(xi)}" y="${f1(YA(0)-2)}" width="${f1(bw)}" height="3" style="fill:var(--good)"/>`}
    s+=`<line x1="${L.x0}" x2="${L.x1}" y1="${f1(YA(508))}" y2="${f1(YA(508))}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:4 3;opacity:.6"/>`;
    s+=T(L.x1,YA(508)-5,'mean difference +508 kcal/day','t-xs t-end',INK);
    /* chart B: weight change */
    [-1,0,1].forEach(v=>{s+=`<line x1="${L.x0}" x2="${L.x1}" y1="${f1(YB(v))}" y2="${f1(YB(v))}" class="${v?'grid':'axis'}"/>`+T(L.x0-6,YB(v)+3.5,(v>0?'+':v<0?'−':'')+Math.abs(v)+' kg','t-xs t-end')});
    s+=`<text transform="translate(${L.lab} ${f1(L.by+L.bh/2)}) rotate(-90)" class="t-xs t-mid" style="fill:var(--ink)">weight change</text>`;
    let q='';const n=Math.max(1,Math.round(d*4));for(let i=0;i<=n;i++){const dd=d*i/n;q+=(i?'L':'M')+f1(X(dd))+' '+f1(YB(wAt(dd)))}
    s+=`<path d="${q}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2.4;stroke-dasharray:6 3;stroke-linejoin:round"/>`;
    [[14,wAt(14)],[28,wAt(28)]].forEach((pt,i)=>{if(d>=pt[0]-.01){const dlt=i?wAt(28)-wAt(14):wAt(14);
      s+=`<circle cx="${f1(X(pt[0]))}" cy="${f1(YB(pt[1]))}" r="5" style="fill:${dlt>0?'var(--accent)':'var(--good)'};stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:2"/>`+T(X(pt[0])-8,YB(pt[1])+(dlt>0?-9:16),(dlt>0?'+0.9 kg':'−0.9 kg')+(N?'':' in 2 weeks'),'t-xs t-end',INK)}});
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(X(d))}" cy="${f1(YB(wAt(d)))}" r="4" style="fill:var(--ink)"/>`;
    /* day axis */
    [0,7,14,21,28].forEach(v=>{s+=`<line x1="${f1(X(v))}" x2="${f1(X(v))}" y1="${L.by+L.bh}" y2="${L.by+L.bh+4}" class="axis"/>`+T(X(v),L.by+L.bh+16,String(v),'t-xs t-mid')});
    s+=T(L.x1,L.by+L.bh+30,'day of the trial','t-xs t-end');
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(X(d))}" x2="${f1(X(d))}" y1="${L.ay-2}" y2="${L.by+L.bh}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 3;opacity:.5"/>`;
    usv.innerHTML=s;
    const dd=Math.min(28,Math.max(0,Math.round(d))),upDays=[...Array(dd)].map((_,i)=>dietOf(i+1)).filter(x=>x==='upf').length;
    uread.innerHTML=`<span>Day <b>${dd}</b> of 28</span><span>Diet now: <b>${d<=0?'about to start':dietOf(Math.max(1,Math.ceil(d)))==='upf'?'ultra-processed':'unprocessed'}</b></span><span>Extra eaten so far: <b>≈${(upDays*CA_UPF.extra).toLocaleString('en-GB')} kcal</b> (508 × ${upDays} ultra-processed days, calculated here)</span>`+(split?`<span><i class="ca-sw" style="background:var(--accent)"></i>carbohydrate +280</span><span><i class="ca-sw" style="background:var(--gold)"></i>fat +230</span><span>protein −2 kcal/day</span>`:'');
    const key=d<.5?'start':d>=27.5?'end':dietOf(Math.ceil(d));
    unote.innerHTML=noteHTML(CA_UPF_NOTES[key]);
  }
  const stopU=playWire(urg,$('#caUpfPlay'),drawUpf,10000,'Replay','causes');
  ubtn.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('[data-ord]');if(!b)return;order=b.dataset.ord;$$('[data-ord]',ubtn).forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',x===b));stopU();drawUpf(+urg.value)});
  usplit.addEventListener('change',()=>drawUpf(+urg.value));
  drawUpf(+urg.value);
};
/* =============== 1.4 Appetite: the gut-brain loop =============== */
/* The main player follows one loop: the stomach, gut and fat tissue send hormones (drawn as particles, each with its own
   colour and shape) to the hypothalamus, where POMC (fullness) and AgRP (hunger) neurons in the arcuate nucleus act on
   MC4R in the paraventricular nucleus. Particle counts and meter levels are schematic: they show direction and balance,
   never measured amounts. The published numbers sit in the notes and in the meter's fact lines (research pass C). */
const AP_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.1,k:'Before a meal',t:'Fasting: ghrelin rises',
  txt:'Ghrelin is a 28-amino-acid peptide from the stomach whose activity needs an octanoyl group on serine 3. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kojima1999" title="Source 296"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kojima1999">296</a></sup> Across 24 hours, plasma ghrelin rose nearly twofold just before each meal. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup> It switches on the hunger neurons: in rodents it activated NPY/AgRP neurons, and blocking them abolished ghrelin-induced feeding. <sup class="c" data-ref="Nakazato2001" title="Source 379"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Nakazato2001">379</a></sup> In 9 volunteers, a ghrelin infusion raised buffet intake by 28% and everyone ate more. <sup class="c" data-ref="Wren2001" title="Source 608"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wren2001">608</a></sup>',
  pt:'Ghrelin comes from the stomach. It rises before meals and drops after you eat, which is one reason hunger follows a rhythm. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup>',
  hook:'Ghrelin: 28 amino acids, octanoylated at serine 3, from the stomach; it rises nearly twofold before meals and acts on arcuate NPY/AgRP neurons. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kojima1999,Cummings2001,Nakazato2001" title="Source 103,296,379"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kojima1999">103,296,379</a></sup>'},
 {from:.17,at:.28,k:'A meal arrives',t:'Eating: ghrelin falls, CCK rises',
  txt:'Within 1 hour of eating, ghrelin fell to its trough, the reverse of insulin\'s pattern. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup> The gut-brain axis works through stomach stretch, satiety peptides from the intestine and pancreas, and ghrelin, with gut endocrine cells sensing nutrients. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2007" title="Source 105"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2007">105</a></sup> CCK reduces food intake: an infusion of its C-terminal octapeptide cut intake by an average of 122 g in 12 lean men, who stopped eating sooner. <sup class="c" data-ref="Gibbs1973,Kissileff1981" title="Source 193,288"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Gibbs1973">193,288</a></sup>',
  pt:'As food arrives, the stomach stops sending its hunger signal and the first fullness signals start. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001,Cummings2007" title="Source 103,105"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103,105</a></sup>',
  hook:'Ghrelin falls to its trough within 1 hour of eating; CCK shortens the meal. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001,Kissileff1981" title="Source 103,288"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103,288</a></sup>'},
 {from:.34,at:.45,k:'After the meal',t:'Fullness: GLP-1 and PYY',
  txt:'PYY(3-36) is released after meals in proportion to the calories eaten and acts on Y2 receptors on arcuate NPY neurons; infusing post-meal levels cut food intake by 33% over 24 hours. <sup class="c" data-ref="Batterham2002" title="Source 40"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Batterham2002">40</a></sup> GLP-1 from intestinal L cells is released after meals <sup class="c" data-ref="Holst2007" title="Source 231"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Holst2007">231</a></sup>, slows gastric emptying even at a physiological dose <sup class="c" data-ref="Nauck1997" title="Source 381"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Nauck1997">381</a></sup> and cut lunch intake by 12% in healthy men. <sup class="c" data-ref="Flint1998" title="Source 160"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Flint1998">160</a></sup> POMC neurons release alpha-MSH, which activates MC4R; mice lacking MC4R overeat and develop obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Huszar1997" title="Source 240"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Huszar1997">240</a></sup>',
  pt:'After a meal, your gut releases PYY, CCK and GLP-1, which help you feel full. GLP-1 also slows how fast your stomach empties. <sup class="c" data-ref="Batterham2002,Kissileff1981,Flint1998,Nauck1997" title="Source 40,160,288,381"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Batterham2002">40,160,288,381</a></sup>',
  hook:'POMC → alpha-MSH → MC4R in the paraventricular nucleus = fullness. PYY(3-36) acts on Y2 receptors on NPY neurons. <sup class="c" data-ref="Huszar1997,Batterham2002" title="Source 40,240"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Huszar1997">40,240</a></sup>'},
 {from:.5,at:.61,k:'The long-term signal',t:'Leptin reports the stores',
  txt:'Leptin, the product of the ob gene, was cloned in 1994. <sup class="c" data-ref="Zhang1994" title="Source 619"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Zhang1994">619</a></sup> Serum leptin rises with fat mass: 31.3 ng/mL on average in 139 people with obesity against 7.5 ng/mL in 136 without, with r = 0.85 against percentage body fat. <sup class="c" data-ref="Considine1996" title="Source 93"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Considine1996">93</a></sup> Leptin excites POMC neurons and reduces inhibition from neighbouring NPY/GABA neurons. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cowley2001" title="Source 101"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cowley2001">101</a></sup> The hindbrain\'s nucleus tractus solitarius combines vagal gut signals with hormones, so appetite control is spread across the brain. <sup class="c" data-ref="Grill2012" title="Source 198"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Grill2012">198</a></sup>',
  pt:'Leptin is made by fat. More fat usually means more leptin, a slow, steady report on how much energy is stored. <sup class="c" data-ref="Considine1996" title="Source 93"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Considine1996">93</a></sup>',
  hook:'Leptin excites POMC neurons and inhibits NPY/AgRP input; serum leptin tracks body fat (r = 0.85). <sup class="c" data-ref="Cowley2001,Considine1996" title="Source 93,101"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cowley2001">93,101</a></sup>'},
 {from:.67,at:.78,k:'In common obesity',t:'Leptin resistance',
  txt:'Most people with obesity have high leptin and appear insensitive to it. <sup class="c" data-ref="Considine1996" title="Source 93"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Considine1996">93</a></sup> Serum leptin was 318% higher in obesity (40.2 vs 9.6 ng/mL), but leptin in the cerebrospinal fluid was only about 30% higher (0.337 vs 0.259 ng/mL): the CSF/serum ratio was 4.3-fold lower. <sup class="c" data-ref="Caro1996" title="Source 64"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Caro1996">64</a></sup> Obesity itself weakens leptin signalling inside cells, so cause and effect are hard to separate. <sup class="c" data-ref="Myers2010" title="Source 377"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Myers2010">377</a></sup> In common obesity, leptin injections gave modest, variable weight change (−0.7 to −7.1 kg over 24 weeks). <sup class="c" data-ref="Heymsfield1999" title="Source 225"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Heymsfield1999">225</a></sup>',
  pt:'In most people with obesity the brain hears the leptin signal less well, a bit like a radio turned down. <sup class="c" data-ref="Considine1996,Caro1996" title="Source 64,93"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Considine1996">64,93</a></sup>',
  hook:'High leptin in common obesity means resistance, not deficiency; the CSF/serum leptin ratio is 4.3-fold lower. <sup class="c" data-ref="Considine1996,Caro1996" title="Source 64,93"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Considine1996">64,93</a></sup>'},
 {from:.84,at:.95,k:'When one gene breaks',t:'Leptin deficiency and MC4R',
  txt:'Two children from one family had very low leptin despite high fat mass, from a homozygous frameshift in the leptin gene: the first genetic proof that leptin regulates human energy balance. <sup class="c" data-ref="Montague1997" title="Source 372"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Montague1997">372</a></sup> Leptin treatment reduces their hyperphagia and obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi1999Leptin,Farooqi2002Leptin" title="Source 137,138"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi1999Leptin">137,138</a></sup> MC4R mutations, the most common monogenic cause, were found in 5.8% of 500 people with severe childhood obesity, with hyperphagia and codominant inheritance. <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi2003MC4R" title="Source 139"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi2003MC4R">139</a></sup> The MC4R agonist setmelanotide gave ≥10% weight loss in 80% (POMC deficiency) and 45% (LEPR deficiency) at about a year. <sup class="c" data-ref="Clement2020" title="Source 87"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Clement2020">87</a></sup>',
  pt:'When one key link in the loop is missing, hunger can be intense and constant. That is a medical cause, not a lack of willpower. <sup class="c" data-ref="Farooqi2003MC4R,Montague1997" title="Source 139,372"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Farooqi2003MC4R">139,372</a></sup>',
  hook:'Congenital leptin deficiency: very low leptin, severe early obesity, treatable with leptin. MC4R deficiency: 5.8% of severe childhood obesity, codominant. <sup class="c" data-ref="Montague1997,Farooqi2003MC4R" title="Source 139,372"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Montague1997">139,372</a></sup>'}
];
/* meter rows: hormone kind, name, where from, and a short published fact per step group (no citations inside the SVG) */
const AP_METER=[
 {k:'ghrelin',n:'ghrelin',src:'stomach'},
 {k:'cck',n:'CCK',src:'duodenum'},
 {k:'glp1',n:'GLP-1',src:'L cells'},
 {k:'pyy',n:'PYY',src:'L cells'},
 {k:'leptin',n:'leptin',src:'fat'}];
const AP_FACT=['ghrelin rises nearly twofold before a meal','ghrelin falls to its trough within 1 hour','PYY infusion: −33% food over 24 h','leptin tracks body fat (r = 0.85)','CSF/serum leptin ratio 4.3-fold lower','MC4R: 5.8% of severe childhood obesity'];
/* signal levels along the loop, 0..1: schematic */
function apLv(t){const ph=phaseOf(AP_STEPS,t);
  const ghr=t<.17?lerp(.35,1,ease(ramp(t,0,.14))):t<.5?lerp(1,.12,ease(ramp(t,.18,.3))):ph===5?.4:.3;
  const cck=bump(t,.18,.44),glp=bump(t,.26,.52)*.95,pyy=bump(t,.28,.54)*.9;
  const lep=ph<3?.25:ph===3?lerp(.25,.75,ease(ramp(t,.5,.58))):ph===4?lerp(.75,1,ramp(t,.67,.74)):lerp(1,0,ramp(t,.84,.88));
  const brainLep=ph===4?lerp(.75,.3,ramp(t,.67,.76)):ph===5?lep*.3:lep;
  const food=t>.17&&t<.5?ramp(t,.17,.5)*.55:null,fill=bump(t,.16,.46);
  let pomc=clamp(Math.max(cck*.6,glp,pyy)*.95+brainLep*.6-ghr*.15),agrp=clamp(ghr*1.05-Math.max(glp,pyy)*.4-brainLep*.3);
  if(ph===4){agrp=Math.max(agrp,.45);pomc=Math.min(pomc,.45)}
  if(ph===5){agrp=lerp(agrp,.95,ramp(t,.84,.9));pomc=lerp(pomc,.25,ramp(t,.84,.9))}
  const mc4r=ph===5?lerp(pomc,0,ramp(t,.88,.93)):clamp(pomc*(1-agrp*.6));
  return {ghr:clamp(ghr),cck:clamp(cck),glp1:clamp(glp),pyy:clamp(pyy),leptin:clamp(lep),brainLep:clamp(brainLep),food,fill,pomc,agrp,mc4r}}

/* the 24-hour ghrelin day: schematic shape built from the published pattern <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup> */
const AP_MEALS=[8,12.5,18.5];
const AP_MODES={
 typical:{lab:'Typical day',k:'24 hours of ghrelin',t:'A rise before every meal',
  txt:'In 10 healthy adults sampled 38 times over 24 hours on fixed meals, plasma ghrelin rose nearly twofold just before each meal and fell to its trough within 1 hour after eating, the reverse of insulin. Between meals it followed a daily rhythm, peaking at 01:00 and lowest at 09:00. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup> The meal times drawn here are illustrative.',
  pt:'Ghrelin builds as a meal gets closer, drops soon after eating, and is highest in the middle of the night. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup>',
  hook:'Pre-meal ghrelin surge nearly twofold; trough within 1 hour after eating; diurnal peak 01:00, nadir 09:00. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2001" title="Source 103"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2001">103</a></sup>'},
 diet:{lab:'After diet-induced weight loss',k:'After 17% weight loss by diet',t:'Ghrelin goes up',
  txt:'After diet-induced weight loss of 17%, the 24-hour ghrelin area under the curve rose by 24% compared with before the diet. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002" title="Source 104"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104</a></sup> One year after a 10-week diet programme, ghrelin and hunger were still above baseline, and leptin, PYY and CCK still below. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup> The rise is drawn here as the whole day scaled by 1.24.',
  pt:'After weight loss, the body fights back. Hunger hormones rise and can stay up for a long time. That is biology, not a lack of willpower. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>',
  hook:'Diet-induced weight loss: ghrelin AUC +24%. One year on, ghrelin and hunger still high, leptin, PYY and CCK still low. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002,Sumithran2011" title="Source 104,530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104,530</a></sup>'},
 bypass:{lab:'After gastric bypass',k:'After Roux-en-Y gastric bypass',t:'Ghrelin falls and flattens',
  txt:'After Roux-en-Y gastric bypass with 36% weight loss, the 24-hour ghrelin area under the curve was 77% lower than in normal-weight controls and 72% lower than in matched controls with obesity, and the meal-related swings disappeared. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002" title="Source 104"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104</a></sup> After bypass, post-meal PYY and GLP-1 were also higher than in lean controls, a rise not seen after a gastric band. <sup class="c" data-ref="leRoux2006" title="Source 319"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-leRoux2006">319</a></sup>',
  pt:'Bypass surgery changes the hunger signals themselves: much less ghrelin and more of the fullness hormones. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002,leRoux2006" title="Source 104,319"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104,319</a></sup>',
  hook:'Gastric bypass: ghrelin AUC 77% below normal-weight controls, with no meal swings; post-meal PYY and GLP-1 rise. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002,leRoux2006" title="Source 104,319"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104,319</a></sup>'}
};

inits.appetite=()=>{
  const T=(x,y,s,cls='t-sm',st='')=>`<text x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" class="${cls}"${st?` style="${st}"`:''}>${s}</text>`;
  const INK='fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700';
  /* particles along a quadratic curve from a to b */
  const stream=(a,b,bend,kind,n,lv,ph,r,dashOp=.5)=>{if(lv<=.03)return '';const c=[(a[0]+b[0])/2+bend[0],(a[1]+b[1])/2+bend[1]];
    let s=`<path d="M${f1(a[0])} ${f1(a[1])}Q${f1(c[0])} ${f1(c[1])} ${f1(b[0])} ${f1(b[1])}" style="fill:none;stroke:${HORMONE_INFO[kind].col};stroke-width:1.3;stroke-dasharray:2 4;opacity:${f1(lv*dashOp)}"/>`;
    const m=Math.max(1,Math.round(n*lv));
    for(let i=0;i<m;i++){const u=((i/m)+ph)%1,q=1-u,x=q*q*a[0]+2*q*u*c[0]+u*u*b[0],y=q*q*a[1]+2*q*u*c[1]+u*u*b[1];
      s+=hormoneDot(x,y,kind,{r,op:clamp(lv*1.5)*(u<.08?u/.08:u>.92?(1-u)/.08:1)})}
    return s};
  const cross=(x,y,r=9)=>`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="${r}" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--risk);stroke-width:2"/><path d="M${f1(x-4)} ${f1(y-4)}l8 8m0-8l-8 8" style="stroke:var(--risk);stroke-width:2.2;stroke-linecap:round"/>`;

  /* ---------- the loop player ---------- */
  $('#apKey').innerHTML=['ghrelin','cck','glp1','pyy','leptin'].map(k=>`<span><svg viewBox="0 0 14 14">${hormoneDot(7,7,k,{r:4.6})}</svg>${HORMONE_INFO[k].name}</span>`).join('');
  const svg=$('#apSvg'),rg=$('#apT');
  function draw(t){
    const N=vb(svg,'720 400','400 680'),p=phaseOf(AP_STEPS,t),P=AP_STEPS[p],V=apLv(t),ph=RM?.3:(t*16)%1;
    const L=N?{hx:14,hy:24,bx:4,by:52,bs:1.3,gx:4,gy:290,gs:.98,fx:222,fy:420,fw:164,fh:84,mx:14,my:556,mw:372,r:5.2}
             :{hx:16,hy:26,bx:262,by:20,bs:1.12,gx:14,gy:90,gs:1.06,fx:262,fy:290,fw:150,fh:80,mx:448,my:252,mw:258,r:4.8};
    let s=T(L.hx,L.hy,P.t,'t-big','font-size:18px')+T(L.hx,L.hy+16,P.k,'t-sm');
    const G=gutTract(L.gx,L.gy,L.gs,{fill:V.fill,food:V.food,glow:{stomach:V.ghr*.9,duo:V.cck,ileum:Math.max(V.glp1,V.pyy)}});
    s+=G.svg;
    const F=adiposeTissue(L.fx,L.fy,L.fw,L.fh,{size:p>=3?.75:.55,seed:6,frame:true,cell:24});
    s+=F.svg+kitLabel(L.fx+L.fw/2,L.fy+L.fh+13,'fat tissue',{a:'m'});
    s+=kitLabel(G.at.stomach[0]+8,G.at.stomach[1]-22,'stomach',{a:'m'})+kitLabel(G.at.duo[0]-4,G.at.duo[1]+4,'duodenum',{a:'e'})+kitLabel(G.at.ileum[0],G.at.ileum[1]+24,'ileum (L cells)',{a:'m'});
    const B=brainHypothalamus(L.bx,L.by,L.bs,{pomc:V.pomc,agrp:V.agrp,mc4r:V.mc4r,labels:true});
    s+=B.svg;
    const tgt=B.at.bloodIn,hy=B.at.hypo;
    /* streams to the hypothalamus inset */
    s+=stream(G.at.stomach,tgt,[N?-60:-30,N?-70:-60],'ghrelin',9,V.ghr,ph,L.r);
    s+=stream(G.at.duo,tgt,[N?-80:-40,-30],'cck',7,V.cck,(ph+.33)%1,L.r);
    s+=stream(G.at.ileum,tgt,[N?-40:30,N?-60:-20],'glp1',8,V.glp1,(ph+.15)%1,L.r);
    s+=stream([G.at.ileum[0]+12,G.at.ileum[1]+6],tgt,[N?-10:60,N?-40:0],'pyy',7,V.pyy,(ph+.6)%1,L.r);
    /* leptin: from fat; in resistance only a share crosses into the brain */
    const fatOut=[L.fx+L.fw*.6,L.fy];
    if(p===4){const gf=N?.7:.55,gate=[lerp(fatOut[0],tgt[0],gf),lerp(fatOut[1],tgt[1],gf)];
      s+=stream(fatOut,gate,[N?30:40,-10],'leptin',10,V.leptin,(ph+.4)%1,L.r);
      s+=stream(gate,tgt,[0,0],'leptin',3,V.brainLep,(ph*1.3)%1,L.r,.8);
      const ang=Math.atan2(tgt[1]-gate[1],tgt[0]-gate[0])+Math.PI/2,dx=Math.cos(ang)*22,dy=Math.sin(ang)*22;
      s+=`<line x1="${f1(gate[0]-dx)}" y1="${f1(gate[1]-dy)}" x2="${f1(gate[0]+dx)}" y2="${f1(gate[1]+dy)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:3;stroke-dasharray:4 3;opacity:${f1(ramp(t,.67,.72))}"/>`;
      s+=kitLabel(gate[0]-26,gate[1]+4,'barrier into the brain',{a:'e'})}
    else s+=stream(fatOut,tgt,[N?30:40,-10],'leptin',9,V.leptin,(ph+.4)%1,L.r);
    if(p===5){const o=ramp(t,.86,.9);
      s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(o)}">`+cross(fatOut[0],fatOut[1]-12)+kitLabel(fatOut[0]+14,fatOut[1]-24,'no leptin',{})+'</g>';
      if(B.at.inset){const pv=B.at.pvn;s+=`<g style="opacity:${f1(ramp(t,.88,.93))}">`+cross(pv[0]+B.at.inset[2]*.55,pv[1]-B.at.inset[2]*.25)+'</g>'}}
    /* hunger vs fullness readout near the brain */
    const bal=V.pomc-V.agrp;
    const balTxt=()=>T(L.mx+L.mw,L.my-3,bal>.12?'fullness winning':bal<-.12?'hunger winning':'in balance','t-sm t-end',`font-weight:700;fill:${bal>.12?'var(--brand)':bal<-.12?'var(--accent)':'var(--muted)'}`);
    /* meter */
    const M=L,rowH=N?18:20;
    s+=`<rect x="${M.mx-8}" y="${M.my-18}" width="${M.mw+16}" height="${AP_METER.length*rowH+44}" rx="10" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--line)"/>`;
    s+=T(M.mx,M.my-3,'signal level (schematic)','t-xs',INK)+balTxt();
    AP_METER.forEach((m,i)=>{const y=M.my+8+i*rowH,v=m.k==='leptin'?V.leptin:V[m.k],bw=M.mw-150;
      s+=hormoneDot(M.mx+5,y,m.k,{r:4.5})+T(M.mx+16,y+4,m.n,'t-xs',INK)+T(M.mx+60,y+4,m.src,'t-xs');
      s+=`<rect x="${M.mx+120}" y="${y-5}" width="${bw}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${M.mx+120}" y="${y-5}" width="${f1(Math.max(1,bw*v))}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:${HORMONE_INFO[m.k].col}"/>`});
    s+=T(M.mx,M.my+8+AP_METER.length*rowH+6,AP_FACT[p],'t-xs',`fill:var(--ink)`);
    svg.innerHTML=s;
    setSt(p);$('#apNote').innerHTML=noteHTML(P);
  }
  const stop=playWire(rg,$('#apPlay'),draw,26000,'Replay','appetite');
  const setSt=stepWire($('#apSteps'),AP_STEPS,rg,draw,stop);
  draw(+rg.value);

  /* ---------- the 24-hour ghrelin curve ---------- */
  const gsv=$('#apGh'),grg=$('#apGhT'),gbt=$('#apGhModes'),gins=$('#apGhIns'),gread=$('#apGhRead'),gnote=$('#apGhNote');
  let mode='typical';
  gbt.innerHTML=Object.keys(AP_MODES).map(k=>`<button class="btn" data-gm="${k}" aria-pressed="${k===mode}">${AP_MODES[k].lab}</button>`).join('');
  /* clock hours run 6 → 30 (06:00 to 06:00 next day) */
  const base=h=>{const hh=((h%24)+24)%24;/* intermeal rhythm: lowest 09:00, highest 01:00 */
    const d=(hh-9+24)%24;return d<=16?lerp(.42,.62,(1-Math.cos(Math.PI*d/16))/2):lerp(.62,.42,(1-Math.cos(Math.PI*(d-16)/8))/2)};
  const pre=h=>{let v=0;AP_MEALS.forEach(m=>{if(h>m-3&&h<=m)v=Math.max(v,Math.pow((h-(m-3))/3,2));else if(h>m&&h<m+1)v=Math.max(v,1-(h-m))});return v};
  const dip=h=>{let v=0;AP_MEALS.forEach(m=>{v=Math.max(v,bump(h,m+.4,m+2.6))});return v};
  const ghT=h=>base(h)*(.9+pre(h)*.65-dip(h)*.12);
  let MEAN=0;for(let i=0;i<=240;i++)MEAN+=ghT(6+24*i/240);MEAN/=241;
  const gh=(h,md)=>md==='diet'?ghT(h)*1.24:md==='bypass'?MEAN*.23*(1+.04*Math.sin((h-1)/24*Math.PI*2)):ghT(h);
  const ins=h=>{let v=.06;AP_MEALS.forEach(m=>{v+=bump(h,m,m+3)*.55*(h<m+.8?1:1)});return v};
  const clock=h=>{const hh=((Math.floor(h)%24)+24)%24,mm=Math.round((h-Math.floor(h))*60);return String(hh).padStart(2,'0')+':'+String(mm===60?0:mm).padStart(2,'0')};
  function drawGh(t){
    const N=vb(gsv,'720 310','400 420'),h=6+24*t,md=mode,showI=gins.checked;
    const L=N?{x:46,y:58,w:338,h:290}:{x:60,y:50,w:640,h:210};
    const C=curveAxes(L.x,L.y,L.w,L.h,{x0:6,x1:30,y0:0,y1:2,xt:N?[6,12,18,24,30]:[6,9,12,15,18,21,24,27,30],yt:[0,.5,1,1.5,2],xfmt:v=>String(v%24).padStart(2,'0')+':00',yfmt:v=>v.toFixed(1)});
    let s=C.svg+T(L.x-40,L.y-34,'ghrelin, relative to the typical day\'s average (schematic)','t-xs',INK);
    /* night band */
    s+=`<rect x="${f1(C.X(22))}" y="${L.y}" width="${f1(C.X(30)-C.X(22))}" height="${L.h}" style="fill:var(--panel-2);opacity:.6"/>`+T(C.X(26),L.y+14,'night','t-xs t-mid');
    AP_MEALS.forEach((m,i)=>{const x=C.X(m);s+=`<line x1="${f1(x)}" x2="${f1(x)}" y1="${L.y}" y2="${L.y+L.h}" style="stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/>`+T(x,L.y-6,['breakfast','lunch','dinner'][i],'t-xs t-mid',`fill:var(--accent);font-weight:700`)});
    const nrm=v=>v/MEAN;
    const path=(f,a,b)=>{let q='';const n=200;for(let i=0;i<=n;i++){const hh=lerp(a,b,i/n);q+=(i?'L':'M')+f1(C.X(hh))+' '+f1(C.Y(Math.min(2,nrm(f(hh)))))}return q};
    if(md!=='typical')s+=`<path d="${path(ghT,6,30)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ghrelin);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:5 4;opacity:.55"/>`+T(C.X(29.6),C.Y(nrm(ghT(29.6)))-6,'typical day','t-xs t-end');
    if(showI)s+=`<path d="${path(ins,6,30)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--insulin);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/>`;
    const f=hh=>gh(hh,md);
    s+=`<path d="${path(f,6,h)}L${f1(C.X(h))} ${f1(C.Y(0))}L${f1(C.X(6))} ${f1(C.Y(0))}Z" style="fill:var(--ghrelin);opacity:.14"/>`;
    s+=`<path d="${path(f,6,h)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ghrelin);stroke-width:3;stroke-linejoin:round"/>`;
    const cy=C.Y(Math.min(2,nrm(f(h))));
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(C.X(h))}" x2="${f1(C.X(h))}" y1="${L.y}" y2="${L.y+L.h}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:3 3;opacity:.6"/>`+hormoneDot(C.X(h),cy,'ghrelin',{r:6});
    /* legend */
    const lg=[L.x,L.y+L.h+38];
    s+=hormoneDot(lg[0]+5,lg[1]-4,'ghrelin',{r:5})+T(lg[0]+14,lg[1],md==='typical'?'ghrelin':md==='diet'?'ghrelin after diet (×1.24)':'ghrelin after bypass (77% lower, flat)','t-xs',INK);
    if(showI)s+=`<line x1="${f1(lg[0]+(N?0:250))}" x2="${f1(lg[0]+(N?14:264))}" y1="${lg[1]+(N?14:-4)}" y2="${lg[1]+(N?14:-4)}" style="stroke:var(--insulin);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:2 3"/>`+T(lg[0]+(N?20:270),lg[1]+(N?18:0),'insulin (schematic: the reverse pattern)','t-xs',INK);
    gsv.innerHTML=s;
    /* readout */
    let near=null;AP_MEALS.forEach(m=>{if(h>m-3&&h<=m)near=['before',m];else if(h>m&&h<m+1.2)near=['after',m]});
    const nm=m=>['breakfast','lunch','dinner'][AP_MEALS.indexOf(m)];
    const st=md==='bypass'?'low and flat: no meal swings':near?(near[0]==='before'?`rising before ${nm(near[1])}`:`falling after ${nm(near[1])}`):(((h%24)+24)%24)>=22||(((h%24)+24)%24)<6?'overnight: the daily peak is near 01:00':'between meals';
    gread.innerHTML=`<span>Time <b>${clock(h)}</b></span><span>Ghrelin: <b>${st}</b></span><span>Level <b>${nrm(f(h)).toFixed(2)}×</b> the typical day's average (schematic)</span>`;
  }
  function setMode(m){mode=m;$$('[data-gm]',gbt).forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',b.dataset.gm===m));gnote.innerHTML=noteHTML(AP_MODES[m]);drawGh(+grg.value)}
  const stopG=playWire(grg,$('#apGhPlay'),drawGh,12000,'Replay','appetite');
  gbt.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('[data-gm]');if(!b)return;stopG();setMode(b.dataset.gm)});
  gins.addEventListener('change',()=>drawGh(+grg.value));
  setMode(mode);
};
/* =============== 1.5 fat tissue as an organ =============== */
/* Main player: body -> belly cross-section -> a sheet of fat cells that enlarge, run short of oxygen, gather
   macrophages, shift their signals and finally spill fatty acids into liver, muscle and pancreas. All levels are
   schematic; the numbers in the notes come from the research pass, cited. */
const AD_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.07,k:'The body',t:'Two places to store fat',
  txt:'Fat under the skin is subcutaneous fat; fat inside the abdomen, around the organs, is visceral fat. In 3001 Framingham participants, visceral fat was more strongly linked to metabolic risk: the odds ratio for metabolic syndrome per 1-SD increase was 4.7 for visceral vs 3.0 for subcutaneous fat in women, and 4.2 vs 2.5 in men. Only visceral fat added information after adjusting for BMI and waist. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fox2007Framingham" title="Source 166"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fox2007Framingham">166</a></sup> Visceral fat measured by CT or MRI is an independent marker of cardiovascular and metabolic risk and death. <sup class="c" data-ref="Neeland2019" title="Source 396"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Neeland2019">396</a></sup>',
  pt:'Where fat is stored matters. Fat deep in the belly and fat in the liver are more closely linked to diabetes and heart disease than fat under the skin. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fox2007Framingham,Neeland2019" title="Source 166,396"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fox2007Framingham">166,396</a></sup>',
  hook:'Visceral fat outranks subcutaneous fat: OR for metabolic syndrome 4.7 vs 3.0 per SD in women. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fox2007Framingham" title="Source 166"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fox2007Framingham">166</a></sup>'},
 {from:.17,at:.27,k:'Zoom in',t:'Fat cells grow',
  txt:'Fat tissue can expand through bigger cells (hypertrophy) or more cells (hyperplasia). Cell number is most likely to rise in the first years of life and again at about age 9 to 13. <sup class="c" data-ref="Salans1973" title="Source 486"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Salans1973">486</a></sup> In adults the number stays constant, even after marked weight loss. <sup class="c" data-ref="Spalding2008" title="Source 518"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Spalding2008">518</a></sup> In 764 adults, hypertrophic fat (few large cells) went with higher fasting insulin and lower insulin sensitivity, independent of fat mass; people with hypertrophy made 70% fewer new fat cells per year than people with hyperplasia. <sup class="c" data-ref="Arner2010" title="Source 24"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Arner2010">24</a></sup>',
  pt:'Each fat cell is mostly one big droplet of stored fat. When there is more to store, the cells mainly get bigger. <sup class="c" data-ref="Spalding2008,Arner2010" title="Source 24,518"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Spalding2008">24,518</a></sup>',
  hook:'Hypertrophy (bigger cells) vs hyperplasia (more cells); hypertrophic fat is the less insulin-sensitive pattern. <sup class="c" data-ref="Arner2010" title="Source 24"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Arner2010">24</a></sup>'},
 {from:.34,at:.42,k:'Growing pains',t:'Oxygen runs short',
  txt:'Healthy expansion of fat tissue needs new blood vessels and immune remodelling. Growing fat cells can quickly reach the limit of how far oxygen diffuses from a capillary, and this hypoxia is an early factor that limits healthy expansion. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sun2011" title="Source 531"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sun2011">531</a></sup> In the drawing, cells far from the vessel turn grey-blue.',
  pt:'Very large fat cells sit further from the nearest blood vessel, so they can run short of oxygen. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sun2011" title="Source 531"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sun2011">531</a></sup>',
  hook:'Hypoxia is an early limit on healthy adipose expansion. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sun2011" title="Source 531"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sun2011">531</a></sup>'},
 {from:.5,at:.59,k:'Inflammation',t:'Crown-like structures',
  txt:'More than 90% of the macrophages in the white fat of mice and humans with obesity sit around dead fat cells. They fuse and scavenge the leftover lipid droplet, forming "crown-like structures". Fat-cell death was 30-fold higher in obese db/db mice and rose with cell size. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cinti2005" title="Source 83"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cinti2005">83</a></sup> Macrophage content rose with fat-cell size and body mass in mice and in human fat under the skin, and macrophages made almost all of the tissue\'s TNF-alpha. <sup class="c" data-ref="Weisberg2003" title="Source 588"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Weisberg2003">588</a></sup>',
  pt:'When fat cells get too big, some die. Immune cells called macrophages crowd round them to clear up, and the tissue becomes mildly inflamed. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cinti2005,Weisberg2003" title="Source 83,588"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cinti2005">83,588</a></sup>',
  hook:'Crown-like structure = macrophages ringing a dead, hypertrophic adipocyte; >90% of fat macrophages in obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cinti2005" title="Source 83"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cinti2005">83</a></sup>'},
 {from:.66,at:.75,k:'An endocrine organ',t:'Signals shift',
  txt:'Fat tissue secretes leptin, adiponectin, cytokines, complement, PAI-1, renin-angiotensin proteins and resistin. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kershaw2004" title="Source 278"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kershaw2004">278</a></sup> Leptin rises with body fat (31.3 vs 7.5 ng/mL in people with and without obesity). <sup class="c" data-ref="Considine1996" title="Source 93"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Considine1996">93</a></sup> Adiponectin, made only by fat cells, is paradoxically lower in obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Arita1999" title="Source 22"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Arita1999">22</a></sup> TNF-alpha is induced in fat in rodent obesity, and neutralising it improved insulin-stimulated glucose uptake in obese rats. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hotamisligil1993" title="Source 233"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hotamisligil1993">233</a></sup> In mice, inflammatory genes in fat rose before the sharp rise in blood insulin. <sup class="c" data-ref="Xu2003" title="Source 613"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Xu2003">613</a></sup>',
  pt:'As fat tissue gets inflamed, the messages it sends change: more inflammatory signals, less of the helpful hormone adiponectin. <sup class="c" data-ref="Arita1999,Hotamisligil1993" title="Source 22,233"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Arita1999">22,233</a></sup>',
  hook:'Adiponectin is made only by fat, yet is lower in obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Arita1999" title="Source 22"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Arita1999">22</a></sup> Fat macrophages make almost all fat-tissue TNF-alpha. <sup class="c" data-ref="Weisberg2003" title="Source 588"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Weisberg2003">588</a></sup>'},
 {from:.83,at:.93,k:'Ectopic fat',t:'Fat spills over',
  txt:'In obesity, fat tissue releases more fatty acids, glycerol, hormones and inflammatory cytokines, which drive insulin resistance; type 2 diabetes develops when beta-cell dysfunction is added. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kahn2006" title="Source 270"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kahn2006">270</a></sup> Visceral obesity goes with fat tissue under the skin that cannot expand properly and triglyceride stored in the wrong places: high triglycerides, liver insulin resistance, small dense LDL and low HDL. <sup class="c" data-ref="Tchernof2013" title="Source 544"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Tchernof2013">544</a></sup> It can reverse: on a 600 kcal/day research diet, liver fat in 11 people with type 2 diabetes fell from 12.8% to 2.9% in 8 weeks and pancreatic fat from 8.0% to 6.2%. <sup class="c" data-ref="Lim2011" title="Source 325"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Lim2011">325</a></sup> More in <a href="#diabetes" data-go="diabetes">Obesity &amp; type 2 diabetes</a>.',
  pt:'When fat tissue is full and inflamed, fat ends up in the liver, muscles and pancreas. There it makes insulin work less well. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kahn2006,Tchernof2013" title="Source 270,544"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kahn2006">270,544</a></sup>',
  hook:'Ectopic fat (liver, pancreas) links visceral obesity to insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes. <sup class="c" data-ref="Tchernof2013,Kahn2006" title="Source 270,544"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Tchernof2013">270,544</a></sup>'}
];
const AD_LBL={body:'the body',zoom:'inside fat tissue (zoomed in)',sig:'signals from fat',org:'other organs',sub:'subcutaneous',vis:'visceral',
  adipo:'adiponectin',lep:'leptin',tnf:'inflammatory signals',ffa:'fatty acids',ir:'insulin resistance',o2:'low oxygen',clsx:'crown-like structure',
  liver:'liver',muscle:'muscle',panc:'pancreas',size:['small cells','enlarging cells','enlarged cells']};

/* white / beige / brown */
const AD_KINDS=[
 {id:'white',n:'White fat',
  warm:{t:'White fat: the store',txt:'White fat stores surplus energy. <sup class="c" data-ref="Becher2021,Wu2012" title="Source 42,609"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Becher2021">42,609</a></sup> Each cell is one big lipid droplet with the nucleus pressed against the rim. Cold does not turn it into a heater. White fat is also the tissue that sends leptin and adiponectin. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kershaw2004" title="Source 278"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kershaw2004">278</a></sup>'},
  cold:{t:'White fat in the cold',txt:'White fat stores energy rather than burning it as heat; heat production through UCP1 belongs to brown and beige fat. <sup class="c" data-ref="Becher2021,Wu2012" title="Source 42,609"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Becher2021">42,609</a></sup>'}},
 {id:'beige',n:'Beige fat',
  warm:{t:'Beige fat, switched off',txt:'Beige fat cells appear within white fat and have very low basal UCP1. <sup class="c" data-ref="Wu2012" title="Source 609"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wu2012">609</a></sup> At rest they look much like small white fat cells with several droplets.'},
  cold:{t:'Beige fat, switched on',txt:'When stimulated, beige cells switch on high UCP1 and respiration, like brown fat. Evidence suggests the brown fat found in adults is made of beige cells. <sup class="c" data-ref="Wu2012" title="Source 609"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wu2012">609</a></sup> <span class="ev early">Early evidence</span>'}},
 {id:'brown',n:'Brown fat',
  warm:{t:'Brown fat at room temperature',txt:'Brown fat burns energy as heat through UCP1. <sup class="c" data-ref="Becher2021" title="Source 42"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Becher2021">42</a></sup> At 22 °C, brown fat activity was not seen in a group of young men. <sup class="c" data-ref="vanMarkenLichtenbelt2009" title="Source 563"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-vanMarkenLichtenbelt2009">563</a></sup> On routine PET-CT scans it was found in 7.5% of women and 3.1% of men, less often with older age, warmer weather, beta-blockers and, in older people, higher BMI. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cypess2009" title="Source 108"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cypess2009">108</a></sup>'},
  cold:{t:'Brown fat in the cold',txt:'At 16 °C, activity appeared in 23 of 24 young men; it was lower in men with overweight or obesity and tracked resting metabolic rate. <sup class="c" data-ref="vanMarkenLichtenbelt2009" title="Source 563"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-vanMarkenLichtenbelt2009">563</a></sup> After 2 hours at 19 °C it was seen in 17 of 32 adults aged 23 to 35 but only 2 of 24 aged 38 to 65. <sup class="c" data-ref="Saito2009" title="Source 485"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Saito2009">485</a></sup> Cold raised glucose uptake 15-fold in neck fat, and biopsies showed UCP1-positive brown fat cells. <sup class="c" data-ref="Virtanen2009" title="Source 567"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Virtanen2009">567</a></sup>'}}
];
const AD_BAT=[
 {n:'routine PET-CT, women',v:7.5},{n:'routine PET-CT, men',v:3.1},{n:'young men, 16 °C',v:96},{n:'2 h at 19 °C, age 23–35',v:53},{n:'2 h at 19 °C, age 38–65',v:8}
];
const AD_TXT={cold:'Cold on',heat:'heat (UCP1)',ucp:'UCP1 heat output (schematic)',bat:'active brown fat detected, % of people',kind:'Type'};

inits.adipose=()=>{
  /* ---------- the main player ---------- */
  const svg=$('#adSvg'),rg=$('#adT');
  /* belly cross-section: subcutaneous ring, abdominal cavity with bowel loops, visceral fat between them */
  function disc(cx,cy,R,vis,hl){
    const ri=R*(.8-.05*vis);let s='';
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(cx)}" cy="${f1(cy)}" r="${f1(R)}" style="fill:var(--fat);stroke:var(--figure-line);stroke-width:1.6"/>`;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(cx)}" cy="${f1(cy)}" r="${f1(ri)}" style="fill:var(--panel-2);stroke:var(--fat-line);stroke-width:1"/>`;
    const V=[[-.42,-.18],[.4,-.22],[0,-.48],[-.3,.3],[.34,.26],[.02,.08]],G=[[-.18,-.32],[.2,-.36],[-.44,.08],[.44,.04],[-.12,.36],[.16,.4],[0,-.12],[-.22,.12],[.24,-.06]];
    V.forEach((p,i)=>{s+=`<path d="${blob(cx+p[0]*ri,cy+p[1]*ri,ri*(.1+.16*vis),31+i,{rough:.22})}" style="fill:var(--fat);stroke:var(--fat-line);stroke-width:.8"/>`});
    G.forEach(p=>{s+=`<circle cx="${f1(cx+p[0]*ri)}" cy="${f1(cy+p[1]*ri)}" r="${f1(ri*.13)}" style="fill:var(--gut);stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1"/>`});
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(cx)}" cy="${f1(cy+ri*.74)}" r="${f1(ri*.15)}" style="fill:var(--figure);stroke:var(--figure-line);stroke-width:1"/>`;
    if(hl>0)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(cx)}" cy="${f1(cy)}" r="${f1(ri-3)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:4 3;opacity:${f1(hl)}"/>`;
    return s}
  function muscle(x,y,w,h,fat){let s=`<rect x="${f1(x)}" y="${f1(y)}" width="${f1(w)}" height="${f1(h)}" rx="${f1(h/2)}" style="fill:var(--lean);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-opacity:.4;stroke-width:1"/>`;
    for(let i=1;i<6;i++)s+=`<path d="M${f1(x+h*.4)} ${f1(y+h*i/6)}L${f1(x+w-h*.4)} ${f1(y+h*i/6)}" style="stroke:var(--panel);stroke-width:1;opacity:.45"/>`;
    const rr=rng(5),n=Math.round(fat*12);for(let i=0;i<n;i++)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x+h*.5+rr()*(w-h))}" cy="${f1(y+h*.2+rr()*h*.6)}" r="${f1(2+rr()*1.6)}" style="fill:var(--liverfat)"/>`;
    return s}
  function pancreas(x,y,w,fat){const P=[[0,.5],[.15,.2],[.45,.18],[.8,.05],[1,.22],[.96,.5],[.6,.62],[.3,.8],[.06,.84]].map(p=>[x+p[0]*w,y+p[1]*w*.42]);
    let s=`<path d="${smoothPath(P)}" style="fill:var(--cyto);stroke:var(--gut-line);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
    const rr=rng(9),n=Math.round(fat*9);for(let i=0;i<n;i++)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x+w*(.12+rr()*.72))}" cy="${f1(y+w*.42*(.3+rr()*.36))}" r="${f1(1.8+rr()*1.5)}" style="fill:var(--liverfat)"/>`;
    return s}
  function draw(t){
    const N=vb(svg,'720 380','400 560');
    const L=N?{px:46,py:22,ps:160,dc:[150,100],dR:46,bx:20,by:214,bw:360,bh:170,sx:214,sy:30,sw:112,sgh:40,org:'row',oy:418}
             :{px:56,py:46,ps:270,dc:[160,152],dR:50,bx:236,by:44,bw:236,bh:240,sx:500,sy:44,sw:120,sgh:36,org:'col',oy:178};
    const p=phaseOf(AD_STEPS,t),P=AD_STEPS[p];
    const size=lerp(.18,.95,ramp(t,.17,.34)),hyp=ramp(t,.34,.5)*.9,inf=ramp(t,.5,.64)*.38,mac=ramp(t,.52,.68),spill=ramp(t,.83,.97);
    const vis=lerp(.35,1,ramp(t,.05,.6)),hl=bump(t,0,.17);
    let s='';
    /* panel titles */
    s+=`<text x="${N?16:16}" y="${N?14:24}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${AD_LBL.body}</text>`;
    s+=`<text x="${L.bx}" y="${L.by-8}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${AD_LBL.zoom}</text>`;
    s+=`<text x="${L.sx}" y="${L.sy-12}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${AD_LBL.sig}</text>`;
    /* body and cross-section */
    const pe=person(L.px,L.py,L.ps,{size:.55});s+=pe.svg;
    const b=pe.at.belly,[cx,cy]=L.dc,R=L.dR;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(b[0])}" cy="${f1(b[1])}" r="${N?7:10}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.4"/><path d="M${f1(b[0]+(N?7:10))} ${f1(b[1])}L${f1(cx-R)} ${f1(cy)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:3 3"/>`;
    s+=disc(cx,cy,R,vis,hl);
    s+=kitLabel(cx,cy-R-6,AD_LBL.sub,{a:'m'})+kitLabel(cx,cy+R+14,AD_LBL.vis+' (inside)',{a:'m'});
    /* zoom wedge from the cross-section to the tissue box */
    const zx=cx+R*.55,zy=cy-R*.55;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(zx)}" cy="${f1(zy)}" r="6" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.2"/>`;
    s+=N?`<path d="M${f1(zx-5)} ${f1(zy+4)}L${L.bx} ${L.by}M${f1(zx+5)} ${f1(zy+4)}L${f1(L.bx+L.bw*.4)} ${L.by}" style="stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.2;fill:none"/>`
        :`<path d="M${f1(zx+4)} ${f1(zy-4)}L${L.bx} ${L.by}M${f1(zx+4)} ${f1(zy+4)}L${L.bx} ${L.by+L.bh}" style="stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.2;fill:none"/>`;
    /* the tissue */
    const tis=adiposeTissue(L.bx,L.by,L.bw,L.bh,{size,inflamed:inf,macro:mac,vessel:1,hypoxia:hyp,seed:9,frame:true,cell:N?30:32});
    s+=tis.svg;
    const sz=size<.35?0:size<.7?1:2;
    s+=kitLabel(L.bx+8,L.by+L.bh-8,AD_LBL.size[sz]+(hyp>.3?' · '+AD_LBL.o2:'')+(mac>.3?' · '+AD_LBL.clsx+'s':''),{});
    /* signals */
    const SG=[{n:AD_LBL.adipo,v:.78-.5*ramp(t,.6,.8),col:'var(--brand)'},{n:AD_LBL.lep,v:.28+.55*ramp(t,.15,.45),col:'var(--leptin)'},{n:AD_LBL.tnf,v:.08+.8*ramp(t,.5,.8),col:'var(--macro)'}];
    SG.forEach((g,i)=>{const y=L.sy+i*L.sgh,base=[.78,.28,.08][i],d=g.v-base;
      s+=`<text x="${L.sx}" y="${y+4}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink)">${g.n}</text>`;
      s+=`<rect x="${L.sx}" y="${y+9}" width="${L.sw}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${L.sx}" y="${y+9}" width="${f1(L.sw*g.v)}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:${g.col}"/>`;
      s+=`<rect x="${f1(L.sx+L.sw*base-1)}" y="${y+6}" width="2" height="16" style="fill:var(--ink);opacity:.5"/>`;
      if(Math.abs(d)>.08)s+=`<text x="${L.sx+L.sw+8}" y="${y+18}" class="t-sm" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${d>0?'▲':'▼'}</text>`});
    /* organs and the spill-over of fatty acids */
    let O;
    if(N)O=[{n:AD_LBL.liver,at:[66,L.oy+44],d:()=>liver(18,L.oy+10,.68,{fat:spill*.85}).svg},
            {n:AD_LBL.muscle,at:[200,L.oy+44],d:()=>muscle(154,L.oy+26,92,34,spill)},
            {n:AD_LBL.panc,at:[320,L.oy+44],d:()=>pancreas(272,L.oy+22,100,spill)}];
    else O=[{n:AD_LBL.liver,at:[548,L.oy+40],lp:[548,L.oy+88],d:()=>liver(498,L.oy+8,.72,{fat:spill*.85}).svg},
            {n:AD_LBL.muscle,at:[662,L.oy+39],lp:[662,L.oy+74],d:()=>muscle(616,L.oy+22,92,34,spill)},
            {n:AD_LBL.panc,at:[554,L.oy+122],lp:[554,L.oy+156],d:()=>pancreas(506,L.oy+104,96,spill)}];
    s+=`<text x="${N?16:500}" y="${N?L.oy-4:L.oy-6}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${AD_LBL.org}${spill>.05?' ← '+AD_LBL.ffa:''}</text>`;
    O.forEach((o,k)=>{s+=o.d();
      const lp=o.lp||[o.at[0],o.at[1]+44];
      s+=kitLabel(lp[0],lp[1],o.n,{a:'m'});
      if(spill>.05){const src=N?[L.bx+L.bw*(.2+.3*k),L.by+L.bh]:[L.bx+L.bw,L.by+L.bh*(.45+.2*k)],dst=o.at,
          c=N?[(src[0]+dst[0])/2,(src[1]+dst[1])/2-4]:[(src[0]+dst[0])/2,src[1]];
        s+=`<path d="M${f1(src[0])} ${f1(src[1])}Q${f1(c[0])} ${f1(c[1])} ${f1(dst[0])} ${f1(dst[1])}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--fat-line);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:3 4;opacity:${f1(spill*.7)}"/>`;
        for(let i=0;i<5;i++){const u=(t*14+i/5+k*.13)%1,q=1-u,x=q*q*src[0]+2*q*u*c[0]+u*u*dst[0],y=q*q*src[1]+2*q*u*c[1]+u*u*dst[1];
          s+=`<circle cx="${f1(x)}" cy="${f1(y)}" r="3" style="fill:var(--fat);stroke:var(--fat-line);stroke-width:1;opacity:${f1(spill*bump(u,0,1)*1.2)}"/>`}}
      if(spill>.5)s+=`<circle cx="${f1(o.at[0])}" cy="${f1(o.at[1])}" r="${N?30:32}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--risk);stroke-width:1.6;stroke-dasharray:5 4;opacity:${f1(ramp(spill,.5,1))}"/>`});
    if(spill>.5)s+=N?kitLabel(200,L.oy+128,AD_LBL.ir,{a:'m'}):kitLabel(662,L.oy+128,AD_LBL.ir,{a:'m'});
    svg.innerHTML=s;
    setSt(p);$('#adNote').innerHTML=noteHTML(P);
  }
  const stop=playWire(rg,$('#adPlay'),draw,22000,'Replay','adipose');
  const setSt=stepWire($('#adSteps'),AD_STEPS,rg,draw,stop);
  draw(+rg.value);

  /* ---------- white / beige / brown ---------- */
  const ks=$('#adKind'),kb=$('#adKindBtns'),kn=$('#adKindNote');let ki=0,cold=false;
  kb.innerHTML=`<span class="lbl">${AD_TXT.kind}</span>`+AD_KINDS.map((k,i)=>`<button class="btn" data-kind="${i}" aria-pressed="${i===0}">${k.n}</button>`).join('')+`<button class="btn ghost" id="adCold" aria-pressed="false">❄ ${AD_TXT.cold}</button>`;
  function heat(x,y,w,n,lvl){if(lvl<=.05)return '';let s='';for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const xx=x+w*(i+.5)/n;
      s+=`<path class="ad-heat" d="M${f1(xx)} ${f1(y)}c-6 -8 6 -14 0 -22c-6 -8 6 -14 0 -22" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--fat-hot);stroke-width:2.2;stroke-linecap:round;opacity:${f1(lvl)};animation-delay:${f1(-i*.37)}s"/>`}return s}
  function drawKind(){
    const N=vb(ks,'720 300','400 560'),K=AD_KINDS[ki],lvl={white:0,beige:cold?.85:.06,brown:cold?1:.15}[K.id];
    const L=N?{cx:104,cy:156,r:62,px:214,py:80,pw:170,ph:150,mx:24,my:250,mw:180,bx:20,by:312,bw:250,bh:46}
             :{cx:126,cy:166,r:72,px:250,py:62,pw:170,ph:176,mx:30,my:272,mw:200,bx:456,by:52,bw:180,bh:46};
    let s=`<text x="${N?16:20}" y="${N?22:24}" class="t-big">${K.n}${cold&&K.id!=='white'?' · ❄':''}</text>`;
    s+=heat(L.cx-L.r*.8,L.cy-L.r-6,L.r*1.6,4,lvl)+heat(L.px+10,L.py-4,L.pw-20,4,lvl);
    s+=adipocyte(L.cx,L.cy+8,L.r,{kind:K.id,size:.55,seed:K.id==='white'?0:5}).svg;
    s+=adiposeTissue(L.px,L.py,L.pw,L.ph,{kind:K.id,size:K.id==='white'?.55:.15,cell:K.id==='white'?30:26,vessel:1,seed:4,frame:true}).svg;
    /* UCP1 meter */
    s+=`<text x="${L.mx}" y="${L.my}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink)">${AD_TXT.ucp}</text><rect x="${L.mx}" y="${L.my+6}" width="${L.mw}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${L.mx}" y="${L.my+6}" width="${f1(Math.max(2,L.mw*lvl))}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:var(--fat-hot)"/>`;
    /* detection bars */
    s+=`<text x="${L.bx}" y="${L.by-14}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${AD_TXT.bat}</text>`;
    AD_BAT.forEach((d,i)=>{const y=L.by+i*L.bh;s+=`<text x="${L.bx}" y="${y+4}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink)">${d.n}</text><rect x="${L.bx}" y="${y+10}" width="${L.bw}" height="12" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${L.bx}" y="${y+10}" width="${f1(Math.max(2,L.bw*d.v/100))}" height="12" rx="3" style="fill:var(--brownfat)"/><text x="${f1(L.bx+L.bw+6)}" y="${y+20}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${d.v}%</text>`});
    ks.innerHTML=s;
    const nt=cold?K.cold:K.warm;kn.innerHTML=`<div class="kicker">${K.n}${cold?' · '+AD_TXT.cold:''}</div><h4>${nt.t}</h4><p>${nt.txt}</p>`;
  }
  kb.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('button');if(!b)return;
    if(b.id==='adCold'){cold=!cold;b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',cold)}else{ki=+b.dataset.kind;$$('[data-kind]',kb).forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',x===b))}
    drawKind()});
  drawKind();
  const pk=redraws.adipose;redraws.adipose=()=>{pk&&pk();drawKind();drawTurn(+$('#adTurnT').value)};

  /* ---------- turnover of 100 fat cells ---------- */
  const ts=$('#adTurn'),trg=$('#adTurnT'),tb=$('#adTurnBtns'),tn=$('#adTurnNote');let loss=false;
  const LAM=-Math.log(.9),YMAX=20,rr=rng(2024);
  /* each cell's death (and replacement) times, drawn from about 10% renewal per year */
  const CELLS=[];for(let i=0;i<100;i++){const D=[];let y=0;while(y<YMAX+2){y+=-Math.log(1-rr()*.999)/LAM;D.push(y)}CELLS.push({D,ang:rr()*360})}
  tb.innerHTML=[['stable','Weight stable'],['loss','After weight loss']].map((x,i)=>`<button class="btn" data-w="${x[0]}" aria-pressed="${i===0}">${x[1]}</button>`).join('');
  function drawTurn(y){
    const N=vb(ts,'720 300','400 560');
    const L=N?{gx:90,gy:30,pc:22,cx:200,cy:282,ax:56,ay:396,aw:310,ah:126}:{gx:30,gy:40,pc:22,cx:262,cy:80,ax:430,ay:40,aw:260,ah:190};
    const shrink=loss?.55:1;let s='',renewed=0;
    CELLS.forEach((c,i)=>{const gen=c.D.filter(d=>d<=y).length,born=gen?c.D[gen-1]:-5,next=c.D[gen];
      if(gen)renewed++;
      const grow=gen?ramp(y-born,0,1.2):1,die=ramp(next-y,0,.35),x=L.gx+(i%10)*L.pc+L.pc/2,yy=L.gy+Math.floor(i/10)*L.pc+L.pc/2;
      s+=adipocyte(x,yy,9.2*shrink,{size:lerp(.05,.6,grow),ang:c.ang,op:lerp(.25,1,die)}).svg;
      if(gen)s+=`<rect x="${f1(x-L.pc/2+1)}" y="${f1(yy-L.pc/2+1)}" width="${L.pc-2}" height="${L.pc-2}" rx="4" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:1.4"/>`});
    /* counters */
    const ca=N?'t-mid':'';
    s+=`<text x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy}" class="t-sm ${ca}" style="fill:var(--ink)">fat cells</text><text x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy+34}" class="t-big ${ca}" style="font-size:34px">100</text>`;
    s+=`<text x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy+(N?56:66)}" class="t-sm ${ca}" style="fill:var(--ink)">year ${f1(y)}</text>`;
    s+=`<text x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy+(N?74:90)}" class="t-sm ${ca}" style="fill:var(--brand);font-weight:700">${renewed} new (outlined)</text>`;
    if(!N)s+=`<text x="${L.cx}" y="${L.cy+112}" class="t-xs">${loss?'smaller cells, same number':'number holds steady'}</text>`;
    /* chart: share of original cells still present */
    const A=curveAxes(L.ax,L.ay,L.aw,L.ah,{x0:0,x1:YMAX,y0:0,y1:100,xt:[0,5,10,15,20],yt:[0,50,100],yfmt:v=>v+'%',xlabel:'years',ylabel:'original cells still present'});
    s+=A.svg;
    const M=[];for(let k=0;k<=40;k++){const yy=YMAX*k/40;M.push([yy,100*Math.pow(.9,yy)])}
    s+=plotLine(M,A.X,A.Y,{col:'var(--muted)',lw:1.6,dash:'4 4'}).svg+plotLine(M,A.X,A.Y,{col:'var(--brand)',upto:y,dot:true}).svg;
    s+=`<circle cx="${f1(A.X(y))}" cy="${f1(A.Y(100-renewed))}" r="4" style="fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.6"/>`;
    s+=kitLabel(A.X(y)+8,A.Y(100-renewed)-8,(100-renewed)+' of 100',{});
    ts.innerHTML=s;
    tn.innerHTML=`<div class="kicker">Year ${f1(y)}</div><h4>${renewed} of 100 cells are new; the total is still 100</h4><p>${y<.5?'Each year roughly one cell in ten dies and is replaced, at all adult ages and body sizes. <sup class="c" data-ref="Spalding2008" title="Source 518"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Spalding2008">518</a></sup>':'Fat cells die at about 10% a year and live about 10 years on average, so after a decade most of the original cells have been replaced. <sup class="c" data-ref="Arner2010" title="Source 24"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Arner2010">24</a></sup>'}</p>`+
      (loss?`<div class="pt"><b>In plain words</b>After weight loss the cells are smaller, but there are just as many of them: adipocyte number stayed constant even after marked weight loss. <sup class="c" data-ref="Spalding2008" title="Source 518"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Spalding2008">518</a></sup></div>`
           :`<div class="hook"><b>Exam hook</b>Adipocyte number is set in childhood and adolescence and stays constant in adults; about 10% are renewed each year. <sup class="c" data-ref="Spalding2008" title="Source 518"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Spalding2008">518</a></sup></div>`);
  }
  tb.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('[data-w]');if(!b)return;loss=b.dataset.w==='loss';$$('[data-w]',tb).forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',x===b));drawTurn(+trg.value)});
  playWire(trg,$('#adTurnPlay'),drawTurn,16000,'Replay','adipose');
  drawTurn(+trg.value);
};
/* =============== 1.6 why lost weight comes back =============== */
/* Time axis: the first 30 weeks (the competition) take the first 45% of the slider, then weeks 30 to 312 (6 years).
   Dots are the published group means of the "Biggest Loser" cohort <sup class="c" data-ref="Johannsen2012,Fothergill2016" title="Source 165,266"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Johannsen2012">165,266</a></sup>; curves between
   them are schematic. */
const AA_T30=.45,AA_END=312;
function aaWk(t){return t<=AA_T30?30*t/AA_T30:30+(AA_END-30)*(t-AA_T30)/(1-AA_T30)}
function aaTOf(w){return w<=30?w/30*AA_T30:AA_T30+(1-AA_T30)*(w-30)/(AA_END-30)}
const AA_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.2,k:'Weeks 0 to 30',t:'Weight comes off',
  txt:'Sixteen contestants in a televised weight-loss competition (baseline BMI 49.4) lost 38 ± 9% of their weight by week 30, 83% of it fat. <sup class="c" data-ref="Johannsen2012" title="Source 266"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Johannsen2012">266</a></sup> The mean loss was 58.3 kg. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup> On the see-saw, energy out outweighs energy in, so stored fat is used up.',
  pt:'For a while, the body uses more energy than it takes in, and weight falls. <sup class="c" data-ref="Johannsen2012" title="Source 266"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Johannsen2012">266</a></sup>',
  hook:'Huge losses in this small cohort: 58.3 kg on average by week 30. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup>'},
 {from:.3,at:.43,k:'Week 6 to 30',t:'Burning less than predicted',
  txt:'Resting metabolic rate fell more than the change in body size predicted: metabolic adaptation was −244 ± 231 kcal/day at week 6 and −504 ± 171 kcal/day at week 30, despite vigorous exercise. <sup class="c" data-ref="Johannsen2012" title="Source 266"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Johannsen2012">266</a></sup> In a classic study, holding weight 10% below usual lowered total energy expenditure by 6 to 8 kcal per kg fat-free mass per day. <sup class="c" data-ref="Leibel1995" title="Source 318"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Leibel1995">318</a></sup> Muscle works more efficiently, and sympathetic tone, leptin and thyroid hormones fall. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rosenbaum2005" title="Source 470"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rosenbaum2005">470</a></sup>',
  pt:'A smaller body needs less energy, but after weight loss it uses even less than its new size would predict. <sup class="c" data-ref="Johannsen2012,Leibel1995" title="Source 266,318"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Johannsen2012">266,318</a></sup>',
  hook:'Leibel 1995: TEE falls about 6 to 8 kcal/kg FFM/day below prediction at 10% lower weight. <sup class="c" data-ref="Leibel1995" title="Source 318"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Leibel1995">318</a></sup>'},
 {from:.47,at:.55,k:'After the loss',t:'Hunger turns up',
  txt:'In another study, a year after a mean 13.5 kg loss, leptin, PYY, CCK and insulin were still lower and ghrelin and hunger still higher than at the start. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup> Ghrelin over 24 hours rose 24% after a 17% diet-induced loss. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002" title="Source 104"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104</a></sup> Modelling suggests intake rises by about 100 kcal/day for every kg lost, more than three times the fall in expenditure. <sup class="c" data-ref="Polidori2016" title="Source 432"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Polidori2016">432</a></sup> The see-saw tips the other way.',
  pt:'After weight loss, the hormones that make you hungry go up and the ones that make you feel full go down. You really do feel hungrier. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>',
  hook:'Appetite push-back (~100 kcal/day per kg lost) is about three times the metabolic slowdown. <sup class="c" data-ref="Polidori2016" title="Source 432"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Polidori2016">432</a></sup>'},
 {from:.62,at:.75,k:'Years 1 to 4',t:'Weight returns',
  txt:'Rosenbaum and Leibel report a relapse rate of over 80% to pre-weight-loss body fat after otherwise successful weight loss, from coordinated metabolic, behavioural, neuroendocrine and autonomic responses. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rosenbaum2010" title="Source 472"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rosenbaum2010">472</a></sup> The Endocrine Society notes that most people who complete behavioural and dietary programmes eventually regain most of the weight lost. <sup class="c" data-ref="Schwartz2017EndoSoc" title="Source 499"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Schwartz2017EndoSoc">499</a></sup> The same happens after medicines stop: in a STEP 1 extension, 11.6 of 17.3 percentage points of loss returned within a year of stopping semaglutide. <sup class="c" data-ref="Wilding2022STEP1ext" title="Source 601"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wilding2022STEP1ext">601</a></sup>',
  pt:'Regaining weight is biology at work, not a lack of willpower. It is a main reason obesity is treated as a long-term condition. <sup class="c" data-ref="Schwartz2017EndoSoc,Wilding2022STEP1ext" title="Source 499,601"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Schwartz2017EndoSoc">499,601</a></sup>',
  hook:'Over 80% relapse to pre-loss body fat after successful weight loss. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rosenbaum2010" title="Source 472"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rosenbaum2010">472</a></sup>'},
 {from:.88,at:.99,k:'Year 6',t:'Six years on',
  txt:'Fourteen of the 16 were measured at 6 years. 41.0 ± 31.3 kg of the 58.3 kg lost had returned, yet resting metabolic rate was still 704 ± 427 kcal/day below baseline and metabolic adaptation was −499 ± 207 kcal/day. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup> Adaptation at week 30 did not predict regain (r = −0.1); those who kept off more weight showed more slowing (r = 0.59), read as a response to ongoing efforts to hold weight down. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup> A study of more modest loss measured little lasting adaptation (−54 kcal/day), so size depends on the setting. <sup class="c" data-ref="Martins2020" title="Source 356"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Martins2020">356</a></sup>',
  pt:'Even six years later, the bodies of these people were still burning less energy than expected. The body keeps defending its old weight. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup>',
  hook:'Biggest Loser at 6 years: metabolic adaptation still −499 kcal/day. <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup>'}
];
const AA_W=[[0,0],[30,-58.3],[312,-17.3]];                 /* kg; 312 wk = 58.3 lost minus 41.0 regained <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup> */
const AA_MA=[[0,0],[6,-244],[30,-504],[312,-499]];          /* kcal/day <sup class="c" data-ref="Johannsen2012,Fothergill2016" title="Source 165,266"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Johannsen2012">165,266</a></sup> */
const AA_RMR=[[30,-610],[312,-704]];                       /* kcal/day vs baseline <sup class="c" data-ref="Fothergill2016" title="Source 165"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Fothergill2016">165</a></sup> */
const AA_LBL={inn:'energy in',out:'energy out',hunger:'hunger (schematic)',w:'weight change, kg',ma:'metabolic adaptation, kcal/day',rmr:'resting rate vs baseline',
  wk:'week',yr:'year',x:'weeks 0–30, then years',lep:'leptin',ghr:'ghrelin',pyy:'PYY'};

/* Sumithran 2011: directions at 10 and 62 weeks, and P at 62 weeks <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup> */
const AA_H=[
 {n:'Leptin',kind:'leptin',d:[-1,-1],p:'P<0.001',txt:'Leptin fell with weight loss and was still lower at 62 weeks (P<0.001). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup> Restoring leptin with injections in people holding a 10% loss brought energy expenditure and thyroid hormones back to pre-loss values, so the reduced-weight state behaves like relative leptin deficiency. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rosenbaum2005" title="Source 470"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rosenbaum2005">470</a></sup>'},
 {n:'PYY',kind:'pyy',d:[-1,-1],p:'P<0.001',txt:'PYY, a fullness hormone from the gut, was lower at 10 weeks and still lower at 62 weeks (P<0.001). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>'},
 {n:'CCK',kind:'cck',d:[-1,-1],p:'P=0.04',txt:'Cholecystokinin, a fullness hormone from the upper gut, was lower at 10 weeks and still lower at 62 weeks (P=0.04). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>'},
 {n:'Insulin',kind:'insulin',d:[-1,-1],p:'P=0.01',txt:'Insulin was lower at 10 weeks and still lower at 62 weeks (P=0.01). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>'},
 {n:'Amylin',kind:null,d:[-1,0],p:'',txt:'Amylin fell at 10 weeks. It is not among the changes the abstract lists as still different at 62 weeks. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>'},
 {n:'Ghrelin',kind:'ghrelin',d:[1,1],p:'P<0.001',txt:'Ghrelin, the hunger hormone from the stomach, rose and was still higher at 62 weeks (P<0.001). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup> In another study, ghrelin over 24 hours rose 24% after a 17% diet-induced weight loss. <sup class="c" data-ref="Cummings2002" title="Source 104"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Cummings2002">104</a></sup>'},
 {n:'GIP',kind:'gip',d:[1,1],p:'P<0.001',txt:'GIP rose and was still higher at 62 weeks (P<0.001). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>'},
 {n:'Pancreatic polypeptide',kind:null,d:[1,1],p:'P=0.002',txt:'Pancreatic polypeptide rose and was still higher at 62 weeks (P=0.002). <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup>'},
 {n:'Hunger',kind:null,d:[1,1],p:'P<0.001',txt:'Subjective appetite rose and hunger was still higher at 62 weeks (P<0.001): the hormonal push toward regain had not reverted. <sup class="c" data-ref="Sumithran2011" title="Source 530"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Sumithran2011">530</a></sup> Modelling suggests appetite rises by about 100 kcal/day for each kg lost. <sup class="c" data-ref="Polidori2016" title="Source 432"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Polidori2016">432</a></sup>'}
];
const AA_HT={base:'baseline',w10:'10 weeks',w62:'62 weeks',dir:'direction only',grid:'all measures',np:'not reported as persisting'};

inits.adaptation=()=>{
  /* ---------- the main player ---------- */
  const svg=$('#aaSvg'),rg=$('#aaT');
  const MA=monoFn(AA_MA);
  const wt=w=>w<=30?-58.3*(1-Math.pow(1-w/30,1.6)):-58.3+41*(1-Math.pow(1-(w-30)/(AA_END-30),1.8));
  const TK=[{w:0,l:'0'},{w:10,l:'10'},{w:20,l:'20'},{w:30,l:'30 wk'},{w:104,l:'2 y'},{w:208,l:'4 y'},{w:312,l:'6 y'}];
  function draw(t){
    const N=vb(svg,'720 380','400 600');
    const L=N?{rx:16,ry:30,hx:16,hy:62,gx:96,hb:150,sx:300,sy:236,sw:150,ax:58,aw:322,wy:282,wh:120,my:442,mh:100,ty:560}
             :{rx:20,ry:34,hx:20,hy:76,gx:104,hb:184,sx:130,sy:350,sw:196,ax:330,aw:370,wy:38,wh:128,my:212,mh:116,ty:346};
    const w=aaWk(t),p=phaseOf(AA_STEPS,t),P=AA_STEPS[p],after=ramp(w,30,60);
    let s='';
    /* readout */
    const lab=w<=30?`${AA_LBL.wk} ${Math.round(w)}`:`${AA_LBL.yr} ${(w/52).toFixed(1)}`;
    s+=`<text x="${L.rx}" y="${L.ry}" class="t-big" style="font-size:24px">${lab}</text><text x="${L.rx}" y="${L.ry+18}" class="t-sm" style="fill:var(--ink)">${P.k} · ${f1(wt(w))} kg</text>`;
    /* hormone markers (schematic counts) */
    const lossOn=ramp(w,2,12);
    const HR=[{k:'leptin',n:AA_LBL.lep,c:Math.round(6-3*lossOn),dir:lossOn>.3?'▼':''},{k:'pyy',n:AA_LBL.pyy,c:Math.round(5-2*lossOn),dir:lossOn>.3?'▼':''},{k:'ghrelin',n:AA_LBL.ghr,c:Math.round(3+3*lossOn),dir:lossOn>.3?'▲':''}];
    HR.forEach((h,i)=>{const y=L.hy+i*26;s+=`<text x="${L.hx}" y="${y+4}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink)">${h.n} ${h.dir}</text>`;
      for(let j=0;j<h.c;j++)s+=hormoneDot(L.gx+j*15,y,h.k,{r:5});});
    const hun=lerp(.35,.85,ramp(w,4,40));
    s+=`<text x="${L.hx}" y="${L.hb}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink)">${AA_LBL.hunger}</text><rect x="${L.hx}" y="${L.hb+6}" width="${N?180:200}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:var(--panel-2)"/><rect x="${L.hx}" y="${L.hb+6}" width="${f1((N?180:200)*hun)}" height="10" rx="3" style="fill:var(--ghrelin)"/>`;
    /* see-saw: positive tilt = energy out heavier */
    const tilt=w<30?lerp(0,.75,ramp(w,0,3)):lerp(.75,-.6,ramp(w,30,50))*(1-ramp(w,120,312))+(-.18)*ramp(w,120,312);
    const lw=w<30?.4:lerp(.4,.9,after),rw=w<30?.9:lerp(.9,.55,ramp(w,30,80));
    s+=seesaw(L.sx,L.sy,L.sw,{tilt,lw,rw,left:AA_LBL.inn,right:AA_LBL.out}).svg;
    /* charts */
    const X=tt=>L.ax+L.aw*tt;
    const panel=(y,h,y0,y1,yt,ttl)=>{const Y=v=>y+h-h*(v-y0)/(y1-y0);let q=`<rect x="${L.ax}" y="${y}" width="${L.aw}" height="${h}" style="fill:var(--field)"/>`;
      TK.forEach(k=>{q+=`<line x1="${f1(X(aaTOf(k.w)))}" x2="${f1(X(aaTOf(k.w)))}" y1="${y}" y2="${y+h}" class="grid"/>`});
      yt.forEach(v=>{q+=`<line x1="${L.ax}" x2="${L.ax+L.aw}" y1="${f1(Y(v))}" y2="${f1(Y(v))}" class="grid"/><text x="${L.ax-6}" y="${f1(Y(v)+3)}" class="t-xs t-end">${v}</text>`});
      q+=`<line x1="${L.ax}" x2="${L.ax+L.aw}" y1="${f1(Y(0))}" y2="${f1(Y(0))}" class="axis"/><text x="${L.ax}" y="${y-7}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${ttl}</text>`;
      return {q,Y}};
    const curve=(f,Y,t1)=>{let d='';const n=Math.max(2,Math.round(200*t1));for(let i=0;i<=n;i++){const tt=t1*i/n;d+=(i?'L':'M')+f1(X(tt))+' '+f1(Y(f(aaWk(tt))))}return d};
    const A=panel(L.wy,L.wh,-65,5,[0,-30,-60],AA_LBL.w);s+=A.q;
    s+=`<path d="${curve(wt,A.Y,1)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--figure-line);stroke-width:1.4;stroke-dasharray:3 4;opacity:.6"/><path d="${curve(wt,A.Y,t)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:3;stroke-linejoin:round"/>`;
    AA_W.forEach(q=>{const on=w>=q[0];s+=`<circle cx="${f1(X(aaTOf(q[0])))}" cy="${f1(A.Y(q[1]))}" r="4" style="fill:${on?'var(--brand)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:1.6"/>`});
    if(w>=30)s+=kitLabel(X(aaTOf(30))+6,A.Y(-58.3)+4,'−58.3 kg',{});
    if(w>=AA_END-1)s+=kitLabel(X(1)-4,A.Y(-48),'41.0 of 58.3 kg regained',{a:'e'});
    const B=panel(L.my,L.mh,-800,50,[0,-400,-800],AA_LBL.ma);s+=B.q;
    s+=`<path d="${curve(MA,B.Y,1)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--figure-line);stroke-width:1.4;stroke-dasharray:3 4;opacity:.6"/><path d="${curve(MA,B.Y,t)}" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:3;stroke-linejoin:round"/>`;
    AA_MA.forEach(q=>{const on=w>=q[0];s+=`<circle cx="${f1(X(aaTOf(q[0])))}" cy="${f1(B.Y(q[1]))}" r="4" style="fill:${on?'var(--accent)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:1.6"/>`});
    AA_RMR.forEach(q=>{const on=w>=q[0];s+=`<rect x="${f1(X(aaTOf(q[0]))-4)}" y="${f1(B.Y(q[1])-4)}" width="8" height="8" style="fill:${on?'var(--ink)':'var(--panel)'};stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.4"/>`});
    if(w>=30)s+=kitLabel(X(aaTOf(30))+8,B.Y(-504)-6,'−504',{})+kitLabel(X(aaTOf(30))+8,B.Y(-610)+12,'−610 '+(N?'RMR':AA_LBL.rmr),{});
    if(w>=AA_END-1)s+=kitLabel(X(1)-8,B.Y(-499)-6,'−499',{a:'e'})+kitLabel(X(1)-8,B.Y(-704)+14,'−704',{a:'e'});
    /* now line and ticks */
    s+=`<line x1="${f1(X(t))}" x2="${f1(X(t))}" y1="${L.wy-2}" y2="${L.my+L.mh+2}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.2;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/>`;
    TK.forEach(k=>{if(N&&(k.w===10||k.w===20))return;const x=X(aaTOf(k.w)),last=k.w===AA_END;s+=`<text x="${f1(last?x+2:x)}" y="${L.ty}" class="t-xs ${last?'t-end':'t-mid'}">${k.l}</text>`});
    s+=`<text x="${L.ax+L.aw}" y="${L.ty+16}" class="t-xs t-end">${AA_LBL.x}</text>`;
    svg.innerHTML=s;
    setSt(p);$('#aaNote').innerHTML=noteHTML(P);
  }
  const stop=playWire(rg,$('#aaPlay'),draw,22000,'Replay','adaptation');
  const setSt=stepWire($('#aaSteps'),AA_STEPS,rg,draw,stop);
  draw(+rg.value);

  /* ---------- Sumithran comparator ---------- */
  const hs=$('#aaHSvg'),hb=$('#aaHBtns'),hn=$('#aaHNote');let hi=0,grow=1,stopH=null;
  hb.innerHTML=AA_H.map((h,i)=>`<button class="btn" data-h="${i}" aria-pressed="${i===0}">${h.n}</button>`).join('');
  function drawH(){
    const N=vb(hs,'720 300','400 580'),H=AA_H[hi];
    const L=N?{bx:40,by:56,bh:170,bw:70,gap:40,gx:16,gy:330,rh:26,c1:250,c2:330}:{bx:50,by:56,bh:180,bw:70,gap:30,gx:400,gy:44,rh:27,c1:600,c2:672};
    const base=L.by+L.bh;let s='';
    s+=`<text x="${N?16:20}" y="26" class="t-big">${H.n}</text>`;
    if(H.kind)s+=hormoneDot(N?16+H.n.length*9.5+16:20+H.n.length*9.5+16,21,H.kind,{r:6});
    s+=`<text x="${N?16:20}" y="44" class="t-xs">${AA_HT.dir}</text>`;
    s+=`<line x1="${L.bx-10}" x2="${L.bx+3*L.bw+2*L.gap+10}" y1="${base}" y2="${base}" class="axis"/>`;
    const lv=[1,1+H.d[0]*.42*grow,H.d[1]?1+H.d[1]*.32*grow:null],nm=[AA_HT.base,AA_HT.w10,AA_HT.w62],unit=L.bh/1.55;
    const ref=base-unit;
    s+=`<line x1="${L.bx-10}" x2="${L.bx+3*L.bw+2*L.gap+10}" y1="${f1(ref)}" y2="${f1(ref)}" style="stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1;stroke-dasharray:4 3;opacity:.5"/>`;
    lv.forEach((v,i)=>{const x=L.bx+i*(L.bw+L.gap);
      if(v==null){s+=`<rect x="${x}" y="${f1(ref)}" width="${L.bw}" height="${f1(unit)}" rx="4" style="fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.4;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="${x+L.bw/2}" y="${f1(ref-8)}" class="t-xs t-mid">?</text>`}
      else{const h=unit*v,col=i===0?'var(--figure)':H.d[0]>0?'var(--ghrelin)':'var(--glp1)';
        s+=`<rect x="${x}" y="${f1(base-h)}" width="${L.bw}" height="${f1(h)}" rx="4" style="fill:${col}"/>`;
        if(i>0)s+=`<text x="${x+L.bw/2}" y="${f1(base-h-8)}" class="t-lbl t-mid">${(i===1?H.d[0]:H.d[1])>0?'▲':'▼'}</text>`}
      s+=`<text x="${x+L.bw/2}" y="${base+16}" class="t-xs t-mid" style="fill:var(--ink)">${nm[i]}</text>`});
    s+=`<text x="${L.bx+2*(L.bw+L.gap)+L.bw/2}" y="${base+30}" class="t-xs t-mid" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${H.d[1]?H.p:AA_HT.np}</text>`;
    /* grid of all measures */
    s+=`<text x="${L.gx}" y="${L.gy-6}" class="t-xs" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:700">${AA_HT.grid}</text><text x="${L.c1}" y="${L.gy-6}" class="t-xs t-mid">${AA_HT.w10}</text><text x="${L.c2}" y="${L.gy-6}" class="t-xs t-mid">${AA_HT.w62}</text>`;
    AA_H.forEach((h,i)=>{const y=L.gy+i*L.rh,sel=i===hi;
      s+=`<rect x="${L.gx}" y="${y}" width="${L.c2+36-L.gx}" height="${L.rh-3}" rx="5" style="fill:${sel?'var(--brand-soft)':'var(--panel-2)'};${sel?'stroke:var(--brand);stroke-width:1.2':''}"/>`;
      s+=`<text x="${L.gx+8}" y="${y+16}" class="t-sm" style="fill:var(--ink);font-weight:${sel?700:500}">${h.n}</text>`;
      const ar=d=>d>0?'▲':d<0?'▼':'–';
      s+=`<text x="${L.c1}" y="${y+16}" class="t-sm t-mid" style="fill:var(--ink)">${ar(h.d[0])}</text><text x="${L.c2}" y="${y+16}" class="t-sm t-mid" style="fill:var(--ink)">${ar(h.d[1])}</text>`});
    hs.innerHTML=s;
    hn.innerHTML=`<div class="kicker">${H.d[0]>0?'Rose':'Fell'} with weight loss</div><h4>${H.n}: ${H.d[1]?'still '+(H.d[1]>0?'higher':'lower')+' a year later':'changed at 10 weeks'}</h4><p>${H.txt}</p>`;
  }
  hb.addEventListener('click',e=>{const b=e.target.closest('[data-h]');if(!b)return;hi=+b.dataset.h;$$('[data-h]',hb).forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',x===b));
    stopH&&stopH();stopH=animate(600,q=>{grow=ease(q);drawH()},()=>{stopH=null;grow=1;drawH()})});
  drawH();
  const pr=redraws.adaptation;redraws.adaptation=()=>{pr&&pr();drawH()};
};
/* =============== 2.1 Complications across the body =============== */
/* The body map lights one organ system per step and grows its published relative risks on a log scale beside it.
   Every number in CO_ROWS is a population statistic from the source named in the step's note; nothing here is a
   personal risk. The figure is the kit's neutral person(): no face, one colour, never a "before and after". */
const CO_STEPS=[
 {from:0,at:.1,k:'Heart & vessels',t:'Heart and blood vessels',
  txt:'In a meta-analysis of 89 prospective cohorts, obesity (BMI ≥30) compared with normal BMI went with incidence rate ratios for high blood pressure of 2.42 in women and 1.84 in men, for coronary artery disease of 3.10 and 1.72, and for congestive heart failure of about 1.8 in both. <sup class="c" data-ref="Guh2009" title="Source 203"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Guh2009">203</a></sup> In Framingham, heart-failure risk rose 5% in men and 7% in women for each 1-unit rise in BMI. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kenchaiah2002" title="Source 277"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kenchaiah2002">277</a></sup> Across 51 studies, each 5-unit BMI rise meant 29% more atrial fibrillation (OR 1.29). <sup class="c" data-ref="Wong2015AF" title="Source 607"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wong2015AF">607</a></sup> Ischaemic stroke RR was 1.64 <sup class="c" data-ref="Strazzullo2010" title="Source 526"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Strazzullo2010">526</a></sup> and venous thromboembolism OR 2.33. <sup class="c" data-ref="Ageno2008" title="Source 8"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Ageno2008">8</a></sup>',
  pt:'Extra body fat makes the heart and blood vessels work harder. In large groups, high blood pressure, heart failure and an irregular heartbeat all become more common.',
  hook:'Framingham: each 1-unit BMI rise, heart failure +5% (men) and +7% (women). <sup class="c" data-ref="Kenchaiah2002" title="Source 277"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Kenchaiah2002">277</a></sup> Obesity-linked AF ran through left atrial enlargement. <sup class="c" data-ref="Wang2004AF" title="Source 580"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wang2004AF">580</a></sup>'},
 {from:1/6,at:1/6+.1,k:'Liver & gut',t:'Liver, gallbladder and gullet',
  txt:'MASLD, the new name for NAFLD, means fat in the liver plus at least 1 of 5 cardiometabolic risk factors. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rinella2023MASLD" title="Source 463"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rinella2023MASLD">463</a></sup> A meta-analysis of 151 studies found it in 75% of people with obesity and 70% of people with overweight; among people with obesity and the disease, 21.6% had significant fibrosis. <sup class="c" data-ref="Quek2023" title="Source 451"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Quek2023">451</a></sup> Each 5 kg/m² higher BMI meant 82% higher liver mortality (HR 1.82). <sup class="c" data-ref="Whitlock2009PSC" title="Source 597"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Whitlock2009PSC">597</a></sup> Gallbladder disease RR was 2.32 in women with obesity <sup class="c" data-ref="Guh2009" title="Source 203"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Guh2009">203</a></sup>; reflux symptoms OR 1.94 above BMI 30, and oesophageal adenocarcinoma OR 2.78. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hampel2005" title="Source 215"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hampel2005">215</a></sup>',
  pt:'Fat can build up inside the liver itself. It usually causes no symptoms, so it is found with blood tests or scans, not by how someone feels.',
  hook:'MASLD = steatosis + at least 1 of 5 cardiometabolic risk factors. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rinella2023MASLD" title="Source 463"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rinella2023MASLD">463</a></sup> A "normal" ALT does not exclude it. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rinella2023AASLD" title="Source 462"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rinella2023AASLD">462</a></sup>'},
 {from:2/6,at:2/6+.1,k:'Airway & lungs',t:'Airway, sleep and breathing',
  txt:'In the Wisconsin Sleep Cohort, a 10% weight gain predicted a 32% rise in the apnoea-hypopnoea index (AHI) and about 6-fold odds of developing moderate-to-severe sleep-disordered breathing (95% CI 2.2–17.0); a 10% weight loss predicted a 26% fall in AHI. <sup class="c" data-ref="Peppard2000" title="Source 421"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Peppard2000">421</a></sup> In US adults in 2007–2010, an estimated 10% of men aged 30–49 and 17% aged 50–70 had moderate-to-severe sleep-disordered breathing. <sup class="c" data-ref="Peppard2013" title="Source 422"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Peppard2013">422</a></sup> Asthma RR was 1.78 in women and 1.43 in men with obesity; pulmonary embolism 3.51 in a single study. <sup class="c" data-ref="Guh2009" title="Source 203"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Guh2009">203</a></sup>',
  pt:'Fat around the neck and airway can narrow it in sleep. Breathing stops and starts, sleep breaks up, and daytime tiredness follows. Loud snoring is a reason to ask about a sleep test.',
  hook:'Peppard 2000: +10% weight, about 6-fold odds of moderate-to-severe sleep-disordered breathing; −10% weight, AHI −26%. <sup class="c" data-ref="Peppard2000" title="Source 421"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Peppard2000">421</a></sup>'},
 {from:3/6,at:3/6+.1,k:'Pancreas & kidneys',t:'Pancreas, diabetes and kidneys',
  txt:'Type 2 diabetes is the strongest association: IRR 12.41 in women and 6.74 in men with obesity versus normal BMI. <sup class="c" data-ref="Guh2009" title="Source 203"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Guh2009">203</a></sup> Among 51 529 US male health professionals, BMI ≥35 carried an RR of 42.1 against BMI under 23. <sup class="c" data-ref="Chan1994" title="Source 72"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Chan1994">72</a></sup> Mendelian randomisation supports a causal role (OR 1.67). <sup class="c" data-ref="Riaz2018" title="Source 459"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Riaz2018">459</a></sup> Chronic kidney disease RR was 1.83 with obesity <sup class="c" data-ref="Wang2008Kidney" title="Source 581"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Wang2008Kidney">581</a></sup>, and end-stage kidney disease rose step by step to an adjusted RR of 7.07 at BMI ≥40 in 320 252 adults. <sup class="c" data-ref="Hsu2006" title="Source 235"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Hsu2006">235</a></sup> <a href="#" data-go="diabetes">Module 2.2</a> follows the diabetes story.',
  pt:'Extra fat makes insulin work less well, so the pancreas has to strain to keep blood sugar normal. Over years the kidneys can be harmed too.',
  hook:'Guh 2009: obesity and type 2 diabetes, IRR 12.41 (women) and 6.74 (men), the strongest of the 18 comorbidities pooled. <sup class="c" data-ref="Guh2009" title="Source 203"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Guh2009">203</a></sup>'},
 {from:4/6,at:4/6+.1,k:'Joints & pelvis',t:'Joints, fertility and bladder',
  txt:'Each 5-unit BMI rise raised knee osteoarthritis risk by 35% (RR 1.35). <sup class="c" data-ref="Jiang2012" title="Source 265"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Jiang2012">265</a></sup> Each kilogram lost meant about 40.6 N less compressive force on the knee per step, roughly 4 times the weight lost. <sup class="c" data-ref="Messier2005" title="Source 365"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Messier2005">365</a></sup> Joint replacement for osteoarthritis: IRR 4.20 in men with obesity; chronic back pain 2.81. <sup class="c" data-ref="Guh2009" title="Source 203"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Guh2009">203</a></sup> Obesity was more common in women with PCOS (RR 2.77). <sup class="c" data-ref="Lim2012PCOS" title="Source 326"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Lim2012PCOS">326</a></sup> An estimated 25% of ovulatory infertility in US women may be attributable to BMI ≥25 <sup class="c" data-ref="RichEdwards2002" title="Source 460"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-RichEdwards2002">460</a></sup>, and longer time to pregnancy was linked to higher BMI in both partners. <sup class="c" data-ref="RamlauHansen2007" title="Source 454"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-RamlauHansen2007">454</a></sup> Chronic urinary incontinence is one of the Lancet Commission criteria for clinical obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Rubino2025Commission" title="Source 480"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Rubino2025Commission">480</a></sup>',
  pt:'Knees carry several times body weight with every step, so they feel extra load early. Weight can also affect periods, fertility and bladder control.',
  hook:'Messier 2005: 1 kg lost, about 4 kg less load through the knee with each step. <sup class="c" data-ref="Messier2005" title="Source 365"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Messier2005">365</a></sup>'},
 {from:5/6,at:5/6+.11,k:'Cancer & mood',t:'Thirteen cancers, and mood',
  txt:'The IARC Working Group found sufficient evidence that the absence of excess body fat lowers the risk of 13 cancers: oesophageal adenocarcinoma, gastric cardia, colon and rectum, liver, gallbladder, pancreas, postmenopausal breast, corpus uteri, ovary, kidney, meningioma, thyroid and multiple myeloma. For endometrial cancer the RR climbs from about 1.5 (overweight) to 7.1 (class 3 obesity). <sup class="c" data-ref="LaubySecretan2016" title="Source 311"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-LaubySecretan2016">311</a></sup> In the US in 2014, 40% of all cancers diagnosed were types associated with overweight and obesity. <sup class="c" data-ref="Steele2017MMWR" title="Source 522"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Steele2017MMWR">522</a></sup> Mood runs both ways: obesity raised the odds of later depression (OR 1.55), and depression the odds of later obesity (OR 1.58). <sup class="c" data-ref="Luppino2010" title="Source 346"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Luppino2010">346</a></sup>',
  pt:'Extra body fat is linked to 13 kinds of cancer. Low mood and weight can feed each other, so help for one can help with the other.',
  hook:'IARC: 13 sites, including meningioma, thyroid and multiple myeloma. <sup class="c" data-ref="LaubySecretan2016" title="Source 311"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-LaubySecretan2016">311</a></sup> Obesity and depression: OR 1.55 one way, 1.58 the other. <sup class="c" data-ref="Luppino2010" title="Source 346"><a href="/obesity/sources/#src-Luppino2010">346</a></sup>'}
];
